UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Overview</h4> <p> Develop a keen market focus, commercial awareness, and an innovative and international outlook to succeed in the food and fibre industries. </p><p>This program is designed for recent business, agricultural or rural science graduates, and for established professionals wanting to upgrade their management skills or redirect their career into agribusiness.</p><p>Select from more than 20 courses providing you with specialised knowledge of modern agribusiness practices, emerging technologies, business communication and the latest sustainability practices.</p><p>Our academics and industry experts share actionable insights on contemporary agribusiness issues such as sustainability, globalisation, food security and international trade. You''ll learn how agribusinesses from different contexts could respond to global opportunities and challenges.</p><p>You’ll explore all aspects of the supply chain to confidently work with small- and large-scale producers, processors, transporters, financial institutions, and Australian and international retailers to deliver high-quality and affordable products.</p><p>With courses in accounting, marketing, logistics and effective stakeholder engagement, you will position yourself as a future business leader.</p><p>Choose to complete a research project on a topic of your choice and increase your technical and research skills. Work alongside some of UQ''s leading academics and researchers, or in an industry setting.</p><p>Graduate with a market-oriented focus, commercial awareness, an innovative and heightened global outlook, and the required technical skills to work in the food and fibre industries in managerial, administrative or research roles.</p><p><a href="#tab1">Domestic</a><a href="#tab2">International</a></p><p><a href="#entry-requirements">See full entry requirements</a></p><p>LocationExternal, GattonDuration 1.5 Years full-time (or part-time equivalent) 2 Years full-time (or part-time equivalent) Start SemesterSemester 1 (22 Feb, 2027), Semester 2 (26 Jul, 2027)Program Code5562AQFLevel 9</p><p><a href="#fees-scholarships">Scholarships available</a></p><p><a href="#entry-requirements">See full entry requirements</a></p><p>LocationExternal, GattonFees<a href="#fees-scholarships">A$56800</a>Duration 1.5 Years full-time (only available as full-time study) 2 Years full-time (only available as full-time study) Start Semester Semester 1 (22 Feb, 2027), Semester 2 (26 Jul, 2027) Semester dates for 2028 are yet to be confirmed Program Code5562CRICOS Code079391EAQFLevel 9</p><p><a href="#fees-scholarships">Scholarships available</a></p> <p> <h5> Program highlights </h5> </p> <p> <h5> Program highlights </h5> </p> <ul><li>Access some of the best animal and agricultural facilities in the Southern Hemisphere across more than 1,000 hectares of subtropical farmland.</li><li>Benefit from regular contact with practising managers and their businesses through a hands-on approach to learning.</li><li>Gain exposure to the latest technological advancements in agriculture through practicals and industry engagement.</li><li>This program can be completed online.</li></ul> <p>1 in Australia for agriculture and forestry</p><p>QS World University Rankings 2026</p> <p>26 in the world for agriculture and forestry</p><p>QS World University Rankings 2026</p> <p> <h5> Fields of study </h5> </p> <p>Tailor your studies to suit your goals. This program offers these options:</p><ul><li><p>Rural Development</p></li></ul><p><a href="#majors">See all fields of study</a></p> <p> <h5> How you''ll learn </h5> </p> <p>Your learning experiences are designed to best suit the learning outcomes of the courses you choose.</p><ul><li>Lectures</li><li>Tutorials</li><li>Research experience</li><li>Fieldwork</li><li>Seminars</li><li>Workshops</li></ul> <p> <h5> What you''ll study </h5> </p> <p>At UQ, degrees are called ''programs'' and subjects are called ''courses''. Here''s a sample of the courses you could study in this program:</p><ul><li>Agribusiness Value Chain Management [Core course]</li><li>Agribusiness Marketing [Core course]</li><li>Agrifood Strategy &amp; Competitiveness [Core course]</li><li>Agribusiness Project Appraisal [Core course]</li><li>Global Challenges in Agriculture [Elective]</li><li>Effective Stakeholder Engagement [Elective] </li><li>Sustainable Business Practice [Elective]</li></ul><p><a href="https://programs-courses.uq.edu.au/requirements/program/5562/2027">See courses and program structure</a></p> <p> <h5> Career possibilities </h5> </p> <p>Postgraduate study can take you anywhere. Depending on which field you choose, here are some of the careers you could be on your way to:</p><ul><li>Agribusiness manager</li><li>Commodity trader</li><li>Agribusiness researcher</li><li>Export marketing officer</li><li>Biosecurity field officer</li><li>Farm management consultant</li><li>Agribusiness banker</li><li>Agribusiness analyst</li><li>Export trader</li><li>Agricultural economist</li></ul> <p>Average annual salary range</p><h5>Logistics Manager</h5>$110–$130K<p>seek.com.au</p><p>Average annual salary range</p><h5>Supply Chain Manager</h5>$130–$150K<p>seek.com.au</p> <p> <h5> Next steps after graduation </h5> </p> <p>Your scientific expertise and knowledge of agribusiness managerial principles will place you in high demand within the Australian and international agriculture sectors.</p><p>You can expect to find employment in:</p><ul><li>government departments and agencies</li><li>research institutions, including universities and CSIRO</li><li>banks, financial institutions, and investment and insurance companies</li><li>agribusinesses, such as agricultural service companies, seed companies, food producers and agricultural consultancies</li><li>biosecurity, extension and animal production enterprises</li><li>organisations involved in production, post-harvest and marketing of horticultural products</li><li>commodity trade, sales and marketing companies</li><li>export marketing and management companies</li><li>feed mills, stock equipment manufacturers, and livestock and poultry health companies within allied industries</li><li>property management companies</li><li>supply chain management organisations</li><li>tourism bodies.</li></ul><p><a href="https://career-profiles.science.uq.edu.au/">Find out more about careers that started in science</a></p> <p>The program stood out for its emphasis on global food systems, sustainability and leadership, and its strong reputation in the industry. I’ve learnt from inspiring academics and engaged with professionals who are shaping the future of agriculture, making my experience rewarding and transformative.</p><p> Douglas Walden </p><p> Current student, Master of Agribusiness </p><p>Studying Agribusiness at UQ has diversified my knowledge and equipped me with new skills and perspectives to support farmers, enhance their agricultural economic activities and drive improvements to support the growth and development of agricultural sectors in Indonesia.</p><p> Mahmud Rifai </p><p> Graduate, Master of Agribusiness </p><p>I chose to study at UQ because it is one of the world''s best universities for agricultural subjects. It offered the widest range of agribusiness courses and the opportunity to study at a rural campus with excellent facilities for agricultural studies.</p><p> Iqbal Sitompul </p><p> Master of Agribusiness </p> <p><a href="/events">See all events</a></p> <a href="/events/uq-open-day"> UQ Open Day </a><p>2 August </p><h5> UQ Open Day </h5><p>St Lucia</p> <p><a href="/stories">See all stories</a></p> <a href="/stories/agriculture-vs-agribusiness"> Agriculture vs agribusiness </a><p>Careers</p><h5> Agriculture vs agribusiness </h5><p>5-minute read</p><a href="/stories/agribusiness-career-australia"> Is an agribusiness degree worth it? </a><p>Careers</p><h5> Is an agribusiness degree worth it? </h5><p>5-minute read</p><a href="/stories/whats-it-really-study-agribusiness-and-agriculture-uq"> What''s it really like to study agribusiness and agriculture at UQ? </a><p>Uni life</p><h5> What''s it really like to study agribusiness and agriculture at UQ? </h5><p>5-minute read</p>',
