UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Overview</h4> <p> Gain the skills to tackle global environmental challenges and improve agricultural practices anywhere in the world. </p><p>As the world’s population continues to expand, demand is high for agricultural scientists.</p><p>This program is designed for recent graduates in any field, and for established professionals wanting to upgrade their skills.</p><p>Tailor your studies to suit your interests, expanding your career prospects into a wide range of government, commercial, community or research-based roles.</p><p>Our highly awarded academics will teach you the latest advances in agricultural science, including precision agriculture techniques, genetic technologies and sustainable resource management.</p><p>Access some of the best animal and agricultural facilities in the Southern Hemisphere, specialist research greenhouses, and more than 1,000 hectares of working farmland.</p><p>Graduate ready to apply leadership, research and problem-solving skills to meet the global challenges associated with feeding the world and maintaining our environment in the areas of animal welfare, biosecurity concerns, and competition for limited resources.</p><p><a href="#tab1">Domestic</a><a href="#tab2">International</a></p><p><a href="#entry-requirements">See full entry requirements</a></p><p>LocationGattonDuration Half Year (or part time equivalent)Start SemesterSemester 1 (22 Feb, 2027), Semester 2 (26 Jul, 2027)Program Code5561AQFLevel 8</p><p><a href="#fees-scholarships">Scholarships available</a></p><p><a href="#entry-requirements">See full entry requirements</a></p><p>LocationGattonFees<a href="#fees-scholarships">A$28400</a>Duration Half Year Start Semester Semester 1 (22 Feb, 2027), Semester 2 (26 Jul, 2027) Semester dates for 2028 are yet to be confirmed Program Code5561CRICOS Code079376DAQFLevel 8</p><p><a href="#fees-scholarships">Scholarships available</a></p> <p> <h5> Program highlights </h5> </p> <p> <h5> Program highlights </h5> </p> <ul><li>Access some of the best animal and agricultural facilities in the Southern Hemisphere across more than 1,000 hectares of subtropical farmland. </li><li>Learn from highly awarded academics who are world leaders in their disciplines. </li><li>Build your leadership skills with courses in rural leadership, entrepreneurship and international agricultural development. </li></ul> <p>1 in Australia for agriculture and forestry</p><p>QS World University Rankings 2026</p> <p>26 in the world for agriculture and forestry</p><p>QS World University Rankings 2026</p> <p> <h5> How you''ll learn </h5> </p> <p>Your learning experiences are designed to best suit the learning outcomes of the courses you choose.</p><ul><li>Lectures</li><li>Tutorials</li><li>Research experience</li><li>Laboratory work</li><li>Fieldwork</li></ul> <p> <h5> What you''ll study </h5> </p> <p>At UQ, degrees are called ''programs'' and subjects are called ''courses''. Here''s a sample of the courses you could study in this program:</p><ul><li>Global Challenges in Agriculture [Core course]</li><li>Leadership in Rural Industries and Communities [Core course]</li><li>Advanced Agronomy [Elective]</li><li>International Agricultural Development [Elective]</li><li>Integrated Crop Health &amp; Management [Elective]</li><li>Agricultural &amp; Resource Policy [Elective] </li></ul><p><a href="https://programs-courses.uq.edu.au/requirements/program/5561/2027">See courses and program structure</a></p> <p> <h5> Career possibilities </h5> </p> <p>Postgraduate study can take you anywhere. Here are some of the careers you could be on your way to:</p><ul><li>Agricultural scientist</li><li>Biosecurity field officer</li><li>Agricultural consultant</li><li>Extension and inspection officer</li><li>Agricultural economist</li><li>Land information systems officer</li><li>Industrial agricultural scientist</li><li>Plant protection adviser</li></ul> <p>Average annual salary range</p><h5>Protection Officer</h5>$85K–$105K<p>seek.com.au</p><p>Average annual salary range</p><h5>Agronomist</h5>$85K–$100K<p>seek.com.au</p> <p> <h5> Next steps after graduation </h5> </p> <p>As the world’s population continues to expand, demand is high for agricultural scientists.</p><p>You will find diverse career opportunities in organisations such as:</p><ul><li>local, national and international agribusiness companies such as agricultural service companies, banks, seed companies, food producers and agricultural consultancies</li><li>research institutions, including universities and CSIRO</li><li>local, state or federal government departments</li><li>biosecurity, extension and animal production enterprises</li><li>small- or large-scale organisations involved in production, post-harvest and marketing of horticultural products</li><li>feed mills, stock equipment manufacturers, and livestock and poultry health companies within allied industries.</li></ul><p>Alternatively, you can further your research ambitions and continue into the <a href="/study-options/programs/master-agricultural-science-5564?year=2027">Master of Agricultural Science</a>.</p><p><a href="https://career-profiles.science.uq.edu.au/">Find out more about careers that started in science</a></p> <p>Studying at UQ gave me vital foundational knowledge of plant science and strengthened my leadership skills.</p><p> Ruby Maunder </p><p> Graduate, Graduate Certificate in Agricultural Science </p> <p><a href="/events">See all events</a></p> <a href="/events/uq-open-day"> UQ Open Day </a><p>2 August </p><h5> UQ Open Day </h5><p>St Lucia</p> <p><a href="/stories">See all stories</a></p> <a href="/stories/career-opportunities-in-agricultural-science"> Career opportunities in agricultural science </a><p>Careers</p><h5> Career opportunities in agricultural science </h5><p>4-minute read</p><a href="/stories/agriculture-vs-agribusiness"> Agriculture vs agribusiness </a><p>Careers</p><h5> Agriculture vs agribusiness </h5><p>5-minute read</p><a href="/stories/whats-it-really-study-agribusiness-and-agriculture-uq"> What''s it really like to study agribusiness and agriculture at UQ? </a><p>Uni life</p><h5> What''s it really like to study agribusiness and agriculture at UQ? </h5><p>5-minute read</p>',
