agricultural scientist</li><li>Biosecurity field officer</li><li>Plant protection adviser</li></ul> <p>Average annual salary range</p><h5>Protection Officer</h5>$85K–$105K<p>seek.com.au</p><p>Average annual salary range</p><h5>Agronomist</h5>$85K–$100K<p>seek.com.au</p> <p> <h5> Next steps after graduation </h5> </p> <p>As the world’s population continues to expand, demand is high for agricultural scientists.</p><p>You will find diverse career opportunities in organisations such as:</p><ul><li>local, national and international agribusiness companies such as agricultural service companies, banks, seed companies, food producers and agricultural consultancies</li><li>research institutions, including universities and CSIRO</li><li>local, state or federal government departments</li><li>biosecurity, extension and animal production enterprises</li><li>small- or large-scale organisations involved in production, post-harvest and marketing of horticultural products</li><li>feed mills, stock equipment manufacturers, and livestock and poultry health companies within allied industries.</li></ul><p>Alternatively, you can further your research ambitions and continue into the <a href="/study-options/programs/master-agricultural-science-5564?year=2027">Master of Agricultural Science</a>.</p><p><a href="https://career-profiles.science.uq.edu.au/">Find out more about careers that started in science</a></p> <p><a href="/events">See all events</a></p> <a href="/events/uq-open-day"> UQ Open Day </a><p>2 August </p><h5> UQ Open Day </h5><p>St Lucia</p> <p><a href="/stories">See all stories</a></p> <a href="/stories/career-opportunities-in-agricultural-science"> Career opportunities in agricultural science </a><p>Careers</p><h5> Career opportunities in agricultural science </h5><p>4-minute read</p><a href="/stories/whats-it-really-study-agribusiness-and-agriculture-uq"> What''s it really like to study agribusiness and agriculture at UQ? </a><p>Uni life</p><h5> What''s it really like to stu