UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Overview</h4> <p> Advance your skills with leading animal science courses and develop specialisations for further study. </p><p>This program is designed for recent graduates in any field, and for established professionals wanting to upgrade their management skills or redirect their career into animal science.</p><p>Select from more than 20 courses to suit your interests in areas such as genetics, breeding, nutrition, biosecurity, agronomy, agribusiness and human-wildlife interaction, along with business electives that hone your management abilities.</p><p>Acquire the ability to apply leadership, research and problem-solving skills to meet the global challenges associated with feeding the world and maintaining the environment.</p><p>Upon graduation, you''ll have career prospects in a wide range of government, commercial, community or research-based roles tackling issues in animal welfare, biosecurity concerns and competition for limited resources.</p><p><a href="#tab1">Domestic</a><a href="#tab2">International</a></p><p><a href="#entry-requirements">See full entry requirements</a></p><p>LocationGattonDuration Half Year (or part time equivalent)Start SemesterSemester 1 (22 Feb, 2027), Semester 2 (26 Jul, 2027)Program Code5565AQFLevel 8</p><p><a href="#fees-scholarships">Scholarships available</a></p><p><a href="#entry-requirements">See full entry requirements</a></p><p>LocationGattonFees<a href="#fees-scholarships">A$28400</a>Duration Half Year Start Semester Semester 1 (22 Feb, 2027), Semester 2 (26 Jul, 2027) Semester dates for 2028 are yet to be confirmed Program Code5565CRICOS Code079377CAQFLevel 8</p><p><a href="#fees-scholarships">Scholarships available</a></p> <p> <h5> Program highlights </h5> </p> <p> <h5> Program highlights </h5> </p> <ul><li>Learn from world-class academics who are leaders in their disciplines.</li><li>Benefit from hands-on learning in extensive research and teaching facilities on Gatton campus.</li><li>Utilise production animal and wildlife facilities, a dairy, sheep and goat herds, and visit commercial enterprises.</li></ul> <p>1 in Australia for agriculture and forestry</p><p>QS World University Rankings 2026</p> <p>26 in the world for agriculture and forestry</p><p>QS World University Rankings 2026</p> <p> <h5> How you''ll learn </h5> </p> <p>Your learning experiences are designed to best suit the learning outcomes of the courses you choose.</p><ul><li>Lectures</li><li>Tutorials</li><li>Work placements</li><li>Fieldwork</li></ul> <p> <h5> What you''ll study </h5> </p> <p>At UQ, degrees are called ''programs'' and subjects are called ''courses''. Here''s a sample of the courses you could study in this program:</p><ul><li>Animal Nutrition &amp; Technology [Core course]</li><li>Leadership in Rural Industries and Communities [Core course]</li><li>Global Challenges in Agriculture [Core course]</li><li>Animal Breeding &amp; Genetics [Core course]</li><li>Effective Stakeholder Engagement [Elective]</li><li>Biosecurity Plant Pests: Invertebrates [Elective]</li><li>Agribusiness Value Chain Management [Elective]</li></ul><p><a href="https://programs-courses.uq.edu.au/requirements/program/5565/2027">See courses and program structure</a></p> <p> <h5> Career possibilities </h5> </p> <p>Postgraduate study can take you anywhere. Here are some of the careers you could be on your way to:</p><ul><li>Animal nutritionist</li><li>Wildlife scientist</li><li>Biosecurity officer</li><li>Livestock adviser or consultant</li><li>National parks and wildlife officer</li><li>Customs officer</li><li>Animal research scientist</li><li>Wildlife ecologist</li></ul> <p>Average annual salary range</p><h5>Biosecurity Officer</h5>$90K–$95K<p>seek.com.au</p><p>Average annual salary range</p><h5>Protection Officer</h5>$85K–$105K<p>seek.com.au</p> <p> <h5> Next steps after graduation </h5> </p> <p>When you graduate, you''ll be in high demand by employers for your advanced technical, communication, independent thinking and problem-solving skills.</p><p>You''ll find a diverse range of career opportunities in fields or organisations such as:</p><ul><li>ecotourism</li><li>land management</li><li>environmental management</li><li>vertebrae pest and game management</li><li>agricultural services and consultancies</li><li>animal and food production enterprises</li><li>government departments or agencies</li><li>wildlife sanctuaries and zoos.</li></ul><p>Alternatively, you can further your research ambitions and continue into the <a href="https://study.uq.edu.au/study-options/programs/master-animal-science-5571?year=2027">Master of Animal Science</a>.</p><p><a href="http://career-profiles.science.uq.edu.au/">Find out more about careers that started in science</a></p> <p>Learning from world renowned professors at UQ changed my life. I was mesmerized by their work and that inspired me to do pioneering research of my own.</p><p> Johnny Uday </p><p> Researcher and Graduate, Master of Animal Science </p><p>Studying Animal Science at UQ has helped me grow from a student into a passionate activist creating a positive change. The wildlife biology program has helped me evolve my own understanding of human-wildlife conflict as well as the world.</p><p> Azalia Rodriguez </p><p> Graduate, Master of Animal Science </p> <p><a href="/events">See all events</a></p> <a href="/events/uq-open-day"> UQ Open Day </a><p>2 August </p><h5> UQ Open Day </h5><p>St Lucia</p> <p><a href="/stories">See all stories</a></p> <a href="/stories/animal-science-careers"> Animal science careers in Australia </a><p>Careers</p><h5> Animal science careers in Australia </h5><p>4-minute read</p><a href="/stories/wildlife-science-careers"> Why study wildlife conservation? </a><p>Careers</p><h5> Why study wildlife conservation? </h5><p>4-minute read</p><a href="/stories/uq-science-scholarships"> UQ science scholarships to help fund your studies </a><p>Study tips</p><h5> UQ science scholarships to help fund your studies </h5>