UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Overview</h4> <p> Master core skills in animal science to meet the global challenges associated with feeding the world and maintaining the environment. </p><p>This program is designed for recent graduates in any field, those with a Graduate Certificate in Animal Science, and established professionals wanting to upgrade their skills or redirect their career into animal science.</p><p>Specialise in Production Animal Science or Wildlife Biology, and select from more than 30 courses to tailor your studies to suit your interests and career goals, including business electives that hone your management abilities.</p><p>Develop the leadership, research and problem-solving skills to tackle issues in animal welfare, biosecurity concerns and competition for limited resources.</p><p>Complete a significant research project, which may provide a pathway to higher degree by research programs.</p><p>Upon graduation, you''ll have career prospects in a wide range of government, commercial, community or research-based roles.</p><p><a href="#tab1">Domestic</a><a href="#tab2">International</a></p><p><a href="#entry-requirements">See full entry requirements</a></p><p>LocationGattonDuration 1.5 Years full-time (or part-time equivalent) 2 Years full-time (or part-time equivalent) Start SemesterSemester 1 (22 Feb, 2027), Semester 2 (26 Jul, 2027)Program Code5571AQFLevel 9</p><p><a href="#fees-scholarships">Scholarships available</a></p><p><a href="#entry-requirements">See full entry requirements</a></p><p>LocationGattonFees<a href="#fees-scholarships">A$56800</a>Duration 1.5 Years full-time (only available as full-time study) 2 Years full-time (only available as full-time study) Start Semester Semester 1 (22 Feb, 2027), Semester 2 (26 Jul, 2027) Semester dates for 2028 are yet to be confirmed Program Code5571CRICOS Code079383EAQFLevel 9</p><p><a href="#fees-scholarships">Scholarships available</a></p> <p> <h5> Program highlights </h5> </p> <p> <h5> Program highlights </h5> </p> <ul><li>Learn from research academics who are world leaders in their disciplines.</li><li>Benefit from hands-on learning in extensive research and teaching facilities on Gatton campus.</li><li>Utilise production animal and wildlife facilities, a dairy, sheep and goat herds, and visit commercial enterprises.</li></ul> <p>1 in Australia for agriculture and forestry</p><p>QS World University Rankings 2026</p> <p>26 in the world for agriculture and forestry</p><p>QS World University Rankings 2026</p> <p> <h5> Fields of study </h5> </p> <p>Tailor your studies to suit your goals. This program offers these options:</p><ul><li><p>Production Animal Science</p></li><li><p>Wildlife Biology</p></li></ul><p><a href="#majors">See all fields of study</a></p> <p> <h5> How you''ll learn </h5> </p> <p>Your learning experiences are designed to best suit the learning outcomes of the courses you choose.</p><ul><li>Lectures</li><li>Tutorials</li><li>Work placements</li><li>Research experience</li><li>Fieldwork</li></ul> <p> <h5> What you''ll study </h5> </p> <p>At UQ, degrees are called ''programs'' and subjects are called ''courses''. Here''s a sample of the courses you could study in this program:</p><ul><li>Global Challenges in Agriculture [Core course]</li><li>Leadership in Rural Industries &amp; Communities [Core course]</li><li>Advanced Research Methodologies [Core course]</li><li>Effective Stakeholder Engagement [Elective]</li><li>Biosecurity Plant Pests: Invertebrates [Elective]</li><li>Agribusiness Value Chain Management [Elective]</li></ul><p><a href="https://programs-courses.uq.edu.au/requirements/program/5571/2027">See courses and program structure</a></p> <p> <h5> Career possibilities </h5> </p> <p>Postgraduate study can take you anywhere. Depending on which field you choose, here are some of the careers you could be on your way to:</p><ul><li>Wildlife scientist</li><li>Animal nutritionist</li><li>Biosecurity officer</li><li>Animal research scientist</li><li>Customs officer</li><li>Livestock adviser or consultant</li><li>National parks and wildlife officer</li><li>Wildlife ecologist</li></ul> <p>Average annual salary range</p><h5>Biosecurity Officer</h5>$90K–$95K<p>seek.com.au</p><p>Average annual salary range</p><h5>Research Manager</h5>$140–$160K<p>seek.com.au</p> <p> <h5> Next steps after graduation </h5> </p> <p>When you graduate, you''ll be in high demand by employers for your advanced technical, communication, independent thinking and problem-solving skills.</p><p>You''ll find a diverse range of career opportunities in fields or organisations such as:</p><ul><li>ecotourism</li><li>land management</li><li>environmental management</li><li>research</li><li>vertebrae pest and game management</li><li>agricultural services and consultancies</li><li>animal and food production enterprises</li><li>government departments or agencies</li><li>wildlife sanctuaries and zoos.</li></ul><p><a href="http://career-profiles.science.uq.edu.au/">Find out more about careers that started in science</a></p> <p>The curriculum is precisely tailored to my requirements, with a strong emphasis on the practical, hands-on skills essential for a successful career in wildlife conservation and biology.</p><p> Mohammed Zaif Jawed Uddin </p><p> Current student, Master of Animal Science </p><p>Learning from world renowned professors at UQ changed my life. I was mesmerized by their work and that inspired me to do pioneering research of my own.</p><p> Johnny Uday </p><p> Researcher and Graduate, Master of Animal Science </p><p>Studying Animal Science at UQ has helped me grow from a student into a passionate activist creating a positive change. The wildlife biology program has helped me evolve my own understanding of human-wildlife conflict as well as the world.</p><p> Azalia Rodriguez </p><p> Graduate, Master of Animal Science </p> <p><a href="/events">See all events</a></p> <a href="/events/uq-open-day"> UQ Open Day </a><p>2 August </p><h5> UQ Open Day </h5><p>St Lucia</p> <p><a href="/stories">See all stories</a></p> <a href="/stories/animal-science-careers"> Animal science careers in Australia </a><p>Careers</p><h5> Animal science careers in Australia </h5><p>4-minute read</p><a href="/stories/wildlife-science-careers"> Why study wildlife conservation? </a><p>Careers</p><h5> Why study wildlife conservation? </h5><p>4-minute read</p><a href="/stories/10-awesome-reasons-study-gatton"> 10 awesome reasons to study at Gatton </a><p>UQ people</p><h5> 10 awesome reasons to study at Gatton </h5><p>6-minute read</p>',
