    course_description = '<h4>Overview</h4> <p> Expand your skill-set with advanced bioinformatics courses and develop specialisations for further study. </p><p>The program is designed for graduates or experienced professionals who wish to develop and effectively use best bioinformatics practice to solve scientific problems.</p><p>You''ll study foundational courses in computing, statistics and biology, through to advanced courses in your specialised area of study, to be an effective bioinformatician and data-minded scientist.</p><p><a href="#tab1">Domestic</a><a href="#tab2">International</a></p><p><a href="#entry-requirements">See full entry requirements</a></p><p>LocationSt LuciaDuration 1 Year full-time (or part-time equivalent) Start SemesterSemester 1 (22 Feb, 2027)Program Code5754AQFLevel 8</p><p><a href="#fees-scholarships">Scholarships available</a></p><p><a href="#entry-requirements">See full entry requirements</a></p><p>LocationSt LuciaFees<a href="#fees-scholarships">A$56800</a>Duration 1 Year full-time Start Semester Semester 1 (22 Feb, 2027) Semester dates for 2028 are yet to be confirmed Program Code5754CRICOS Code108890HAQFLevel 8</p><p><a href="#fees-scholarships">Scholarships available</a></p> <p> <h5> Program highlights </h5> </p> <p> <h5> Program highlights </h5> </p> <ul><li>Gain advanced knowledge in computational statistics, software engineering, data mining and genome informatics.</li><li>Learn from academics who are leading researchers in their fields.</li><li>Take advantage of links to industry, government and academic institutions in Australia and overseas.</li></ul> <p>1 in Australia for biotechnology</p><p>Global Ranking of Academic Subjects 2025</p> <p>26 in the world for biotechnology</p><p>Global Ranking of Academic Subjects 2025</p> <p> <h5> How you''ll learn </h5> </p> <p>Your learning experiences are designed to best suit the learning outcomes of the courses you choose.</p><ul><li>Lectures</li><li>Tutorials</li><li>Laboratory work</li><li>Workshops</li></ul> <p> <h5> What you''ll study </h5> </p> <p>At UQ, degrees are called ''programs'' and subjects are called ''courses''. Here''s a sample of the courses you could study in this program:</p><ul><li>Applications of Computational Statistics [Core course]</li><li>Genomics [Elective]</li><li>Statistical Analysis of Genetic Data [Elective]</li><li>Object Oriented Programming [Elective] </li><li>Data Mining [Elective]</li><li>Multivariate Data Analysis &amp; Machine Learning in Biology [Elective]</li></ul><p><a href="https://programs-courses.uq.edu.au/requirements/program/5754/2027">See courses and program structure</a></p> <p> <h5> Career possibilities </h5> </p> <p>Postgraduate study can take you anywhere. Here are some of the careers you could be on your way to:</p><ul><li>Bioinformatician</li><li>Data scientist</li><li>Data analyst</li><li>Biostatistician</li><li>Clinical data manager</li><li>Geneticist</li><li>Medical writer</li><li>Technical writer</li><li>Research scientist</li><li>Software/database programmer</li></ul> <p>Average annual salary range</p><h5>Data Scientist</h5>$115–$135K<p>seek.com.au</p><p>Average annual salary range</p><h5>Technical Writer</h5>$95K–$115K<p>seek.com.au</p> <p> <h5> Next steps after graduation </h5> </p> <p>As industries are moving more deeply into genetic technologies, the demand for bioinformaticians is expanding.</p><p>This program will prepare you for a highly rewarding career in a variety of organisations, including pharmaceutical and biotechnology companies, research organisations and government.</p><p>It also provides preparation for entry into a Higher Degree by Research program.</p><p><a href="http://career-profiles.science.uq.edu.au/">Find out more about careers that started in science</a></p> <p><a href="/events">See all events</a></p> <a href="/events/uq-open-day"> UQ Open Day </a><p>2 August </p><h5> UQ Open Day </h5><p>St Lucia</p> <p><a href="/stories">See all stories</a></p> <a href="/stories/uq-postgraduate-study-top-5-reasons"> Top 5 reasons to choose UQ for postgraduate study </a><p>Careers</p><h5> Top 5 reasons to choose UQ for postgraduate study </h5><p>3-minute read</p><a href="/stories/it-worth-doing-masters-degree"> Is it worth doing a master’s degree? </a><p>Careers</p><h5> Is it worth doing a master’s degree? </h5><p>4-minute read</p><a href="/stories/phd-story-florian-bachmann"> Florian’s PhD story: a new avenue for prostate cancer research </a><p>UQ people</p><h5> Florian’s PhD story: a new avenue for prostate cancer research </h5><p>4-minute read</p>',
