UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Overview</h4> <p> Equip yourself with advanced scientific skills and the business, legal and regulatory understanding needed to translate discoveries from the laboratory to real life. </p><p>This flexible program is designed for scientists, or industry professionals from business, finance or law with a science background, who want to learn about the latest technological developments.</p><p>You''ll integrate practical scientific training with commercialisation and innovation, giving you a dynamic mix of skills that are highly sought after across biotechnology and a broad range of industries in Australia and overseas.</p><p>Learn from entrepreneurial scientists who have successfully commercialised their discoveries in this rapidly emerging industry.</p><p>You''ll receive hands-on training applying cutting-edge techniques in state-of-the-art laboratory and research facilities similar to professional working environments.</p><p>Select from more than 30 courses, allowing you to tailor your studies to suit your interests and career goals. Specialise in one of 5 fields of biotechnology study: </p><ul><li>animal agriculture</li><li>medical</li><li>molecular imaging</li><li>plant agriculture, or </li><li>synthetic biology and industrial.</li></ul><p>Put your learning into practice through internships, placements and international study options that focus on research and development, commercialisation, marketing and the business of science.</p><p><a href="#tab1">Domestic</a><a href="#tab2">International</a></p><p><a href="#entry-requirements">See full entry requirements</a></p><p>LocationSt LuciaDuration 1 Year full-time (or part-time equivalent) 1.5 Years full-time (or part-time equivalent) 2 Years full-time (or part-time equivalent) Start SemesterSemester 1 (22 Feb, 2027), Semester 2 (26 Jul, 2027)Program Code5599AQFLevel 9</p><p><a href="#fees-scholarships">Scholarships available</a></p><p><a href="#entry-requirements">See full entry requirements</a></p><p>LocationSt LuciaFees<a href="#fees-scholarships">A$60952</a>Duration 1 Year full-time (only available as full-time study) 1.5 Years full-time (only available as full-time study) 2 Years full-time (only available as full-time study) Start Semester Semester 1 (22 Feb, 2027), Semester 2 (26 Jul, 2027) Semester dates for 2028 are yet to be confirmed Program Code5599CRICOS Code082611EAQFLevel 9</p><p><a href="#fees-scholarships">Scholarships available</a></p> <p> <h5> Program highlights </h5> </p> <p> <h5> Program highlights </h5> </p> <ul><li>Choose from a large suite of electives in science that underpin new biotechnologies.</li><li>Learn from entrepreneurial scientists who have successfully commercialised their scientific discoveries.</li><li>Take advantage of UQ’s strong links to industry, government and the research community to build your professional network, skills and experience. </li><li>This program is recognised by the US National Professional Science Master''s Association as an affiliated Professional Science Master''s program.</li></ul> <p>1 in Australia for biotechnology</p><p>Global Ranking of Academic Subjects 2025</p> <p>26 in the world for biotechnology</p><p>Global Ranking of Academic Subjects 2025</p> <p> <h5> Fields of study </h5> </p> <p>Tailor your studies to suit your goals. This program offers these options:</p><ul><li><p>Animal Agricultural Biotechnology</p></li><li><p>Medical Biotechnology</p></li><li><p>Molecular Imaging Technology</p></li><li><p>Plant Agricultural Biotechnology</p></li></ul><p><a href="#majors">See all fields of study</a></p> <p> <h5> How you''ll learn </h5> </p> <p>Your learning experiences are designed to best suit the learning outcomes of the courses you choose.</p><ul><li>Lectures</li><li>Tutorials</li><li>Work placements</li><li>Research experience</li><li>Laboratory work</li><li>Workshops</li></ul> <p> <h5> What you''ll study </h5> </p> <p>At UQ, degrees are called ''programs'' and subjects are called ''courses''. Here''s a sample of the courses you could study in this program:</p><ul><li>Commercialisation of Biotechnology Products [Core course]</li><li>Issues in Biotechnology [Core course] </li><li>Quality Management Systems in Biotechnology [Core course]</li><li>Principles of Entrepreneurship [Elective]</li><li>Creativity for Innovation and Design Thinking [Elective]</li><li>Advanced Proteins &amp; Nucleic Acids [Elective] </li><li>Biomanufacturing Technology [Elective]</li></ul><p><a href="https://programs-courses.uq.edu.au/requirements/program/5599/2027">See courses and program structure</a></p> <p> <h5> Career possibilities </h5> </p> <p>Postgraduate study can take you anywhere. Depending on which field you choose, here are some of the careers you could be on your way to:</p><ul><li>Nanotechnology and biosensor application specialist</li><li>Diagnostic test developer</li><li>Business plan analyst</li><li>Pharmaceutical producer</li><li>University researcher</li><li>Venture capital consultant</li><li>Plant breeding, engineering, cropping or horticulture specialist</li><li>Plant and animal geneticist</li><li>Biochemical engineer</li><li>Policy adviser</li></ul> <p>Average annual salary range</p><h5>Research Manager</h5>$140–$160K<p>seek.com.au</p><p>Average annual salary range</p><h5>Business Analyst</h5>$110–$130K<p>seek.com.au</p> <p> <h5> Next steps after graduation </h5> </p> <p>Graduates from this program can pursue a diverse range of scientific, technical or leadership opportunities in Australia or overseas, including in:</p><ul><li>research institutes and government</li><li>biotechnology startups or commercial companies</li><li>biopharmaceutical companies</li><li>vaccine manufacturing</li><li>diagnostics laboratories</li><li>venture capital and IP management firms</li><li>regulatory or advisory bodies</li><li>top universities worldwide.</li></ul><p><a href="http://career-profiles.science.uq.edu.au/">Find out more about careers that started in science</a></p> <p>UQ’s excellent reputation as a leader in the field of biotechnology means it is well-connected to research institutes as well as biotech industries, so you can easily choose the preferred direction for your career. </p><p> Suchita Gera </p><p> Graduate, Master of Biotechnology </p><p>The Master of Biotechnology is a blend of academic depth and industry relevance. The program strengthens technical capability through advanced coursework, but the real turning point for me was the semester-long industry placement. This experience transformed my classroom learning into tangible outcomes and showed me how biotechnology functions at industrial scale.</p><p> Shangyu Gao </p><p> Current student, Master of Biotechnology </p><p>UQ offers so many opportunities to help students gain vital hands-on experience in their prospective industry outside of the classroom. </p><p> Tiffany Shar </p><p> Graduate, Master of Biotechnology </p> <p><a href="/events">See all events</a></p> <a href="/events/uq-open-day"> UQ Open Day </a><p>2 August </p><h5> UQ Open Day </h5><p>St Lucia</p> <p><a href="/stories">See all stories</a></p> <a href="/stories/study-biotechnology-degree-uq"> Study biotechnology at UQ to cultivate a cutting-edge career </a><p>Careers</p><h5> Study biotechnology at UQ to cultivate a cutting-edge career </h5><p>5-minute read</p><a href="/stories/biotechnology-career-paths"> Lucas''s biotechnology career path </a><p>UQ people</p><h5> Lucas''s biotechnology career path </h5><p>3-minute read</p><a href="/stories/financing-postgraduate-study"> How to finance postgraduate study </a><p>Study tips</p><h5> How to finance postgraduate study </h5><p>6-minute read</p>',
    total_course_duration = '1 Year full-time (or part-time equivalent) 1.5 Years full-time (or part-time equivalent) 2 Years full-time (or part-time equivalent)',
    offshore_tuition_fee = 60952,
    onshore_tuition_fee = 9540,
    enrolment_fee = NULL,
    materials_fee = NULL,
    entry_requirements = '<h4>Entry Requirements</h4> <h5>Entry requirements</h5> <p>It''s possible to complete this degree in 2 years, 1.5 years or 1 year depending on your qualifications and experience.</p><p>You can apply for any duration as long as you meet the entry requirements. You may also be eligible to apply for <a href="/admissions/postgraduate-coursework/check-credit-eligibility">credit or exemptions</a> to shorten your degree further. You''ll graduate with the same qualification no matter how long you take to complete the degree.</p> <h5>2-year degree (32 units of study)</h5><p>To be eligible to complete the degree in 2 years full-time (only available as full-time study), you''ll need:</p><ul><li>a bachelor''s degree (or equivalent) in any discipline, or</li><li>a graduate certificate or graduate diploma (or equivalent) in biotechnology, or</li><li>to have successfully completed 3 years of study towards an approved qualification at an overseas partner institution, with a formal pathway to the Master of Biotechnology.</li></ul><p>You must have a grade point average (GPA) of 5.0 on a 7-point scale in your previous qualification.</p><h5>1.5-year degree (24 units of study)</h5><p>If you have relevant prior learning or experience, you can reduce the number of courses you need to complete and graduate in less time.</p><p>To be eligible to complete the degree in 1.5 years full-time (only available as full-time study), you''ll need:</p><ul><li>a bachelor''s degree (or equivalent) in biomedical science, biotechnology, science, bioinformatics, pharmacy or engineering, or</li><li>to have successfully completed at least 3.5 years of study towards an approved qualification at an overseas partner institution, including research requirements, with a formal pathway to the Master of Biotechnology. </li></ul><p><br/></p><p>You must have a grade point average (GPA) of 5.0 on a 7-point scale in your previous qualification.</p><h5>1-year degree (16 units of study)</h5><p>If you have relevant prior learning or experience, you can reduce the number of courses you need to complete and graduate in less time.</p><p>To be eligible to complete the degree in 1 year full-time (only available as full-time study), you''ll need:</p><ul><li>a bachelor honours degree (or equivalent) in biomedical science, biotechnology, science, bioinformatics, pharmacy or engineering, including a minimum of one semester of full-time research (or equivalent).</li></ul><p><br/></p><p>You must have a grade point average (GPA) of 5.0 on a 7-point scale in your previous qualification.</p> <p> <h5> GPA equivalent </h5> </p> <p>Select where you studied and your qualification to see the GPA equivalent you need to be considered for this program.</p><p>Use the GPA equivalent as a guide. When you apply, we’ll calculate your GPA using the UQ grading scale. Any failing grades will be included. Entry requirements are subject to change.</p> <h5>Equivalent subjects</h5> <table><thead><tr><th>Subject</th><th>Qualification equivalent</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table><p> <h5> Related programs </h5> </p> <p>Depending on your previous qualifications and current goals, you might want to consider<br/> one of these related programs:</p><ul><li><a href="/study-options/programs/master-biotechnology-research-extensive-5627">Master of Biotechnology Research Extensive</a></li><li><a href="/study-options/programs/graduate-diploma-biotechnology-5119">Graduate Diploma in Biotechnology</a></li><li><a href="/study-options/programs/graduate-certificate-biotechnology-5013">Graduate Certificate in Biotechnology</a></li></ul> <p> <h5> English language requirements </h5> </p> <p>IELTS overall 6.5; reading 6; writing 6; speaking 6; listening 6. For other English Language Proficiency Tests and Scores approved for UQ</p><p>TOEFL iBT (including Paper Edition) - Overall 87, listening 19, reading 19, writing 21 and speaking 19.</p><p>PTE Academic - Overall Score of 64 and 60 in all sub bands.</p><p>BE - A minimum overall grade of 4 plus a minimum grade of C in all macro skills.</p><p>CES - Overall 176 and 169 in all sub bands.</p><p>OET is not accepted.</p><p>There are other ways to meet the English language requirements. For some programs, additional conditions apply.</p><p><a href="/admissions/english-language-requirements">Learn how to meet the English language requirements</a></p> <p> <h5> Student visas </h5> </p> <p>International students who are accepted into full-time study in the Master of Biotechnology are eligible to apply for an Australian student visa (subclass 500).</p><p>There are a number of requirements you must satisfy before a visa is granted, including the Genuine Student (GS) requirement.</p><p><a href="/university-life/getting-prepared-to-come-to-australia/student-visas">Learn more about student visas</a></p>',
    apply_form = 'https://study.uq.edu.au/study-options/programs/master-biotechnology-5599',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '082611E';

UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Overview</h4> <p> Pioneer new frontiers in health, agriculture, science, engineering and beyond. </p><p>Deepen your understanding of the key issues within biotechnology to join a fast-evolving industry improving global health and wellbeing.</p><p>At UQ, you’ll learn from award-winning scientists who have successfully commercialised their discoveries.</p><p>They''ll guide you in your independent research project in one of the following fields of biotechnology:</p><ul><li>Agricultural</li><li>Chemical and Nano</li><li>Medical</li><li>Molecular and Microbial</li><li>Synthetic Biology and Industrial.</li></ul><p>This program will prepare you for a wide variety of employment opportunities in Australia’s thriving life sciences sector, including the biotechnology, pharmaceutical, food, medical and agricultural technology industries.</p><p>Alternatively, further your research ambitions and make significant contributions to knowledge by enrolling in a higher degree by research program.</p><p><a href="#tab1">Domestic</a><a href="#tab2">International</a></p><p><a href="#entry-requirements">See full entry requirements</a></p><p>LocationSt LuciaDuration 1 Year full-time (or part-time equivalent) Start SemesterSemester 1 (22 Feb, 2027), Semester 2 (26 Jul, 2027)Program Code2457AQFLevel 8</p><p><a href="#fees-scholarships">Scholarships available</a></p><p><a href="#entry-requirements">See full entry requirements</a></p><p>LocationSt LuciaFees<a href="#fees-scholarships">A$60952</a>Duration 1 Year full-time Start Semester Semester 1 (22 Feb, 2027), Semester 2 (26 Jul, 2027) Semester dates for 2028 are yet to be confirmed Program Code2457CRICOS Code102787MAQFLevel 8</p><p><a href="#fees-scholarships">Scholarships available</a></p> <p> <h5> Program highlights </h5> </p> <p> <h5> Program highlights </h5> </p> <ul><li>Tailor your studies to your interests and career goals with a flexible program that gives you the freedom to follow your scientific and entrepreneurial passion.</li><li>Access world-class laboratory, research and computer facilities to gain hands-on experience.</li><li>Learn from Australia''s leading educators in biotechnology and equip yourself with advanced skills.</li><li>Take advantage of UQ’s strong links to industry, government and the research community to build your professional network.</li></ul> <p>1 in Australia for biotechnology</p><p>Global Ranking of Academic Subjects 2025</p> <p>26 in the world for biotechnology</p><p>Global Ranking of Academic Subjects 2025</p> <p> <h5> Majors </h5> </p> <p>Tailor your studies to suit your goals. This program offers these options:</p><ul><li><p>Agricultural Biotechnology</p></li><li><p>Chemical and Nano Biotechnology</p></li><li><p>Medical Biotechnology</p></li><li><p>Molecular and Microbial Biotechnology</p></li></ul><p><a href="#majors">See all majors</a></p> <p> <h5> How you''ll learn </h5> </p> <p>Your learning experiences are designed to best suit the learning outcomes of the courses you choose.</p><ul><li>Work placements</li><li>Research experience</li><li>Laboratory work</li><li>Seminars</li><li>Workshops</li></ul> <p> <h5> What you''ll study </h5> </p> <p>At UQ, degrees are called ''programs'' and subjects are called ''courses''. Here''s a sample of the courses you could study in this program:</p><ul><li>Biotechnology Honours Seminar [Core course]</li><li>Research Methods [Core course]</li><li>Honours Research Project [Core course]</li></ul><p><a href="https://programs-courses.uq.edu.au/requirements/program/2457/2027">See courses and program structure</a></p> <p> <h5> Career possibilities </h5> </p> <p>Our programs prepare you for your first job and beyond. Depending on which major you choose, here are some of the careers you could be on your way to:</p><ul><li>Research officer</li><li>Bioprocess scientist</li><li>Quality control manager</li><li>Biochemist</li><li>Research scientist</li><li>Microbiologist</li><li>Cancer researcher</li><li>Trial coordinator</li><li>Lecturer</li><li>Production biotechnologist</li></ul> <p>Average annual salary range</p><h5>Microbiologist</h5>$110–$130K<p>seek.com.au</p><p>Average annual salary range</p><h5>Research Associate</h5>$10K–$120K<p>seek.com.au</p> <p> <h5> Next steps after graduation </h5> </p> <p>Your high-level knowledge and technical skills will be relevant to a range of modern biotechnologies.</p><p>Careers in biotechnology span many industrial and service sectors, including health, agriculture, diagnostics, environment, forestry, law and commerce.</p><p>You’ll be well placed for roles in:</p><ul><li>agricultural industries (in areas such as plant breeding and engineering)</li><li>chemical companies (in areas such as nanotechnology and biosensor applications, and developing drug leads)</li><li>diagnostic companies (undertaking diagnostic test design, development and production)</li><li>government agencies (as a technology analyst or commercialisation officer)</li><li>legal and consulting companies (as a business plan analyst)</li><li>pharmaceutical companies (in areas such as drug design and development or pharmaceutical production, as well as research institutes, universities or industry)</li><li>venture capital companies</li><li>startup ventures.</li></ul><p>Alternatively, you can use this qualification to further your research ambitions and make significant contributions to knowledge by enrolling in a higher degree by research program.</p><p><a href="http://career-profiles.science.uq.edu.au/">Find out more about careers that started in science</a></p> <p>I loved the visits to research centres outside UQ. I learned about research institutions and industries I could work for. I also enjoyed the enriching research culture at UQ and the opportunities to gain experience working alongside researchers and academics. </p><p> Dr Louisa Parkinson </p><p> Graduate, Bachelor of Biotechnology (Honours) </p><p>Biotechnology students have the competitive edge when it comes to making, identifying and developing scientific discoveries that truly address global problems.</p><p> Avril Robertson </p><p> Professor </p> <p><a href="/events">See all events</a></p> <a href="/events/uq-open-day"> UQ Open Day </a><p>2 August </p><h5> UQ Open Day </h5><p>St Lucia</p> <p><a href="/stories">See all stories</a></p> <a href="/stories/study-biotechnology-degree-uq"> Study biotechnology at UQ to cultivate a cutting-edge career </a><p>Careers</p><h5> Study biotechnology at UQ to cultivate a cutting-edge career </h5><p>5-minute read</p><a href="/stories/enduring-value-commerce-degree"> The enduring value of a commerce degree </a><p>Careers</p><h5> The enduring value of a commerce degree </h5><p>5-minute read</p><a href="/stories/which-advanced-business-program-right-me"> Which advanced business program is right for me? </a><p>Study tips</p><h5> Which advanced business program is right for me? </h5><p>8-minute read</p>',
    total_course_duration = '1 Year full-time (or part-time equivalent)',
    offshore_tuition_fee = 60952,
    onshore_tuition_fee = 10735,
    enrolment_fee = NULL,
    materials_fee = NULL,
    entry_requirements = '<h4>Entry Requirements</h4> <h5>Prerequisites</h5> Bachelor of Biotechnology (or equivalent), with:<ul><li>a grade point average (GPA) of 4.0 on a 7-point scale, and</li><li>a GPA of at least 4.5 for 8 units of courses at level 3 or higher relevant to the honours project, and</li><li>have secured an honours project and supervisor, and</li><li>satisfied any additional requirements set by the head of school.</li></ul> <p> <h5> Minimum entry score </h5> </p> <p>Select where you studied and your qualification to see the minimum entry score you need to be considered for this program.</p><p>Use the minimum entry score as a guide. Your score must be at least equivalent to the required Australian Year 12 ATAR score. Entry requirements are subject to change.</p> <h5>Equivalent subjects</h5> <table><thead><tr><th>Subject</th><th>Qualification equivalent</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table><p> <h5> English language requirements </h5> </p> <p>IELTS overall 6.5; reading 6; writing 6; speaking 6; listening 6. For other English Language Proficiency Tests and Scores approved for UQ</p><p>TOEFL iBT (including Paper Edition) - Overall 87, listening 19, reading 19, writing 21 and speaking 19.</p><p>PTE Academic - Overall Score of 64 and 60 in all sub bands.</p><p>BE - A minimum overall grade of 4 plus a minimum grade of C in all macro skills.</p><p>CES - Overall 176 and 169 in all sub bands.</p><p>OET is not accepted.</p><p>There are other ways to meet the English language requirements. For some programs, additional conditions apply.</p><p><a href="/admissions/english-language-requirements">Learn how to meet the English language requirements</a></p> <p> <h5> Student visas </h5> </p> <p>International students who are accepted into full-time study in the Bachelor of Biotechnology (Honours) are eligible to apply for an Australian student visa (subclass 500).</p><p>There are a number of requirements you must satisfy before a visa is granted, including the Genuine Student (GS) requirement.</p><p><a href="/university-life/getting-prepared-to-come-to-australia/student-visas">Learn more about student visas</a></p>',
    apply_form = 'https://study.uq.edu.au/study-options/programs/bachelor-biotechnology-honours-2457',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '102787M';

UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Overview</h4> <p> Equip yourself with advanced scientific skills and the business, legal and regulatory understanding needed to translate discoveries from the laboratory to real life. </p><p>This program is designed for scientists who wish to increase their technical and research skills in core areas of biotechnology, and to obtain a more extended laboratory immersion than is available in the regular <a href="https://study.uq.edu.au/study-options/programs/master-biotechnology-5599?year=2027">Master of Biotechnology</a>.</p><p>Learn from entrepreneurial scientists who have successfully commercialised their discoveries in this rapidly emerging industry. You''ll receive hands-on training applying cutting-edge techniques in state-of-the-art laboratory and research facilities similar to professional working environments.</p><p>Select from more than 30 courses, allowing you to tailor your studies to suit your interests and career goals. Specialise in one of 5 fields of biotechnology study: animal agriculture, medical, molecular imaging, plant agriculture, or synthetic biology and industrial.</p><p>Apply your expertise to a research project of your choice, working alongside leading UQ researchers or with one of UQ’s industry partners.</p><p>Put your learning into practice through internships, placements and international study options that focus on research and development, commercialisation, marketing and the business of science.</p><p>This program also provides strong preparation for entry into a PhD program.</p><p><a href="#tab1">Domestic</a><a href="#tab2">International</a></p><p><a href="#entry-requirements">See full entry requirements</a></p><p>LocationSt LuciaDuration 1.5 Years full-time (or part-time equivalent) 2 Years full-time (or part-time equivalent) Start SemesterSemester 1 (22 Feb, 2027), Semester 2 (26 Jul, 2027)Program Code5627AQFLevel 9</p><p><a href="#fees-scholarships">Scholarships available</a></p><p><a href="#entry-requirements">See full entry requirements</a></p><p>LocationSt LuciaFees<a href="#fees-scholarships">A$60952</a>Duration 1.5 Years full-time (only available as full-time study) 2 Years full-time (only available as full-time study) Start Semester Semester 1 (22 Feb, 2027), Semester 2 (26 Jul, 2027) Semester dates for 2028 are yet to be confirmed Program Code5627CRICOS Code085552JAQFLevel 9</p><p><a href="#fees-scholarships">Scholarships available</a></p> <p> <h5> Program highlights </h5> </p> <p> <h5> Program highlights </h5> </p> <ul><li>Choose from a large suite of electives in science that underpin new biotechnologies.</li><li>Take advantage of UQ’s strong links to industry, government and the research community to build your professional network, skills and experience. </li><li>Learn from entrepreneurial scientists who have successfully commercialised their scientific discoveries.</li><li>Apply your expertise to a research project of your choice, working alongside leading UQ researchers or with one of UQ’s industry partners. </li><li>This program is recognised by the US National Professional Science Master''s Association as an affiliated Professional Science Master''s program.</li></ul> <p>1 in Australia for biotechnology</p><p>Global Ranking of Academic Subjects 2025</p> <p>26 in the world for biotechnology</p><p>Global Ranking of Academic Subjects 2025</p> <p> <h5> Fields of study </h5> </p> <p>Tailor your studies to suit your goals. This program offers these options:</p><ul><li><p>Animal Agricultural Biotechnology</p></li><li><p>Medical Biotechnology</p></li><li><p>Molecular Imaging Technology</p></li><li><p>Plant Agricultural Biotechnology</p></li></ul><p><a href="#majors">See all fields of study</a></p> <p> <h5> How you''ll learn </h5> </p> <p>Your learning experiences are designed to best suit the learning outcomes of the courses you choose.</p><ul><li>Lectures</li><li>Tutorials</li><li>Work placements</li><li>Research experience</li><li>Laboratory work</li><li>Workshops</li></ul> <p> <h5> What you''ll study </h5> </p> <p>At UQ, degrees are called ''programs'' and subjects are called ''courses''. Here''s a sample of the courses you could study in this program:</p><ul><li>Quality Management Systems in Biotechnology [Core course]</li><li>Biologics [Core course]</li><li>Issues in Biotechnology [Core course]</li><li>Commercialisation of Biotechnology Products [Core course]</li><li>Biomanufacturing Technology [Elective]</li><li>Managing Innovation [Elective]</li><li>Principles of Entrepreneurship [Elective] </li></ul><p><a href="https://programs-courses.uq.edu.au/requirements/program/5627/2027">See courses and program structure</a></p> <p> <h5> Career possibilities </h5> </p> <p>Postgraduate study can take you anywhere. Depending on which field you choose, here are some of the careers you could be on your way to:</p><ul><li>Nanotechnology and biosensor application specialist</li><li>Diagnostic test producer</li><li>Business plan analyst</li><li>Pharmaceutical developer</li><li>University researcher</li><li>Venture capital consultant</li><li>Plant breeding, engineering, cropping or horticulture specialist</li><li>Plant and animal geneticist</li></ul> <p>Average annual salary range</p><h5>Research Fellow</h5>$115–$135K<p>seek.com.au</p><p>Average annual salary range</p><h5>Business Analyst</h5>$110–$130K<p>seek.com.au</p> <p> <h5> Next steps after graduation </h5> </p> <p>Graduates from this program can pursue a diverse range of scientific, technical or leadership opportunities in Australia or overseas, including in:</p><ul><li>research institutes and government</li><li>biotechnology startups or commercial companies</li><li>biopharmaceutical companies</li><li>vaccine manufacturing</li><li>diagnostics laboratories</li><li>venture capital and IP management firms</li><li>regulatory or advisory bodies</li><li>top universities worldwide.</li></ul><p><a href="http://career-profiles.science.uq.edu.au/">Find out more about careers that started in science</a></p> <p>The expertise I gained in biotechnology, bioprocess development and project management while studying at UQ has been valuable in enabling me to strengthen my impact in progressing research outcomes in my career to date.</p><p> Miguel Aguirre </p><p> Graduate, Master of Biotechnology Research Extensive </p> <p><a href="/events">See all events</a></p> <a href="/events/uq-open-day"> UQ Open Day </a><p>2 August </p><h5> UQ Open Day </h5><p>St Lucia</p> <p><a href="/stories">See all stories</a></p> <a href="/stories/study-biotechnology-degree-uq"> Study biotechnology at UQ to cultivate a cutting-edge career </a><p>Careers</p><h5> Study biotechnology at UQ to cultivate a cutting-edge career </h5><p>5-minute read</p><a href="/stories/biotechnology-career-paths"> Lucas''s biotechnology career path </a><p>UQ people</p><h5> Lucas''s biotechnology career path </h5><p>3-minute read</p><a href="/stories/financing-postgraduate-study"> How to finance postgraduate study </a><p>Study tips</p><h5> How to finance postgraduate study </h5><p>6-minute read</p>',
    total_course_duration = '1.5 Years full-time (or part-time equivalent) 2 Years full-time (or part-time equivalent)',
    offshore_tuition_fee = 91428,
    onshore_tuition_fee = 14310,
    enrolment_fee = NULL,
    materials_fee = NULL,
    entry_requirements = '<h4>Entry Requirements</h4> <h5>Entry requirements</h5> <p>It''s possible to complete this degree in 2 years or 1.5 years depending on your qualifications and experience.</p><p>You can apply for any duration as long as you meet the entry requirements. You may also be eligible to apply for <a href="/admissions/postgraduate-coursework/check-credit-eligibility">credit or exemptions</a> to shorten your degree further. You''ll graduate with the same qualification no matter how long you take to complete the degree.</p> <h5>2-year degree (32 units of study)</h5><p>To be eligible to complete the degree in 2 years full-time (only available as full-time study), you''ll need:</p><ul><li>a bachelor''s degree (or equivalent) in biotechnology, science, bioinformatics, pharmacy or engineering.</li></ul><p><br/></p><p>You must have a grade point average (GPA) of 5.0 on a 7-point scale in your previous qualification.</p><h5>1.5-year degree (24 units of study)</h5><p>If you have relevant prior learning or experience, you can reduce the number of courses you need to complete and graduate in less time.</p><p>To be eligible to complete the degree in 1.5 years full-time (only available as full-time study), you''ll need:</p><ul><li>a bachelor honours degree (or equivalent) in biotechnology, science, bioinformatics, pharmacy or engineering, including a minimum of one semester of full-time research (or equivalent).</li></ul><p><br/></p><p>You must have a grade point average (GPA) of 5.0 on a 7-point scale in your previous qualification.</p> <p> <h5> Relevant disciplines for previous qualifications </h5> </p> <p>Relevant disciplines include biotechnology, science, bioinformatics, pharmacy and engineering. </p> <p> <h5> GPA equivalent </h5> </p> <p>Select where you studied and your qualification to see the GPA equivalent you need to be considered for this program.</p><p>Use the GPA equivalent as a guide. When you apply, we’ll calculate your GPA using the UQ grading scale. Any failing grades will be included. Entry requirements are subject to change.</p> <h5>Equivalent subjects</h5> <table><thead><tr><th>Subject</th><th>Qualification equivalent</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table><p> <h5> Related programs </h5> </p> <p>Depending on your previous qualifications and current goals, you might want to consider<br/> one of these related programs:</p><ul><li><a href="/study-options/programs/master-biotechnology-5599">Master of Biotechnology</a></li><li><a href="/study-options/programs/graduate-diploma-biotechnology-5119">Graduate Diploma in Biotechnology</a></li><li><a href="/study-options/programs/graduate-certificate-biotechnology-5013">Graduate Certificate in Biotechnology</a></li></ul> <p> <h5> English language requirements </h5> </p> <p>IELTS overall 6.5; reading 6; writing 6; speaking 6; listening 6. For other English Language Proficiency Tests and Scores approved for UQ</p><p>TOEFL iBT (including Paper Edition) - Overall 87, listening 19, reading 19, writing 21 and speaking 19.</p><p>PTE Academic - Overall Score of 64 and 60 in all sub bands.</p><p>BE - A minimum overall grade of 4 plus a minimum grade of C in all macro skills.</p><p>CES - Overall 176 and 169 in all sub bands.</p><p>OET is not accepted.</p><p>There are other ways to meet the English language requirements. For some programs, additional conditions apply.</p><p><a href="/admissions/english-language-requirements">Learn how to meet the English language requirements</a></p> <p> <h5> Student visas </h5> </p> <p>International students who are accepted into full-time study in the Master of Biotechnology Research Extensive are eligible to apply for an Australian student visa (subclass 500).</p><p>There are a number of requirements you must satisfy before a visa is granted, including the Genuine Student (GS) requirement.</p><p><a href="/university-life/getting-prepared-to-come-to-australia/student-visas">Learn more about student visas</a></p>',
    apply_form = 'https://study.uq.edu.au/study-options/programs/master-biotechnology-research-extensive-5627',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '085552J';

UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Overview</h4> <p> Gain in-demand knowledge and capabilities to become a business leader, ready to succeed in any field. </p><p>This 8-unit program is ideal if you aspire to a management role and want to grow your business acumen. The knowledge you’ll gain over 6 months (or part-time equivalent) will jump-start or advance your career in your chosen business profession.</p><p>Studying at a Business School renowned for cutting-edge research and outstanding academic staff, you''ll gain the most relevant, up-to-date insights, and learn how to apply them in different business contexts.</p><p><a href="#tab1">Domestic</a><a href="#tab2">International</a></p><p><a href="#entry-requirements">See full entry requirements</a></p><p>LocationSt LuciaDuration Half Year (or part time equivalent)Start SemesterSemester 1 (22 Feb, 2027), Semester 2 (26 Jul, 2027)Program Code5248AQFLevel 8</p><p><a href="#fees-scholarships">Scholarships available</a></p><p><a href="#entry-requirements">See full entry requirements</a></p><p>LocationSt LuciaFees<a href="#fees-scholarships">A$30476</a>Duration Half Year Start Semester Semester 1 (22 Feb, 2027), Semester 2 (26 Jul, 2027) Semester dates for 2028 are yet to be confirmed Program Code5248CRICOS Code038553JAQFLevel 8</p><p><a href="#fees-scholarships">Scholarships available</a></p> <p> <h5> Program highlights </h5> </p> <p> <h5> Program highlights </h5> </p> <ul><li>Receive comprehensive training in business fundamentals, including analysis and decision-making, accounting and finance, and professional communication.</li><li>Tailor your studies with your choice of elective across advertising and marketing, HR, information systems, entrepreneurship, international business, leadership, organisational sustainability and supply chain management.</li></ul> <p>1 in Queensland for business and management studies</p><p>QS World University Rankings 2026</p> <p>#3 Best Business School in Australia</p><p>Australian Financial Review BOSS 2025</p> <p> <h5> How you''ll learn </h5> </p> <p>Your learning experiences are designed to best suit the learning outcomes of the courses you choose.</p><ul><li>Lectures</li><li>Tutorials</li><li>Work placements</li><li>Seminars</li></ul> <p> <h5> What you''ll study </h5> </p> <p>At UQ, degrees are called ''programs'' and subjects are called ''courses''. Here''s a sample of the courses you could study in this program:</p><ul><li>Business and Society</li><li>Tools and Techniques for Business Analysis</li><li>Financial Management for Decision Makers</li><li>Management Communication [Core course]</li><li>Supply Chain Management [Elective]</li><li>Sustainability: Strategy and Leadership [Elective]</li><li>Marketing [Elective]</li></ul><p><a href="https://programs-courses.uq.edu.au/requirements/program/5248/2027">See courses and program structure</a></p> <p> <h5> Career possibilities </h5> </p> <p>Postgraduate study can take you anywhere. Here are some of the careers you could be on your way to:</p><ul><li>Creative director</li><li>Digital marketing manager</li><li>Campaign manager</li><li>Media planner</li><li>Change manager</li><li>Human resource adviser</li><li>Business analyst</li><li>Purchasing officer</li><li>Startup founder</li><li>Business development manager</li></ul> <p>Average annual salary range</p><h5>Business Analyst</h5>$110–$130K<p>seek.com.au</p><p>Average annual salary range</p><h5>Brand Manager</h5>$105–$125K<p>seek.com.au</p> <p> <h5> Next steps after graduation </h5> </p> <p>Many students use this degree as a pathway to a master''s program such as the <a href="/study-options/programs/master-business-5583?year=2027">Master of Business</a>. </p> <p>My program focused on essential theoretical concepts and promoting their active application to real business case studies. This approach challenged me to think creatively and critically, analysing innovative strategies to address business challenges and provide effective recommendations.</p><p> Matilde Seidita </p><p> Graduate, Master of Business </p><p>Participating in industry networking opportunities at UQ has been incredibly beneficial for my career development. Engaging with professionals in my field has provided valuable insights into industry trends and challenges.</p><p> ChingJung Huang (Dani) </p><p> Graduate, Master of Business </p><p>Engaging with leaders from BHP, Glencore, MMG, IBM, Microsoft and other leading organisations has broadened my understanding of global leadership, digital transformation, sustainability priorities and strategic decision-making, while highlighting the critical skills needed to succeed in fast-evolving business environments.</p><p> Jose Ricardo Contreras Acevedo </p><p> Current student, Master of Business </p> <p><a href="/events">See all events</a></p> <a href="/events/uq-open-day"> UQ Open Day </a><p>2 August </p><h5> UQ Open Day </h5><p>St Lucia</p> <p><a href="/stories">See all stories</a></p> <a href="/stories/graduate-certificate-vs-graduate-diploma"> Graduate certificate vs graduate diploma </a><p>Study tips</p><h5> Graduate certificate vs graduate diploma </h5><p>5-minute read</p><a href="/stories/whats-it-like-study-master-business-uq"> Why study a Master of Business at UQ? </a><p>UQ people</p><h5> Why study a Master of Business at UQ? </h5><p>4-minute read</p><a href="/stories/microsoft-joins-uq-hack-business-student-potential"> Microsoft joins UQ to ‘hack’ business student potential </a><p>Uni life</p><h5> Microsoft joins UQ to ‘hack’ business student potential </h5><p>4-minute read</p>',
    total_course_duration = '',
    offshore_tuition_fee = 30476,
    onshore_tuition_fee = 22172,
    enrolment_fee = NULL,
    materials_fee = NULL,
    entry_requirements = '<h4>Entry Requirements</h4> <h5>Entry requirements</h5> <p>To be eligible for entry, you''ll need:</p> <ul><li>a bachelor''s degree (or equivalent) in any discipline, or</li><li>to have completed post-secondary studies, plus 5 years of full-time equivalent work experience, or</li><li>7 years of full-time equivalent work experience.</li></ul><br/>You must have a grade point average (GPA) of 4.0 on a 7-point scale in your previous qualification.<br/>Applications on the basis of post-secondary study and/or work experience will be individually assessed. <p> <h5> GPA equivalent </h5> </p> <p>Select where you studied and your qualification to see the GPA equivalent you need to be considered for this program.</p><p>Use the GPA equivalent as a guide. When you apply, we’ll calculate your GPA using the UQ grading scale. Any failing grades will be included. Entry requirements are subject to change.</p> <h5>Equivalent subjects</h5> <table><thead><tr><th>Subject</th><th>Qualification equivalent</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table><p> <h5> Related programs </h5> </p> <p>Depending on your previous qualifications and current goals, you might want to consider<br/> one of these related programs:</p><ul><li><a href="/study-options/programs/master-business-5583">Master of Business</a></li></ul> <p> <h5> English language requirements </h5> </p> <p>IELTS overall 6.5; reading 6; writing 6; speaking 6; listening 6. For other English Language Proficiency Tests and Scores approved for UQ</p><p>TOEFL iBT (including Paper Edition) - Overall 87, listening 19, reading 19, writing 21 and speaking 19.</p><p>PTE Academic - Overall Score of 64 and 60 in all sub bands.</p><p>BE - A minimum overall grade of 4 plus a minimum grade of C in all macro skills.</p><p>CES - Overall 176 and 169 in all sub bands.</p><p>OET is not accepted.</p><p>There are other ways to meet the English language requirements. For some programs, additional conditions apply.</p><p><a href="/admissions/english-language-requirements">Learn how to meet the English language requirements</a></p> <p> <h5> Student visas </h5> </p> <p>International students who are accepted into full-time study in the Graduate Certificate in Business are eligible to apply for an Australian student visa (subclass 500).</p><p>There are a number of requirements you must satisfy before a visa is granted, including the Genuine Student (GS) requirement.</p><p><a href="/university-life/getting-prepared-to-come-to-australia/student-visas">Learn more about student visas</a></p> <p> <h5> Additional application information </h5> </p> <p>The following supporting documentation is required for all applications. Please ensure that you have included ALL required documentation when you submit your application.</p><ul><li>Official transcripts of previous studies.</li><li>Evidence of work experience in the form of a CV. Please ensure that your CV includes your full work history, and outlines the major activities you undertake on a daily basis (if you are applying on the basis of work experience).</li><li>Evidence of residency status.</li></ul>',
    apply_form = 'https://study.uq.edu.au/study-options/programs/graduate-certificate-business-5248',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '038553J';

UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Overview</h4> <p> Hone your business skills and build specialist knowledge to accelerate your career in any field. </p><p>With 9 industry-relevant specialisations to choose from, this master’s program has been designed for those seeking a career transition without prior training in the available fields of study.</p><p>If you’re a current manager seeking formal qualifications, are aspiring to management roles through gaining specialist knowledge in a particular topic, or are hoping to change career direction, this program will equip you for success. The expertise you gain may also provide a pathway to a higher degree.</p><p>Study the most up-to-date and relevant theory, then apply what you''ve learned through industry projects and internships, through our well-established links with the business world. </p><p>The Business School is renowned for cutting-edge research, outstanding academic staff and close associations with leading global organisations. We’re also passionate about business that creates sustained and positive change.</p><p><a href="#tab1">Domestic</a><a href="#tab2">International</a></p><p><a href="#entry-requirements">See full entry requirements</a></p><p>LocationSt LuciaDuration 1.5 Years full-time (or part-time equivalent) 2 Years full-time (or part-time equivalent) Start SemesterSemester 1 (22 Feb, 2027), Semester 2 (26 Jul, 2027)Program Code5583AQFLevel 9</p><p><a href="#fees-scholarships">Scholarships available</a></p><p><a href="#entry-requirements">See full entry requirements</a></p><p>LocationSt LuciaFees<a href="#fees-scholarships">A$60952</a>Duration 1.5 Years full-time (only available as full-time study) 2 Years full-time (only available as full-time study) Start Semester Semester 1 (22 Feb, 2027), Semester 2 (26 Jul, 2027) Semester dates for 2028 are yet to be confirmed Program Code5583CRICOS Code082595MAQFLevel 9</p><p><a href="#fees-scholarships">Scholarships available</a></p> <p> <h5> Program highlights </h5> </p> <p> <h5> Program highlights </h5> </p> <ul><li>Gain an understanding of the global economy and business fundamentals, including professional communication analysis, strategic decision-making and financial management.</li><li>Develop specialised knowledge of essential business areas by choosing to complete at least one of 9 practical fields of study.</li><li>Complete an optional industry placement or industry consultancy project to apply your learning, gain practical experience and expand your professional network.</li><li>Prepare to hit the ground running in your new career by completing a career transition course in your final year of study.</li></ul> <p>1 in Queensland for business and management studies</p><p>QS World University Rankings 2026</p> <p>#3 Best Business School in Australia</p><p>Australian Financial Review BOSS 2025</p> <p> <h5> Fields of study </h5> </p> <p>Tailor your studies to suit your goals. This program offers these options:</p><ul><li><p>Advertising</p></li><li><p>Human Resource Management</p></li><li><p>Information Systems</p></li><li><p>Innovation and Entrepreneurship</p></li></ul><p><a href="#majors">See all fields of study</a></p> <p> <h5> How you''ll learn </h5> </p> <p>Your learning experiences are designed to best suit the learning outcomes of the courses you choose.</p><ul><li>Lectures</li><li>Tutorials</li><li>Work placements</li><li>Online study</li><li>Seminars</li><li>Workshops</li></ul> <p> <h5> Placements and work experience </h5> </p> <p> RBUS7999 is a Work Integrated Learning (WIL) course that provides you with the opportunity to apply theoretical and conceptual knowledge to the workplace via a professional placement. The course is particularly focused on enabling you to develop employability skills, gain workplace knowledge, understand the attitudes of working professionals, grow a professional network, and engage with real world business issues. </p> <p> <h5> What you''ll study </h5> </p> <p>At UQ, degrees are called ''programs'' and subjects are called ''courses''. Here''s a sample of the courses you could study in this program:</p><ul><li>Financial Management for Decision Makers</li><li>The Fundamentals of Designing and Staffing Organisations [part of Human Resource Management field of study]</li><li>Business and Society</li><li>Management Communication [Core course]</li><li>Career Transition</li><li>Digital Advertising Strategy [part of Advertising field of study]</li><li>Machine Learning for Analysis [part of Information Systems field of study]</li></ul><p><a href="https://programs-courses.uq.edu.au/requirements/program/5583/2027">See courses and program structure</a></p> <p> <h5> Career possibilities </h5> </p> <p>Postgraduate study can take you anywhere. Depending on which field you choose, here are some of the careers you could be on your way to:</p><ul><li>Human resources manager</li><li>Employee relations specialist</li><li>Sales and marketing manager</li><li>Business systems analyst</li><li>Business data analyst</li><li>Business development manager</li><li>Startup founder</li><li>Innovation manager</li><li>Change management consultant</li><li>Corporate social responsibility and sustainability consultant</li></ul> <p>Average annual salary range</p><h5>Brand Manager</h5>$105–$125K<p>seek.com.au</p><p>Average annual salary range</p><h5>Risk and Compliance Manager</h5>$130–$150K<p>seek.com.au</p> <p> <h5> Professional memberships </h5> </p> <p>When you graduate, you may be eligible for memberships with the following professional organisations. Contact the organisation to find out how to become a member.</p><ul><li>Australian Marketing Institute</li></ul> <p>My program focused on essential theoretical concepts and promoting their active application to real business case studies. This approach challenged me to think creatively and critically, analysing innovative strategies to address business challenges and provide effective recommendations.</p><p> Matilde Seidita </p><p> Graduate, Master of Business </p><p>Engaging with leaders from BHP, Glencore, MMG, IBM, Microsoft and other leading organisations has broadened my understanding of global leadership, digital transformation, sustainability priorities and strategic decision-making, while highlighting the critical skills needed to succeed in fast-evolving business environments.</p><p> Jose Ricardo Contreras Acevedo </p><p> Current student, Master of Business </p><p>Participating in industry networking opportunities at UQ has been incredibly beneficial for my career development. Engaging with professionals in my field has provided valuable insights into industry trends and challenges.</p><p> ChingJung Huang (Dani) </p><p> Graduate, Master of Business </p> <p><a href="/events">See all events</a></p> <a href="/events/uq-open-day"> UQ Open Day </a><p>2 August </p><h5> UQ Open Day </h5><p>St Lucia</p> <p><a href="/stories">See all stories</a></p> <a href="/stories/whats-it-like-study-masters-degree-business"> What’s it like to study a master’s degree in business? </a><p>Uni life</p><h5> What’s it like to study a master’s degree in business? </h5><p>6-minute read</p><a href="/stories/microsoft-joins-uq-hack-business-student-potential"> Microsoft joins UQ to ‘hack’ business student potential </a><p>Uni life</p><h5> Microsoft joins UQ to ‘hack’ business student potential </h5><p>4-minute read</p><a href="/stories/whats-it-like-study-master-business-uq"> Why study a Master of Business at UQ? </a><p>UQ people</p><h5> Why study a Master of Business at UQ? </h5><p>4-minute read</p>',
    total_course_duration = '1.5 Years full-time (or part-time equivalent) 2 Years full-time (or part-time equivalent)',
    offshore_tuition_fee = 91428,
    onshore_tuition_fee = 66516,
    enrolment_fee = NULL,
    materials_fee = NULL,
    entry_requirements = '<h4>Entry Requirements</h4> <h5>Entry requirements</h5> <p>It''s possible to complete this degree in 2 years or 1.5 years depending on your qualifications and experience.</p><p>You can apply for any duration as long as you meet the entry requirements. You may also be eligible to apply for <a href="/admissions/postgraduate-coursework/check-credit-eligibility">credit or exemptions</a> to shorten your degree further. You''ll graduate with the same qualification no matter how long you take to complete the degree.</p> <h5>2-year degree (32 units of study)</h5><p>To be eligible to complete the degree in 2 years full-time (only available as full-time study), you''ll need:</p><ul><li>a bachelor''s degree (or equivalent) in any discipline with a GPA of 4.5 on a 7-point scale, or</li><li>a Graduate Certificate in Business from UQ (or equivalent) with a GPA of 4.</li></ul><p><br/></p><h5>1.5-year degree (24 units of study)</h5><p>If you have relevant prior learning or experience, you can reduce the number of courses you need to complete and graduate in less time.</p><p>To be eligible to complete the degree in 1.5 years full-time (only available as full-time study), you''ll need:</p><ul><li>a bachelor''s degree (or equivalent) in a relevant discipline (see below).</li></ul><p><br/></p><p>You must have a grade point average (GPA) of 4.5 on a 7-point scale in your previous qualification.</p> <p> <h5> Relevant disciplines for previous qualifications </h5> </p> <p>Relevant disciplines include accounting, advertising (business degree related only), business, business administration, business information systems, commercialisation (business degree related only), economics, entrepreneurship, finance, human resources, international business, international hotel and tourism management (UQ BIHTM or BTHEM and Griffith University BITHM degrees permitted, others considered on a case by case basis), management, marketing, strategy and sustainability (business degree related only).</p> <p> <h5> GPA equivalent </h5> </p> <p>Select where you studied and your qualification to see the GPA equivalent you need to be considered for this program.</p><p>Use the GPA equivalent as a guide. When you apply, we’ll calculate your GPA using the UQ grading scale. Any failing grades will be included. Entry requirements are subject to change.</p> <h5>Equivalent subjects</h5> <table><thead><tr><th>Subject</th><th>Qualification equivalent</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table><p> <h5> Related programs </h5> </p> <p>Depending on your previous qualifications and current goals, you might want to consider<br/> one of these related programs:</p><ul><li><a href="/study-options/programs/graduate-certificate-business-5248">Graduate Certificate in Business</a></li></ul> <p> <h5> English language requirements </h5> </p> <p>IELTS overall 6.5; reading 6; writing 6; speaking 6; listening 6. For other English Language Proficiency Tests and Scores approved for UQ</p><p>TOEFL iBT (including Paper Edition) - Overall 87, listening 19, reading 19, writing 21 and speaking 19.</p><p>PTE Academic - Overall Score of 64 and 60 in all sub bands.</p><p>BE - A minimum overall grade of 4 plus a minimum grade of C in all macro skills.</p><p>CES - Overall 176 and 169 in all sub bands.</p><p>OET is not accepted.</p><p>There are other ways to meet the English language requirements. For some programs, additional conditions apply.</p><p><a href="/admissions/english-language-requirements">Learn how to meet the English language requirements</a></p> <p> <h5> Student visas </h5> </p> <p>International students who are accepted into full-time study in the Master of Business are eligible to apply for an Australian student visa (subclass 500).</p><p>There are a number of requirements you must satisfy before a visa is granted, including the Genuine Student (GS) requirement.</p><p><a href="/university-life/getting-prepared-to-come-to-australia/student-visas">Learn more about student visas</a></p> <p> <h5> Additional application information </h5> </p> <p>The following supporting documentation is required for all applications. Please ensure that you have included ALL required documentation when you submit your application:</p><ul><li>Official transcripts of previous studies.</li><li>Evidence of residency status.</li></ul>',
    apply_form = 'https://study.uq.edu.au/study-options/programs/master-business-5583',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '082595M';

UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Overview</h4> <p> Hone your business acumen, expand your knowledge and enhance your career success in any field. </p><p>During this half-year full-time (or part-time equivalent) program, you''ll learn from renowned academics connected to industry.</p><p>Designed to give you a comprehensive understanding of multiple business functions, you''ll increase your confidence to make complex decisions. You can incorporate your own workplace projects into your studies for applied learning opportunities.</p><p>Whether your goal is to accelerate your career progression, switch industries or start your own business, the opportunities for self-reflection in this engaging program will help you become a more influential leader.</p><p>As a graduate, you''ll be equipped with the capabilities to address real business challenges and drive industry change.</p><p><a href="#tab1">Domestic</a><a href="#tab2">International</a></p><p><a href="#entry-requirements">See full entry requirements</a></p><p>LocationBrisbane CityDuration Half Year (or part time equivalent)Start SemesterSemester 1 (22 Feb, 2027), Semester 2 (26 Jul, 2027)Program Code5769AQFLevel 8</p><p><a href="#fees-scholarships">Scholarships available</a></p><p><a href="#entry-requirements">See full entry requirements</a></p><p>LocationBrisbane CityFees<a href="#fees-scholarships">A$34556</a>Duration Half Year Start Semester Semester 1 (22 Feb, 2027), Semester 2 (26 Jul, 2027) Semester dates for 2028 are yet to be confirmed Program Code5769CRICOS Code020139DAQFLevel 8</p><p><a href="#fees-scholarships">Scholarships available</a></p> <p> <h5> Program highlights </h5> </p> <p> <h5> Program highlights </h5> </p> <ul><li>Create a unique study plan to suit your schedule, with full-time and part-time options, weekend and evening classes plus intensives. </li><li>Learn online or attend classes at UQ Brisbane City in the heart of the CBD. </li><li>Join an experienced cohort of industry leaders in the MBA classroom to challenge your thinking and grow your career. </li></ul> <p>1 in Queensland for business and management studies</p><p>QS World University Rankings 2026</p> <p>#3 Best Business School in Australia</p><p>Australian Financial Review BOSS 2025</p> <p> <h5> How you''ll learn </h5> </p> <p>Your learning experiences are designed to best suit the learning outcomes of the courses you choose.</p><ul><li>Lectures</li><li>Tutorials</li><li>Online study</li><li>Seminars</li></ul> <p> <h5> What you''ll study </h5> </p> <p>At UQ, degrees are called ''programs'' and subjects are called ''courses''. Here''s a sample of the courses you could study in this program:</p><ul><li>Accounting and Business Analysis [Core course]</li><li>Resonant Leadership</li><li>Leading People and Teams</li><li>Strategy: From Design to Practice</li><li>Financial Management</li><li>Impact Academy 1: Discovering New Solutions for Complex Problems [Core course]</li><li>Qualitative Business Research Methods I [Elective]</li></ul><p><a href="https://programs-courses.uq.edu.au/requirements/program/5769/2027">See courses and program structure</a></p> <p> <h5> Career possibilities </h5> </p> <p>Postgraduate study can take you anywhere. Here are some of the careers you could be on your way to:</p><ul><li>Strategy and insights consultant</li><li>Business migration adviser</li><li>Social sustainability manager</li><li>Human resources executive</li><li>Infrastructure adviser</li><li>Insolvency analyst</li></ul> <p>Average annual salary range</p><h5>Change Manager</h5>$140–$160K<p>seek.com.au</p><p>Average annual salary range</p><h5>General Manager</h5>$150–$170K<p>seek.com.au</p> <p> <h5> Next steps after graduation </h5> </p> <p>Continue your studies and move into a <a href="https://study.uq.edu.au/study-options/programs/master-business-administration-5770?year=2027">Master of Business Administration</a>.</p> <p>After not studying for 2 decades, the graduate certificate gave me time to develop good study habits as I moved into the MBA. The relationships I formed early on were invaluable and have endured since completing the program.</p><p> Peter Noyes </p><p> Graduate, Graduate Certificate in Business Administration, Master of Business Administration </p> <p><a href="/events">See all events</a></p> <a href="/events/uq-open-day"> UQ Open Day </a><p>2 August </p><h5> UQ Open Day </h5><p>St Lucia</p> <p><a href="/stories">See all stories</a></p> <a href="/stories/mba-pathways-without-degree"> MBA pathways: how to get into an MBA without a degree </a><p>Study tips</p><h5> MBA pathways: how to get into an MBA without a degree </h5><p>4-minute read</p><a href="/stories/uq-postgraduate-study-top-5-reasons"> Top 5 reasons to choose UQ for postgraduate study </a><p>Careers</p><h5> Top 5 reasons to choose UQ for postgraduate study </h5><p>3-minute read</p><a href="/stories/graduate-certificate-worth-it"> Is a graduate certificate worth it? </a><p>Careers</p><h5> Is a graduate certificate worth it? </h5><p>5-minute read</p>',
    total_course_duration = '',
    offshore_tuition_fee = 34556,
    onshore_tuition_fee = 32112,
    enrolment_fee = NULL,
    materials_fee = NULL,
    entry_requirements = '<h4>Entry Requirements</h4> <h5>Entry requirements</h5> <p>To be eligible for entry, you''ll need:</p> <ul><li>a bachelor''s degree (or equivalent) in any discipline, plus 4 years full-time equivalent work experience (see below), including 2 years in a dedicated supervisory/management role, or</li><li>7 years full-time equivalent work experience, including 3 years in a dedicated supervisory/management role.</li></ul><br/>You must have a grade point average (GPA) of 4.0 on a 7-point scale in your previous qualification.<br/><br/>Applications on the basis of work experience will be individually assessed.<br/><br/>International applicants must have completed the <a href="https://www.mba.com/">Graduate Management Admissions Test (GMAT)</a> with a minimum score of 550. <p> <h5> Relevant work experience </h5> </p> <p>Relevant work experience for applicants with a bachelor’s degree (or equivalent) should typically be post-graduation. </p> <p> <h5> GPA equivalent </h5> </p> <p>Select where you studied and your qualification to see the GPA equivalent you need to be considered for this program.</p><p>Use the GPA equivalent as a guide. When you apply, we’ll calculate your GPA using the UQ grading scale. Any failing grades will be included. Entry requirements are subject to change.</p> <h5>Equivalent subjects</h5> <table><thead><tr><th>Subject</th><th>Qualification equivalent</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table><p> <h5> Related programs </h5> </p> <p>Depending on your previous qualifications and current goals, you might want to consider<br/> one of these related programs:</p><ul><li><a href="/study-options/programs/master-business-administration-5770">Master of Business Administration</a></li></ul> <p> <h5> English language requirements </h5> </p> <p>IELTS overall 6.5; reading 6; writing 6; speaking 6; listening 6. For other English Language Proficiency Tests and Scores approved for UQ</p><p>TOEFL iBT (including Paper Edition) - Overall 87, listening 19, reading 19, writing 21 and speaking 19.</p><p>PTE Academic - Overall Score of 64 and 60 in all sub bands.</p><p>BE - A minimum overall grade of 4 plus a minimum grade of C in all macro skills.</p><p>CES - Overall 176 and 169 in all sub bands.</p><p>OET is not accepted.</p><p>There are other ways to meet the English language requirements. For some programs, additional conditions apply.</p><p><a href="/admissions/english-language-requirements">Learn how to meet the English language requirements</a></p> <p> <h5> Student visas </h5> </p> <p>International students who are accepted into full-time study in the Graduate Certificate in Business Administration are eligible to apply for an Australian student visa (subclass 500).</p><p>There are a number of requirements you must satisfy before a visa is granted, including the Genuine Student (GS) requirement.</p><p><a href="/university-life/getting-prepared-to-come-to-australia/student-visas">Learn more about student visas</a></p> <p> <h5> Additional application information </h5> </p> <p>You will need to provide the following supporting documentation when you submit your application:</p><ul><li>Official transcripts of previous studies.</li><li>Your CV, with your full work history, including details of management experience (of people and projects). Ensure your CV includes start and finish dates and outlines the major activities you undertake daily.</li><li>Two written references that are work-related, dated, signed and preferably on company letterhead. Your referees need to confirm they key duties of your work. They also need to verify your management experience. This might include managing a team of people, managing client accounts, the managerial components of any major projects you have been directly responsible for, or financial delegations you are directly responsible for.</li><li>Evidence of residency status.</li></ul><p>Permanent residents should refer to UQ''s <a href="https://study.uq.edu.au/admissions/english-language-requirements">English language requirements.</a></p><p>Permanent residents many need to sit a <a href="https://www.mba.com/">GMAT test.</a></p><p><a href="https://study.uq.edu.au/stories/how-prepare-your-uq-mba-application-insider-tips-and-common-questions">Read more about how to prepare your application.</a></p>',
    apply_form = 'https://study.uq.edu.au/study-options/programs/graduate-certificate-business-administration-5769',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '020139D';

UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Overview</h4> <p> With a reputation for excellence, our Master of Business Administration (MBA) will give you the leadership agility to navigate an ever-changing business landscape and drive outcomes in your industry. </p><p>Great leadership requires more than ambition. It''s your curiosity, passion and relentless drive that will ignite disruptive thinking and create change.</p><p>Challenge your thinking by learning from MBA teachers who are renowned academics at the forefront of research. Our connection to industry keeps the learning fresh and relevant, supporting you in addressing real business challenges. Designed to give you a comprehensive understanding of multiple business functions, you''ll increase your confidence to make complex business decisions. You''ll learn with an experienced cohort who will enrich your studies and connect you with ongoing career opportunities.</p><p>Design your own customised program to gain maximum value. Align your learning experience with your interests and career goals, pursue a research project or even explore topics outside the MBA.</p><p>You can incorporate your own workplace projects into your studies for applied learning opportunities, work with industry clients on solutions to real challenges, or explore your entrepreneurial projects.</p><p>Achieve your career goals with ongoing personalised support from a team of experts, industry mentoring, exclusive career events and 1-1 career consultations.</p><p>Whether you want to accelerate your career, switch industries, pursue a research career, get board-ready or start your own business, this transformational program will help you reach your potential.</p><p><a href="#tab1">Domestic</a><a href="#tab2">International</a></p><p><a href="#entry-requirements">See full entry requirements</a></p><p>LocationBrisbane CityDuration 1.5 Years (or part time equivalent)Start SemesterSemester 1 (22 Feb, 2027), Semester 2 (26 Jul, 2027), Summer Semester (29 Nov, 2027)Program Code5770AQFLevel 9</p><p><a href="#fees-scholarships">Scholarships available</a></p><p><a href="#entry-requirements">See full entry requirements</a></p><p>LocationBrisbane CityFees<a href="#fees-scholarships">A$69112</a>Duration 1.5 Years Start Semester Semester 1 (22 Feb, 2027), Semester 2 (26 Jul, 2027) Semester dates for 2028 are yet to be confirmed Program Code5770CRICOS Code116551EAQFLevel 9</p><p><a href="#fees-scholarships">Scholarships available</a></p> <p> <h5> Program highlights </h5> </p> <p> <h5> Program highlights </h5> </p> <ul><li>Create a unique study plan to suit your schedule, with full-time and part-time options, weekend and PM classes plus intensives.</li><li>Learn online, or attend classes at UQ Brisbane City in the heart of the CBD. </li><li>Gain international experience and expand your global network with optional short-term exchanges to partner institutions like Harvard Business School.</li></ul> <p>#4 MBA in Australia</p><p>QS Global MBA Ranking 2026</p> <p>16 in the world for business administration</p><p>Global Ranking of Academic Subjects 2025</p> <p> <h5> How you''ll learn </h5> </p> <p>Your learning experiences are designed to best suit the learning outcomes of the courses you choose.</p><ul><li>Lectures</li><li>Work placements</li><li>Online study</li><li>Overseas study</li><li>Seminars</li><li>Workshops</li></ul> <p> <h5> What you''ll study </h5> </p> <p>At UQ, degrees are called ''programs'' and subjects are called ''courses''. Here''s a sample of the courses you could study in this program:</p><ul><li>Accounting and Business Analysis [Core course]</li><li>Financial Management [Core course]</li><li>Leading People and Teams [Core course]</li><li>Strategic Human Resources Management [Elective]</li><li>Operations Delivery and Transformation [Elective]</li><li>Innovation Leadership [Elective]</li><li>Impact Academy 1: Discovering New Solutions for Complex Problems [Core course]</li></ul><p><a href="https://programs-courses.uq.edu.au/requirements/program/5770/2027">See courses and program structure</a></p> <p> <h5> Career possibilities </h5> </p> <p>Postgraduate study can take you anywhere. Here are some of the careers you could be on your way to:</p><ul><li>Chief executive officer</li><li>Director of operations</li><li>Chief financial officer</li><li>Marketing director</li><li>National sales manager</li><li>Chief operations officer (COO)</li><li>Strategy and innovation manager</li><li>Program director</li><li>Chief marketing officer</li><li>Chief human resources officer</li></ul> <p>Average annual salary range</p><h5>Chief Executive Officer (CEO)</h5>$220–240K<p>seek.com.au</p><p>Average annual salary range</p><h5>Chief Operating Officer (COO)</h5>$190–$210K<p>seek.com.au</p> <p> <h5> Next steps after graduation </h5> </p> <p>After you graduate, you can continue to access one-on-one career advice at any stage in your career. You’ll also be invited to regular networking and professional development events with your peers. </p> <p>The network is one of the most powerful outcomes of the MBA. I’m now connected to a broad network of alumni from all kinds of industries and backgrounds. I regularly tap into this community for strategic input, specialised advice and collaborative projects.</p><p> Helen Barker </p><p> Graduate, Master of Business Administration </p><p>I saw the UQ MBA as an investment in my future, my future earnings, my future career, my potential. After successfully getting a new general manager role, which increased my salary, I found my MBA paid for itself.</p><p> Ashton Tuckerman </p><p> Graduate, Master of Business Administration </p><p>Studying on top of parenting and FIFO work was never going to be easy. The only way to balance these competing priorities is to pick a degree with the flexibility you need. That’s why I chose the UQ MBA.</p><p> Ben Goldsworthy </p><p> Current student, Master of Business Administration </p> <p><a href="/events">See all events</a></p> <a href="/events/uq-open-day"> UQ Open Day </a><p>2 August </p><h5> UQ Open Day </h5><p>St Lucia</p> <p><a href="/stories">See all stories</a></p> <a href="/stories/is-mba-worth-it"> Is an MBA worth it? </a><p>Careers</p><h5> Is an MBA worth it? </h5><p>9-minute read</p><a href="/stories/flexible-mba"> Flexible MBA: how to tailor your study to your schedule and goals </a><p>Uni life</p><h5> Flexible MBA: how to tailor your study to your schedule and goals </h5><p>8-minute read</p><a href="/stories/how-customise-uq-mba-suit-your-goals"> How to customise the UQ MBA to suit your goals </a><p>Study tips</p><h5> How to customise the UQ MBA to suit your goals </h5><p>4-minute read</p>',
    total_course_duration = '1.5 Years (or part time equivalent)',
    offshore_tuition_fee = 103668,
    onshore_tuition_fee = 96336,
    enrolment_fee = NULL,
    materials_fee = NULL,
    entry_requirements = '<h4>Entry Requirements</h4> <h5>Entry requirements</h5> <p>To be eligible for entry, you''ll need:</p> <ul><li>a bachelor''s degree (or equivalent) in any discipline with a GPA of 4.5 on a 7-point scale, plus 4 years full-time equivalent, relevant work experience (see below), or</li><li>the Graduate Certificate in Business Administration from UQ with a GPA of 4.</li></ul><br/>International applicants must have completed the <a href="http://www.mba.com/global">Graduate Management Admissions Test (GMAT)</a> with a minimum score of 550. <p> <h5> Relevant work experience </h5> </p> <p>Relevant work experience should typically be post-graduation, and include 2 years in a dedicated supervisory/management role (of people or projects).</p> <p> <h5> GPA equivalent </h5> </p> <p>Select where you studied and your qualification to see the GPA equivalent you need to be considered for this program.</p><p>Use the GPA equivalent as a guide. When you apply, we’ll calculate your GPA using the UQ grading scale. Any failing grades will be included. Entry requirements are subject to change.</p> <h5>Equivalent subjects</h5> <table><thead><tr><th>Subject</th><th>Qualification equivalent</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table><p> <h5> Related programs </h5> </p> <p>Depending on your previous qualifications and current goals, you might want to consider<br/> one of these related programs:</p><ul><li><a href="/study-options/programs/graduate-certificate-business-administration-5769">Graduate Certificate in Business Administration</a></li></ul> <p> <h5> English language requirements </h5> </p> <p>IELTS overall 6.5; reading 6; writing 6; speaking 6; listening 6. For other English Language Proficiency Tests and Scores approved for UQ</p><p>TOEFL iBT (including Paper Edition) - Overall 87, listening 19, reading 19, writing 21 and speaking 19.</p><p>PTE Academic - Overall Score of 64 and 60 in all sub bands.</p><p>BE - A minimum overall grade of 4 plus a minimum grade of C in all macro skills.</p><p>CES - Overall 176 and 169 in all sub bands.</p><p>OET is not accepted.</p><p>There are other ways to meet the English language requirements. For some programs, additional conditions apply.</p><p><a href="/admissions/english-language-requirements">Learn how to meet the English language requirements</a></p> <p> <h5> Student visas </h5> </p> <p>International students who are accepted into full-time study in the Master of Business Administration are eligible to apply for an Australian student visa (subclass 500).</p><p>There are a number of requirements you must satisfy before a visa is granted, including the Genuine Student (GS) requirement.</p><p><a href="/university-life/getting-prepared-to-come-to-australia/student-visas">Learn more about student visas</a></p> <p> <h5> Additional application information </h5> </p> <p>You will need to provide the following supporting documentation when you submit your application:</p><ul><li>Official transcripts of previous studies.</li><li>Your CV, with your full work history, including details of management experience (of people and projects). Ensure your CV includes start and finish dates and outlines the major activities you undertake daily.</li><li>Two written references that are work-related, dated, signed and preferably on company letterhead. Your referees need to confirm they key duties of your work. They also need to verify your management experience. This might include managing a team of people, managing client accounts, the managerial components of any major projects you have been directly responsible for, or financial delegations you are directly responsible for.</li><li>Evidence of residency status.</li></ul><p>Permanent residents should refer to UQ''s <a href="https://study.uq.edu.au/admissions/english-language-requirements">English language requirements.</a></p><p>Permanent residents many need to sit a <a href="https://www.mba.com/">GMAT test.</a></p><p><a href="https://study.uq.edu.au/stories/how-prepare-your-uq-mba-application-insider-tips-and-common-questions">Read more about how to prepare your application.</a></p>',
    apply_form = 'https://study.uq.edu.au/study-options/programs/master-business-administration-5770',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '116551E';

