UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Overview</h4> <p> Be prepared for a future in business and gain specialist capabilities in problem identification, critical thinking and designing for purpose. </p><p>This versatile dual program will equip you with the expertise and creativity to respond to the complex needs of a thriving professional environment.</p><p>The Bachelor of Business Management / Bachelor of Design dual program will teach you to challenge conventional thinking and bring a different mindset to business and societal problems.</p><p>The Bachelor of Business Management is designed to equip you with the skills you’ll need for a future in business. You’ll study topics including entrepreneurship, human resources, marketing, management and business technologies.</p><p>Complement your business knowledge with specialist capabilities in problem identification, critical thinking, and designing for purpose through the Bachelor of Design.</p><p>During practical studio-based projects, you’ll work in teams to collaborate, challenge assumptions, prototype innovative and sustainable solutions, and systematically solve problems in creative and novel ways.</p><p>Graduate from this versatile dual program with a range of skills and expertise that will help you succeed in almost any industry.</p><p><a href="#tab1">Domestic</a><a href="#tab2">International</a></p><p><a href="#entry-requirements">See full entry requirements</a></p>LocationSt LuciaDuration 4 Years (or part time equivalent)Start SemesterSemester 1 (22 Feb, 2027), Semester 2 (26 Jul, 2027)QTAC Code<p>709511</p>Program Code2554AQFLevel 7<p><a href="#how-to-apply">Admission schemes available</a></p><p><a href="#fees-scholarships">Scholarships available</a></p><p><a href="#entry-requirements">See full entry requirements</a></p>LocationSt LuciaFees<a href="#fees-scholarships">A$56800</a>Duration 4 Years Start Semester Semester 1 (22 Feb, 2027), Semester 2 (26 Jul, 2027) Semester dates for 2028 are yet to be confirmed QTAC Code<p>709511</p>Program Code2554CRICOS Code104903GAQFLevel 7<p><a href="#fees-scholarships">Scholarships available</a></p> <p> <h5> Program highlights </h5> </p> <p> <h5> Program highlights </h5> </p> <ul><li>Learn the core principles of design across hands-on studio-based projects.</li><li>Benefit from guest lectures by industry experts.</li><li>Take advantage of opportunities for placements and internships with leading businesses.</li><li>Tailor your studies to suit your interests and goals. Choose one major from 7 diverse business specialisations.</li></ul> <p>1 in Queensland for business and management studies</p><p>QS World University Rankings 2026</p> <p>1 in Queensland for arts and humanities</p><p>QS World University Rankings 2026</p> <p> <h5> Majors </h5> </p> <p>Tailor your studies to suit your goals. This program offers these options:</p><ul><li><p>Business Economics</p></li><li><p>Business Information Systems</p></li><li><p>Human Resources</p></li><li><p>Innovation and Entrepreneurship</p></li></ul><p><a href="#majors">See all majors</a></p> <p> <h5> How you''ll learn </h5> </p> <p>Your learning experiences are designed to best suit the learning outcomes of the courses you choose.</p><ul><li>Lectures</li><li>Tutorials</li><li>Fieldwork</li><li>Seminars</li><li>Studios</li></ul> <p> <h5> What you''ll study </h5> </p> <p>At UQ, degrees are called ''programs'' and subjects are called ''courses''.</p><p><a href="https://programs-courses.uq.edu.au/requirements/program/2554/2027">See courses and program structure</a></p><p><a href="https://www.uq.edu.au/study/docs/dual-degree-planners-2027/2027-Bachelors-of-Business-Management-Design-2554.pdf">View dual degree planner (PDF)</a></p> <p> <h5> Career possibilities </h5> </p> <p>Our programs prepare you for your first job and beyond. Depending on which major you choose, here are some of the careers you could be on your way to:</p><ul><li>Design manager</li><li>Business analyst</li><li>Change manager</li><li>Advertising specialist</li><li>Information systems designer</li><li>Workplace innovation consultant</li><li>Marketing manager</li><li>Business entrepreneur</li><li>Wayfinding designer</li><li>Product designer</li></ul> <p>Average annual salary range</p><h5>Innovation Manager</h5>$150–$170K<p>seek.com.au</p><p>Average annual salary range</p><h5>Design Manager</h5>$175–$195K<p>seek.com.au</p> <p> <h5> Professional memberships </h5> </p> <p>When you graduate, you may be eligible for memberships with the following professional organisations. Contact the organisation to find out how to become a member.</p><ul><li>Australian Human Resources Institute</li><li>Australian Marketing Institute</li><li>Economic Society of Australia</li></ul> <p>I chose to study this dual program to develop both my creative abilities and business acumen. My journey led me to unexpected opportunities, and what I’ve gained extends far beyond strategic and innovation skills.</p><p> Cory Su </p><p> Graduate, Bachelors of Business Management / Design </p><p>I have developed leadership, communication, and teamwork skills through my program. The experience of working with real companies during internships through UQ has given me the edge to be prepared for the real work environment after graduation.</p><p> Anantha (Nandu) Padmanabhan Anu </p><p> Graduate, Bachelor of Business Management </p> <p><a href="/events">See all events</a></p> <a href="/events/uq-open-day"> UQ Open Day </a><p>2 August </p><h5> UQ Open Day </h5><p>St Lucia</p> <p><a href="/stories">See all stories</a></p> <a href="/stories/business-management-majors-diversify-your-career-opportunities"> Business management majors: diversify your career opportunities </a><p>Careers</p><h5> Business management majors: diversify your career opportunities </h5><p>4-minute read</p><a href="/stories/why-study-business-uq"> Why study business at UQ? </a><p>Study tips</p><h5> Why study business at UQ? </h5><p>7-minute read</p><a href="/stories/what-can-you-do-with-a-bachelor-of-design"> What can you do with a Bachelor of Design? </a><p>Careers</p><h5> What can you do with a Bachelor of Design? </h5><p>6-minute read</p>',
    total_course_duration = '4 Years (or part time equivalent)',
    offshore_tuition_fee = 227200,
    onshore_tuition_fee = 55380,
    enrolment_fee = NULL,
    materials_fee = NULL,
    entry_requirements = '<h4>Entry Requirements</h4> <p> <h5> Prerequisites </h5> </p> Queensland Year 12 (or equivalent):<ul><li>General English subject (Units 3 &amp; 4, C), and</li><li>one of General Mathematics, Mathematical Methods or Specialist Mathematics (Units 3 &amp; 4, C).</li></ul> <p> <h5> Minimum entry score </h5> </p> <p>Select where you studied and your qualification to see the minimum entry score you need to be considered for this program.</p><p>Use the minimum entry score as a guide. Your score must be at least equivalent to the required Australian Year 12 ATAR score. Entry scores are reviewed each year.</p> <h5>Equivalent subjects</h5> <table><thead><tr><th>Subject</th><th>Qualification equivalent</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table><p> <h5> English language requirements </h5> </p> <p>IELTS overall 6.5; reading 6; writing 6; speaking 6; listening 6. For other English Language Proficiency Tests and Scores approved for UQ</p><p>TOEFL iBT (including Paper Edition) - Overall 87, listening 19, reading 19, writing 21 and speaking 19.</p><p>PTE Academic - Overall Score of 64 and 60 in all sub bands.</p><p>BE - A minimum overall grade of 4 plus a minimum grade of C in all macro skills.</p><p>CES - Overall 176 and 169 in all sub bands.</p><p>OET is not accepted.</p><p>There are other ways to meet the English language requirements. For some programs, additional conditions apply.</p><p><a href="/admissions/english-language-requirements">Learn how to meet the English language requirements</a></p> <p> <h5> Student visas </h5> </p> <p>International students who are accepted into full-time study in the Bachelors of Business Management / Design are eligible to apply for an Australian student visa (subclass 500).</p><p>There are a number of requirements you must satisfy before a visa is granted, including the Genuine Student (GS) requirement.</p><p><a href="/university-life/getting-prepared-to-come-to-australia/student-visas">Learn more about student visas</a></p> <p> <h5> Need help meeting the entry requirements? </h5> </p> <p>We can help you meet the minimum entry score, subject prerequisites or English language requirements for your preferred program.</p><p><a href="/admissions/undergraduate/consider-your-pathway-options">Learn about pathway options</a></p>',
    apply_form = 'https://study.uq.edu.au/study-options/programs/bachelors-business-management-design-2554',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '104903G';

UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Overview</h4> <p> Become a leader who thrives in dynamic, competitive global environments by combining business knowledge with in-demand language skills and cultural understanding. </p><p>Designed to develop your understanding of core business concepts, the Bachelor of Business Management allows you to specialise in one or 2 key areas.</p><p>Choose from marketing, human resources, business information systems, innovation and entrepreneurship, business economics, international business, and leadership and management science to focus your studies.</p><p>As a dual program, combining transferable business capabilities with language skills will give you a professional edge. Demand for language capabilities is increasing in the international business environment, and this program allows you to specialise in one or 2 languages.</p><p>The combination of these areas with the practical experience you’ll gain ensures you’ll graduate as a versatile, globally minded professional ready to excel in diverse business landscapes.</p><p><a href="#tab1">Domestic</a><a href="#tab2">International</a></p><p><a href="#entry-requirements">See full entry requirements</a></p>LocationSt LuciaDuration 4 Years (or part time equivalent)Start SemesterSemester 1 (22 Feb, 2027), Semester 2 (26 Jul, 2027)QTAC Code<p>710701</p>Program Code2543AQFLevel 7<p><a href="#how-to-apply">Admission schemes available</a></p><p><a href="#fees-scholarships">Scholarships available</a></p><p><a href="#entry-requirements">See full entry requirements</a></p>LocationSt LuciaFees<a href="#fees-scholarships">A$54616</a>Duration 4 Years Start Semester Semester 1 (22 Feb, 2027), Semester 2 (26 Jul, 2027) Semester dates for 2028 are yet to be confirmed QTAC Code<p>710701</p>Program Code2543CRICOS Code117052EAQFLevel 7<p><a href="#fees-scholarships">Scholarships available</a></p> <p> <h5> Program highlights </h5> </p> <p> <h5> Program highlights </h5> </p> <ul><li>Gain an edge in the international business environment by specialising in one language major or 2 language minors.</li><li>Develop a broad understanding of key business concepts and specialise in one or 2 fields.</li><li>Get practical business experience, learning from leading lecturers and extensive industry networks.</li></ul> <p>1 in Queensland for business and management studies</p><p>QS World University Rankings 2026</p> <p>1 in Queensland for modern languages</p><p>QS World University Rankings 2026</p> <p> <h5> Majors </h5> </p> <p>Tailor your studies to suit your goals. This program offers these options:</p><ul><li><p>Ancient Greek</p></li><li><p>Ancient Greek</p></li><li><p>Business Economics</p></li><li><p>Business Information Systems</p></li></ul><p><a href="#majors">See all majors</a></p> <p> <h5> How you''ll learn </h5> </p> <p>Your learning experiences are designed to best suit the learning outcomes of the courses you choose.</p><ul><li>Lectures</li><li>Tutorials</li><li>Seminars</li></ul> <p> <h5> Placements and work experience </h5> </p> <p> Work Integrated Learning (WIL) is embedded across our curriculum, with a strong focus in our major capstone courses. Specifically, RBUS3888 and RBUS3999 offer students the chance to apply theoretical and conceptual knowledge in real-world contexts. These courses enable you to either collaborate with industry partners on live projects, addressing genuine business challenges, or undertake a professional placement to gain practical workplace experience. This integrated approach helps you build employability skills, deepen your understanding of professional workplace dynamics, expand your network, and engage with current business issues. </p> <p> <h5> What you''ll study </h5> </p> <p>At UQ, degrees are called ''programs'' and subjects are called ''courses''.</p><p><a href="https://programs-courses.uq.edu.au/requirements/program/2543/2027">See courses and program structure</a></p><p><a href="https://www.uq.edu.au/study/docs/dual-degree-planners-2027/2027-Bachelor-of-Business-Management-Diploma-in-Languages-2543.pdf">View dual degree planner (PDF)</a></p> <p> <h5> Career possibilities </h5> </p> <p>Our programs prepare you for your first job and beyond. Depending on which major you choose, here are some of the careers you could be on your way to:</p><ul><li>Business development manager</li><li>Business analyst</li><li>Corporate communications officer</li><li>Information systems designer</li><li>Human resources adviser</li><li>International trade manager</li><li>Workplace innovation consultant</li><li>Marketing manager</li><li>Banking and financial services officer</li><li>Project manager</li></ul> <p>Average annual salary range</p><h5>Business Development Manager</h5>$105–$125K<p>seek.com.au</p><p>Average annual salary range</p><h5>Supply Chain Manager</h5>$130–$150K<p>seek.com.au</p> <p> <h5> Professional memberships </h5> </p> <p>When you graduate, you may be eligible for memberships with the following professional organisations. Contact the organisation to find out how to become a member.</p><ul><li>Australian Human Resources Institute</li><li>Australian Marketing Institute</li><li>Economic Society of Australia</li></ul> <p>I have developed leadership, communication, and teamwork skills through my program. The experience of working with real companies during internships through UQ has given me the edge to be prepared for the real work environment after graduation.</p><p> Anantha (Nandu) Padmanabhan Anu </p><p> Graduate, Bachelor of Business Management </p><p>I got to meet and work with brilliant startup founders in Singapore who are contributing to solving problems around the world. Connecting with, and learning from, these brilliant minds has been an amazing opportunity.</p><p> Jeremy Kester Hanani </p><p> Bachelor of Business Management </p><p>I was an intern at the Max Planck Institute in Germany and... because I understood the language, I had a seat at the table. That’s truly one of the most powerful aspects of learning another language – it opens so many doors. </p><p> Anna John </p><p> Graduate, Diploma in Languages (French) </p> <p><a href="/events">See all events</a></p> <a href="/events/ancient-history-experience-day"> Ancient History Experience Day </a><p>15 July </p><h5> Ancient History Experience Day </h5><p>St Lucia</p><a href="/events/world-religions-experience-day-2026"> World Religions Experience Day 2026 </a><p>22 July - 23 July </p><h5> World Religions Experience Day 2026 </h5><p>St Lucia</p><a href="/events/uq-open-day"> UQ Open Day </a><p>2 August </p><h5> UQ Open Day </h5><p>St Lucia</p> <p><a href="/stories">See all stories</a></p> <a href="/stories/why-study-business-uq"> Why study business at UQ? </a><p>Study tips</p><h5> Why study business at UQ? </h5><p>7-minute read</p><a href="/stories/business-management-majors-diversify-your-career-opportunities"> Business management majors: diversify your career opportunities </a><p>Careers</p><h5> Business management majors: diversify your career opportunities </h5><p>4-minute read</p><a href="/stories/finding-career-with-purpose"> What is social entrepreneurship? </a><p>Careers</p><h5> What is social entrepreneurship? </h5><p>8-minute read</p>',
    total_course_duration = '4 Years (or part time equivalent)',
    offshore_tuition_fee = 218464,
    onshore_tuition_fee = 53000,
    enrolment_fee = NULL,
    materials_fee = NULL,
    entry_requirements = '<h4>Entry Requirements</h4> <p> <h5> Prerequisites </h5> </p> Queensland Year 12 (or equivalent):<ul><li>General English subject (Units 3 &amp; 4, C)</li><li>one of General Mathematics, Mathematical Methods or Specialist Mathematics (Units 3 &amp; 4, C)</li></ul> <p> <h5> Minimum entry score </h5> </p> <p>Select where you studied and your qualification to see the minimum entry score you need to be considered for this program.</p><p>Use the minimum entry score as a guide. Your score must be at least equivalent to the required Australian Year 12 ATAR score. Entry scores are reviewed each year.</p> <h5>Equivalent subjects</h5> <table><thead><tr><th>Subject</th><th>Qualification equivalent</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table><p> <h5> English language requirements </h5> </p> <p>IELTS overall 6.5; reading 6; writing 6; speaking 6; listening 6. For other English Language Proficiency Tests and Scores approved for UQ</p><p>TOEFL iBT (including Paper Edition) - Overall 87, listening 19, reading 19, writing 21 and speaking 19.</p><p>PTE Academic - Overall Score of 64 and 60 in all sub bands.</p><p>BE - A minimum overall grade of 4 plus a minimum grade of C in all macro skills.</p><p>CES - Overall 176 and 169 in all sub bands.</p><p>OET is not accepted.</p><p>There are other ways to meet the English language requirements. For some programs, additional conditions apply.</p><p><a href="/admissions/english-language-requirements">Learn how to meet the English language requirements</a></p> <p> <h5> Student visas </h5> </p> <p>International students who are accepted into full-time study in the Bachelor of Business Management / Diploma in Languages are eligible to apply for an Australian student visa (subclass 500).</p><p>There are a number of requirements you must satisfy before a visa is granted, including the Genuine Student (GS) requirement.</p><p><a href="/university-life/getting-prepared-to-come-to-australia/student-visas">Learn more about student visas</a></p> <p> <h5> Need help meeting the entry requirements? </h5> </p> <p>We can help you meet the minimum entry score, subject prerequisites or English language requirements for your preferred program.</p><p><a href="/admissions/undergraduate/consider-your-pathway-options">Learn about pathway options</a></p> <p> <h5> Additional application information </h5> </p> <p> Students who commence in Semester 2 may not be able to begin language studies until Semester 1. This will be dependent upon a student¿s previous language proficiency and the language(s) they nominate to undertake; the majority of introductory courses are offered in Semester 1 only each year. Students should contact the School of Languages and Cultures Students Administration team for advice. </p>',
    apply_form = 'https://study.uq.edu.au/study-options/programs/bachelor-business-management-diploma-languages-2543',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '117052E';

UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Overview</h4> <p> Prepare to lead and develop businesses across all sectors. Learn to think like an economist by understanding how people make decisions, how markets operate, and how the world works. </p><p>This dual degree program allows you to combine specific business management studies with an area of focus in economics.</p><p>During your business studies, you''ll examine real-life case studies and undertake projects and placements with leading businesses. With course content developed in close collaboration with industry partners, you''ll study topics including:</p><ul><li>accounting</li><li>economics</li><li>law</li><li>marketing</li><li>business information systems</li><li>organisational behaviour.</li></ul><p>The Bachelor of Economics will teach you how to question, analyse, model and predict behaviour. Economics is central to decision-making in business, markets, trade, government, health and a range of other areas.</p><p>You''ll complete compulsory courses that will build your knowledge about key economic principles, theories and tools. You''ll study topics including microeconomics, macroeconomics, econometrics and more.</p><p>By combining these 2 areas of study, you’ll graduate with strong decision-making and analytical skills, as well as the ability to apply business and economic theory to solve industry challenges.</p><p><a href="#tab1">Domestic</a><a href="#tab2">International</a></p><p><a href="#entry-requirements">See full entry requirements</a></p>LocationSt LuciaDuration 4 Years (or part time equivalent)Start SemesterSemester 1 (22 Feb, 2027), Semester 2 (26 Jul, 2027)QTAC Code<p>710201</p>Program Code2181AQFLevel 7<p><a href="#how-to-apply">Admission schemes available</a></p><p><a href="#fees-scholarships">Scholarships available</a></p><p><a href="#entry-requirements">See full entry requirements</a></p>LocationSt LuciaFees<a href="#fees-scholarships">A$56800</a>Duration 4 Years Start Semester Semester 1 (22 Feb, 2027), Semester 2 (26 Jul, 2027) Semester dates for 2028 are yet to be confirmed QTAC Code<p>710201</p>Program Code2181CRICOS Code098328KAQFLevel 7<p><a href="#fees-scholarships">Scholarships available</a></p> <p> <h5> Program highlights </h5> </p> <p> <h5> Program highlights </h5> </p> <ul><li>Take advantage of UQ''s strong industry collaborations. Gain credit for industry placements, industry consulting projects or global study experiences.</li><li>Learn from award-winning research and industry experts. UQ is home to experts in energy and climate change, productivity and efficiency analysis, business leadership and development economics.</li><li>Unlock opportunities for a diverse range of change-making careers in the public, private and not-for-profit sector.</li></ul> <p>3 in Australia for business and economics</p><p>Times Higher Education World University Rankings 2026</p> <p>1 in Queensland for business and economics</p><p>Times Higher Education World University Rankings 2026</p> <p> <h5> Majors </h5> </p> <p>Tailor your studies to suit your goals. This program offers these options:</p><ul><li><p>Business Information Systems</p></li><li><p>Economics and Public Policy</p></li><li><p>Economics of Strategy and Behaviour</p></li><li><p>Human Resources</p></li></ul><p><a href="#majors">See all majors</a></p> <p> <h5> How you''ll learn </h5> </p> <p>Your learning experiences are designed to best suit the learning outcomes of the courses you choose.</p><ul><li>Lectures</li><li>Tutorials</li><li>Research experience</li><li>Workshops</li></ul> <p> <h5> Placements and work experience </h5> </p> <p> Work Integrated Learning (WIL) is embedded across our curriculum, with a strong focus in our major capstone courses. Specifically, RBUS3888 and RBUS3999 offer students the chance to apply theoretical and conceptual knowledge in real-world contexts. These courses enable you to either collaborate with industry partners on live projects, addressing genuine business challenges, or undertake a professional placement to gain practical workplace experience. This integrated approach helps you build employability skills, deepen your understanding of professional workplace dynamics, expand your network, and engage with current business issues. </p> <p> <h5> What you''ll study </h5> </p> <p>At UQ, degrees are called ''programs'' and subjects are called ''courses''.</p><p><a href="https://programs-courses.uq.edu.au/requirements/program/2181/2027">See courses and program structure</a></p><p><a href="https://www.uq.edu.au/study/docs/dual-degree-planners-2027/2027-Bachelors-of-Business-Management-Economics-2181.pdf">View dual degree planner (PDF)</a></p> <p> <h5> Career possibilities </h5> </p> <p>Our programs prepare you for your first job and beyond. Depending on which major you choose, here are some of the careers you could be on your way to:</p><ul><li>Investment analyst</li><li>Economic consultant</li><li>Economics, policy and social analyst</li><li>Business systems planner</li><li>Business development manager</li><li>Business management consultant</li><li>International trade manager</li><li>Corporate banking analyst</li><li>Product manager</li><li>Policy evaluation officer</li></ul> <p>Average annual salary range</p><h5>Business Analyst</h5>$110–$130K<p>seek.com.au</p><p>Average annual salary range</p><h5>Strategy Consultant</h5>$115–$125K<p>seek.com.au</p> <p> <h5> Professional memberships </h5> </p> <p>When you graduate, you may be eligible for memberships with the following professional organisations. Contact the organisation to find out how to become a member.</p><ul><li>Australian Human Resources Institute</li><li>Australian Marketing Institute</li><li>Economic Society of Australia</li></ul> <p>I have developed leadership, communication, and teamwork skills through my program. The experience of working with real companies during internships through UQ has given me the edge to be prepared for the real work environment after graduation.</p><p> Anantha (Nandu) Padmanabhan Anu </p><p> Graduate, Bachelor of Business Management </p><p>During my studies, I had the chance to intern at a bio-chemical engineering firm in Singapore, where I gained first-hand insight into the startup ecosystem. This experience ultimately led me to compete in a pitch competition at Oxford University on wicked problems.</p><p> Cory Su </p><p> Graduate, Bachelors of Business Management / Design </p><p>Discussing real case studies at UQ has helped me understand current economic and policy challenges. I’ve attended guest lectures from industry professionals, including economists from Queensland Treasury, who shared how policies are designed and implemented in practice.</p><p> Kinaura Maisha Sugiarto </p><p> Graduate, Bachelor of Economics </p> <p><a href="/events">See all events</a></p> <a href="/events/uq-open-day"> UQ Open Day </a><p>2 August </p><h5> UQ Open Day </h5><p>St Lucia</p> <p><a href="/stories">See all stories</a></p> <a href="/stories/business-management-majors-diversify-your-career-opportunities"> Business management majors: diversify your career opportunities </a><p>Careers</p><h5> Business management majors: diversify your career opportunities </h5><p>4-minute read</p><a href="/stories/what-can-you-do-economics-degree"> What can you do with an economics degree? </a><p>Careers</p><h5> What can you do with an economics degree? </h5><p>14-minute read</p><a href="/stories/why-study-economics"> Why study economics? </a><p>Careers</p><h5> Why study economics? </h5><p>5-minute read</p>',
