UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Overview</h4> <p> Learn how to assess and treat a range of emotional and behavioural problems so you can meet your registration requirements to become a psychologist. </p><p>The Master of Clinical Psychology is a 2-year full-time program that provides the training, skills and knowledge to enable you to practice competently and confidently in the psychology profession.</p><p>Clinical psychologists aim to promote optimal levels of psychological functioning and to decrease levels of psychological distress. They have expertise in the assessment, diagnosis, treatment and prevention of a broad range of emotional and behavioural problems, including anxiety, depression, stress, substance use disorders, adjustment to physical illness, relationship difficulties and learning disabilities.</p><p>Through a combination of coursework, supervised practice and research, you’ll gain in-depth knowledge and professional skills in clinical psychology. You''ll also develop a strong foundation in the scientific basis and practice of clinical psychology and receive training in clinical practice, which employs evidence-based, best-practice models in health and mental health settings.</p><p>You''ll build your skills and apply your knowledge through supervised clinical placements in a range of organisations, including not-for-profit, community services, hospitals and private practice.</p><p><a href="#tab1">Domestic</a><a href="#tab2">International</a></p><p><a href="#entry-requirements">See full entry requirements</a></p><p>LocationSt LuciaDuration 2 Years (or part time equivalent)Start SemesterSemester 1 (22 Feb, 2027)Program Code5164AQFLevel 9</p><p><a href="#fees-scholarships">Scholarships available</a></p><p><a href="#entry-requirements">See full entry requirements</a></p><p>LocationSt LuciaFees<a href="#fees-scholarships">A$60952</a>Duration 2 Years Start Semester Semester 1 (22 Feb, 2027) Semester dates for 2028 are yet to be confirmed Program Code5164CRICOS Code026000GAQFLevel 9</p><p><a href="#fees-scholarships">Scholarships available</a></p> <p> <h5> Program highlights </h5> </p> <p> <h5> Program highlights </h5> </p> <ul><li>Be confident and job-ready after completing 4 supervised placements in a range of healthcare settings, including the UQ Psychology Clinic</li><li>Learn from academics who''ve made major contributions to the field and are actively involved in clinical practice and research.</li><li>Participate in collegial practices such as regular case presentations involving academic staff and external supervisors. </li><li>Lead a research thesis with supervision from a leading researcher on an applied mental health and clinical topic.</li></ul> <p>27 in the world for psychology</p><p>QS World University Rankings 2026</p> <p>1 in Queensland for psychology</p><p>Global Ranking of Academic Subjects 2025</p> <p> <h5> How you''ll learn </h5> </p> <p>Your learning experiences are designed to best suit the learning outcomes of the courses you choose.</p><ul><li>Lectures</li><li>Tutorials</li><li>Work placements</li><li>Research experience</li><li>Fieldwork</li></ul> <p> <h5> What you''ll study </h5> </p> <p>At UQ, degrees are called ''programs'' and subjects are called ''courses''. Here''s a sample of the courses you could study in this program:</p><ul><li>Acceptance and Commitment therapy</li><li>Addiction science and practice</li><li>Applied gerontology</li><li>Assessment in psychological practice</li><li>Behavioural Family Intervention</li><li>Clinical psychopathology</li></ul><p><a href="https://programs-courses.uq.edu.au/requirements/program/5164/2027">See courses and program structure</a></p> <p> <h5> Career possibilities </h5> </p> <p>Postgraduate study can take you anywhere. Here are some of the careers you could be on your way to:</p><ul><li>Clinical psychologist</li><li>Mental health clinician</li><li>Mental health social worker</li><li>School psychologist</li><li>Mental health professional</li></ul> <p>Graduate salary</p><h5>Psychology (postgraduate)</h5>$69K–$86K<p>compared.edu.au</p> <p> <h5> Program accreditation </h5> </p> <p>The Master of Clinical Psychology is accredited by:</p><ul><li>Australian Psychology Accreditation Council</li></ul> <p>The composition of the Master of Clinical Psychology program, along with UQ’s involvement in quality research, appealed to me. I really enjoy the practical exercises, allowing me to practise my skills but I also get the chance to learn from my peers. </p><p> Tatiana </p><p> Graduate, Master of Clinical Psychology </p><p>The program’s strong emphasis on reflective practice has deepened my understanding of the therapeutic relationship, and I now feel more confident and equipped to navigate the complexities of mental health care with both empathy and professionalism.</p><p> Sam Reilly </p><p> Graduate, Master of Clinical Psychology </p><p>I loved that the classes were focused on teaching theoretical knowledge and practical skills that would be relevant to my future practice as a psychologist. I felt set up for success on both internal and external placements.</p><p> Lachlan Molan </p><p> Graduate, Master of Clinical Psychology </p><p>From the first year, the program provided diverse experiences that supported my clinical and personal growth. Working with clients from varied backgrounds allowed me to explore different therapeutic approaches and develop skills in cognitive assessment.</p><p> Linda Nguyen </p><p> Graduate, Master of Clinical Psychology </p> <p><a href="/events">See all events</a></p> <a href="/events/uq-open-day"> UQ Open Day </a><p>2 August </p><h5> UQ Open Day </h5><p>St Lucia</p> <p><a href="/stories">See all stories</a></p> <a href="/stories/turning-her-curiosity-healthcare-career"> Turning her curiosity into a healthcare career </a><p>UQ people</p><h5> Turning her curiosity into a healthcare career </h5><p>4-minute read</p><a href="/stories/4-business-psychology-courses-transform-career"> Transform your career with 4 business psychology courses </a><p>Careers</p><h5> Transform your career with 4 business psychology courses </h5><p>3-minute read</p><a href="/stories/studying-business-psychology-postgraduate"> What’s it like to study business psychology as a postgraduate? </a><p>Uni life</p><h5> What’s it like to study business psychology as a postgraduate? </h5><p>5-minute read</p>',
    total_course_duration = '2 Years (or part time equivalent)',
    offshore_tuition_fee = 121904,
    onshore_tuition_fee = 9480,
