UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Overview</h4> <p> Prepare yourself for a career in finance, business or law by combining an in-depth understanding of commerce with advanced legal knowledge and highly transferable skills. </p><p>This program combines training in conducting research relevant to business and finance with high-level instruction in the law. It will also help you develop extensive personal and professional skills.</p><p>In your commerce studies, you''ll examine the fundamental principles of commerce and learn how you can apply and adapt them in response to specific challenges faced by businesses. You''ll build specialised knowledge and skills through a major of your choice.</p><p>Your law courses will take place in modern, customised seminar-style learning spaces. You''ll have the opportunity to test your knowledge with peers and teachers in an active learning environment.</p><p>Your advanced legal and commerce capabilities will set you apart in a competitive job market and can also provide a pathway to future research or learning.</p><p><a href="#tab1">Domestic</a><a href="#tab2">International</a></p><p><a href="#entry-requirements">See full entry requirements</a></p>LocationSt LuciaDuration 5 Years (or part time equivalent)Start SemesterSemester 1 (22 Feb, 2027)QTAC Code<p>711901</p>Program Code2465AQFLevel 8<p><a href="#how-to-apply">Admission schemes available</a></p><p><a href="#fees-scholarships">Scholarships available</a></p><p><a href="#entry-requirements">See full entry requirements</a></p>LocationSt LuciaFees<a href="#fees-scholarships">A$56800</a>Duration 5 Years Start Semester Semester 1 (22 Feb, 2027) Semester dates for 2028 are yet to be confirmed QTAC Code<p>711901</p>Program Code2465CRICOS Code103164AAQFLevel 8<p><a href="#fees-scholarships">Scholarships available</a></p> <p> <h5> Program highlights </h5> </p> <p> <h5> Program highlights </h5> </p> <ul><li>Develop practical legal skills and professional networks through a comprehensive co-curricular program and events.</li><li>Gain the ability to successfully design and conduct research projects.</li><li>Fulfil the academic requirements for admission as a legal practitioner throughout Australia.</li><li>Advance your critical and analytical thinking, communication, problem-solving and project management capabilities. </li></ul> <p>1 in Queensland for law and legal studies</p><p>QS World University Rankings 2026</p> <p>1 in Queensland for accounting and finance</p><p>QS World University Rankings 2026</p> <p> <h5> Majors </h5> </p> <p>Tailor your studies to suit your goals. This program offers these options:</p><ul><li><p>Accounting</p></li><li><p>Business Analytics</p></li><li><p>Business Information Systems</p></li><li><p>Finance</p></li></ul><p><a href="#majors">See all majors</a></p> <p> <h5> How you''ll learn </h5> </p> <p>Your learning experiences are designed to best suit the learning outcomes of the courses you choose.</p><ul><li>Lectures</li><li>Tutorials</li><li>Overseas study</li><li>Research experience</li><li>Seminars</li></ul> <p> <h5> Placements and work experience </h5> </p> <p> Work Integrated Learning (WIL) is embedded across our curriculum, with a strong focus in our major capstone courses. Specifically, RBUS3888 and RBUS3999 offer students the chance to apply theoretical and conceptual knowledge in real-world contexts. These courses enable you to either collaborate with industry partners on live projects, addressing genuine business challenges, or undertake a professional placement to gain practical workplace experience. This integrated approach helps you build employability skills, deepen your understanding of professional workplace dynamics, expand your network, and engage with current business issues. </p> <p> <h5> What you''ll study </h5> </p> <p>At UQ, degrees are called ''programs'' and subjects are called ''courses''.</p><p><a href="https://programs-courses.uq.edu.au/requirements/program/2465/2027">See courses and program structure</a></p><p><a href="https://www.uq.edu.au/study/docs/dual-degree-planners-2027/2027-Bachelors-of-Commerce-Laws-Honours-2465.pdf">View dual degree planner (PDF)</a></p> <p> <h5> Career possibilities </h5> </p> <p>Our programs prepare you for your first job and beyond. Depending on which major you choose, here are some of the careers you could be on your way to:</p><ul><li>Business systems planner</li><li>Business systems analyst</li><li>Risk manager</li><li>Company secretary</li><li>Solicitor</li><li>Barrister</li><li>Legal project manager</li><li>Business analyst</li><li>Management consultant</li></ul> <p>Average annual salary range</p><h5>Risk and Compliance Manager</h5>$130–$150K<p>seek.com.au</p><p>Average annual salary range</p><h5>Solicitor</h5>$100–$120K<p>seek.com.au</p> <p> <h5> Professional memberships </h5> </p> <p>When you graduate, you may be eligible for memberships with the following professional organisations. Contact the organisation to find out how to become a member.</p><ul><li>Association of Certified Chartered Accountants</li><li>Chartered Accountants Australia &amp; New Zealand</li><li>Chartered Financial Analyst (CFA) Institute</li><li>Certified Institute for Management Accountants</li><li>Certified Practising Accountants Australia</li><li>Financial Services Institute of Australasia</li><li>Governance Institute of Australia</li><li>Institute of Public Accountants</li><li>Bar Association of Queensland</li><li>Queensland Law Society</li></ul> <p> <h5> Program accreditation </h5> </p> <p>The Bachelors of Commerce / Laws (Honours) is accredited by:</p><ul><li>Legal Practitioners Admissions Board</li></ul> <p>My law degree has enhanced my advocacy and drafting skills, while my commerce degree has improved my ability to analyse complex financial information. My overall experience at UQ has made me confident to pursue my professional ambitions.</p><p> Priscilla Gyasi-Agyei </p><p> Graduate, Bachelors of Commerce / Laws (Honours) </p><p>UQ incorporates real life challenges into the learning – someone from industry shares insight into the work in almost every course. With this, my knowledge about a field becomes clearer and my direction for the future is brighter.</p><p> Ainur Nabila Nor Azam Azimi </p><p> Graduate, Bachelor of Commerce </p><p>I was lucky enough to travel to Indonesia as part of the New Columbo Plan to explore anti-corruption law. It provided a great opportunity to witness how the skills you learn in university translate to the real world. </p><p> Angus Dick </p><p> Current student, Bachelors of Commerce / Laws (Honours) </p> <p><a href="/events">See all events</a></p> <a href="/events/uq-open-day"> UQ Open Day </a><p>2 August </p><h5> UQ Open Day </h5><p>St Lucia</p> <p><a href="/stories">See all stories</a></p> <a href="/stories/whats-it-like-study-commerce-uq"> What''s it really like to study commerce at UQ? </a><p>Uni life</p><h5> What''s it really like to study commerce at UQ? </h5><p>5-minute read</p><a href="/stories/what-jobs-can-you-get-commerce-degree"> What jobs can you get with a commerce degree? </a><p>Careers</p><h5> What jobs can you get with a commerce degree? </h5><p>4-minute read</p><a href="/stories/why-study-law-uq"> Why study law at UQ? </a><p>UQ people</p><h5> Why study law at UQ? </h5><p>5-minute read</p>',
    total_course_duration = '5 Years (or part time equivalent)',
    offshore_tuition_fee = 284000,
    onshore_tuition_fee = 81450,
    enrolment_fee = NULL,
