UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Overview</h4> <p> Combine computer science foundations with master’s-level cyber security in one accelerated pathway. </p><p>Build the systems people rely on, then learn how to defend them. In this 4-year vertical dual degree, you''ll complete a bachelor’s and master’s qualification in less time than studying them separately.</p><p>In your first years, you''ll explore how computer-based systems are created, analysed and improved. You''ll build technical knowledge across programming, computing theory and computer technology before moving into advanced cyber security study.</p><p>Through hands-on learning, laboratory work, seminars and workshops, you''ll apply your ideas to technical problems and strengthen your ability to analyse, communicate and respond to risk. As your skills grow, you''ll examine the global cyber security landscape and explore ways to defend, adapt and lead in a more resilient digital world.</p><p>The Bachelor of Computer Science / Master of Cyber Security can support your pathway into a range of careers. Choose from majors and fields of study including AI, Cryptography, Cyber Defence and Cyber Security, and prepare for career paths across cyber analysis, digital forensics, security architecture, IT audit, policy and cryptography.</p><p>Learn more about <a href="/sites/default/files/2020-10/eait-vertical-duals.pdf">vertical dual degrees (PDF, 34.2 KB)</a>.</p><p><a href="#tab1">Domestic</a><a href="#tab2">International</a></p><p><a href="#entry-requirements">See full entry requirements</a></p>LocationSt LuciaDuration 4 Years (or part time equivalent)Start SemesterSemester 1 (22 Feb, 2027), Semester 2 (26 Jul, 2027)QTAC Code<p>733411</p>Program Code2560AQFLevel 9<p><a href="#how-to-apply">Admission schemes available</a></p><p><a href="#fees-scholarships">Scholarships available</a></p><p><a href="#entry-requirements">See full entry requirements</a></p>LocationSt LuciaFees<a href="#fees-scholarships">A$60952</a>Duration 4 Years Start Semester Semester 1 (22 Feb, 2027), Semester 2 (26 Jul, 2027) Semester dates for 2028 are yet to be confirmed QTAC Code<p>733411</p>Program Code2560CRICOS Code103152EAQFLevel 9<p><a href="#fees-scholarships">Scholarships available</a></p> <p> <h5> Program highlights </h5> </p> <p> <h5> Program highlights </h5> </p> <ul><li>Save time by completing a bachelor’s and master’s qualification in 4 years instead of 5.</li><li>Graduate with a combination of high-level technical skills and a global perspective on cyber security and information security fundamentals.</li><li>Benefit from a Commonwealth Supported Place throughout the program (Domestic students).</li><li>Enjoy flexible study options: exit early and graduate with a Bachelor of Computer Science.</li></ul> <p>1 in Queensland for computer science and information systems</p><p>QS World University Rankings 2026</p> <p>1 in Queensland for mathematics</p><p>QS World University Rankings 2026</p> <p> <h5> Majors </h5> </p> <p>Tailor your studies to suit your goals. This program offers these options:</p><ul><li><p>Artificial Intelligence</p></li><li><p>Cryptography</p></li><li><p>Cyber Defence</p></li><li><p>Cyber Security</p></li></ul><p><a href="#majors">See all majors</a></p> <p> <h5> How you''ll learn </h5> </p> <p>Your learning experiences are designed to best suit the learning outcomes of the courses you choose.</p><ul><li>Lectures</li><li>Tutorials</li><li>Laboratory work</li><li>Seminars</li><li>Workshops</li></ul> <p> <h5> What you''ll study </h5> </p> <p>At UQ, degrees are called ''programs'' and subjects are called ''courses''.</p><p><a href="https://programs-courses.uq.edu.au/requirements/program/2560/2027">See courses and program structure</a></p><p><a href="https://www.uq.edu.au/study/docs/dual-degree-planners-2027/2027-Bachelor-of-Computer-Science-Master-of-Cyber-Security-2560.pdf">View dual degree planner (PDF)</a></p> <p> <h5> Career possibilities </h5> </p> <p>Our programs prepare you for your first job and beyond. Depending on which major you choose, here are some of the careers you could be on your way to:</p><ul><li>Cyber security analyst</li><li>Cyber criminologist</li><li>Digital forensics specialist</li><li>IT auditor</li><li>Security architect</li><li>Policy adviser</li><li>Cyber insurance adviser and provider</li><li>Cryptographer</li></ul> <p>Average annual salary range</p><h5>Cyber Security Analyst</h5>$100–$120K<p>seek.com.au</p><p>Graduate salary</p><h5>Computing and information systems (undergraduate)</h5>$72K–$78K<p>compared.edu.au</p> <p> <h5> Next steps after graduation </h5> </p> <p>You''ll graduate with 2 qualifications and a combination of computer science foundations and advanced cyber security knowledge. Explore roles across industries, including:</p><ul><li>cyber security</li><li>software</li><li>information security</li><li>digital forensics</li><li>technology governance</li><li>policy.</li></ul><p>Depending on your goals, you can work in technical cyber security roles, advise organisations on digital risk, investigate cyber incidents, or contribute to the design of secure systems and services.</p> <p> <h5> Professional memberships </h5> </p> <p>When you graduate, you may be eligible for memberships with the following professional organisations. Contact the organisation to find out how to become a member.</p><ul><li>Australian Computer Society</li></ul> <p>There is a lack of professionals with cyber security knowledge, problem-solving and some DevOps skills. Experience and specific skills can be acquired on the job, however applicants with solid cyber security knowledge are at an advantage.</p><p> Mike Holm </p><p> Operations Manager, AusCERT </p> <p><a href="/events">See all events</a></p> <a href="/events/uq-open-day"> UQ Open Day </a><p>2 August </p><h5> UQ Open Day </h5><p>St Lucia</p> <p><a href="/stories">See all stories</a></p> <a href="/stories/prepare-courtroom-mooting-uq"> Prepare for the courtroom: mooting at UQ </a><p>Uni life</p><h5> Prepare for the courtroom: mooting at UQ </h5><p>4-minute read</p><a href="/stories/law-pathways-how-get-law-uq"> Law pathways: how to get into law at UQ </a><p>Study tips</p><h5> Law pathways: how to get into law at UQ </h5><p>5-minute read</p><a href="/stories/how-uq-pro-bono-centre-shaping-career-ready-graduates"> How the UQ Pro Bono Centre is shaping career-ready graduates </a><p>UQ people</p><h5> How the UQ Pro Bono Centre is shaping career-ready graduates </h5><p>5-minute read</p>',
