UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Overview</h4> <p> Strengthen your leadership expertise and get a professional advantage in your chosen area of education. </p><p>This program is suitable for practising teachers, administrators and other educational professionals, as well as professionals in other areas wishing to gain expertise in education. It can be completed in six months full-time — and most fields of study can be completed part-time in one year.</p><p>Specialise in one of seven fields of study: Behaviour Support; Curriculum; Guidance, Counselling and Careers; Leadership; Psychology Education; Science of Learning or Inclusive Education. Depending on your area of specialisation you can choose to complete all aspects of a practicum that focuses on advanced research and teaching interests.</p><p>Some pathways offer specific qualifications, while others offer significant professional advantage to educators interested in career advancement or broadening their career options.</p><p><a href="#tab1">Domestic</a><a href="#tab2">International</a></p><p><a href="#entry-requirements">See full entry requirements</a></p><p>LocationExternal, St LuciaDuration Half Year (or part time equivalent)Start SemesterSemester 1 (22 Feb, 2027), Semester 2 (26 Jul, 2027)Program Code5448AQFLevel 8</p><p><a href="#fees-scholarships">Scholarships available</a></p><p><a href="#entry-requirements">See full entry requirements</a></p><p>LocationExternal, St LuciaFees<a href="#fees-scholarships">A$24040</a>Duration Half Year Start Semester Semester 1 (22 Feb, 2027), Semester 2 (26 Jul, 2027) Semester dates for 2028 are yet to be confirmed Program Code5448CRICOS Code061819GAQFLevel 8</p><p><a href="#fees-scholarships">Scholarships available</a></p> <p> <h5> Program highlights </h5> </p> <p> <h5> Program highlights </h5> </p> <ul><li>Strengthen your leadership expertise in educational practice, policy and theory.</li><li>Obtain the knowledge and skills required for specialised fields of work.</li><li>Gain qualifications that enhance career advancement and options.</li><li>Improve your research skills by engaging in an extended research-based project.</li></ul> <p>41 in the world for education</p><p>QS World University Rankings 2026</p> <p>1 in Queensland for education and training</p><p>QS World University Rankings 2026</p> <p> <h5> Fields of study </h5> </p> <p>Tailor your studies to suit your goals. This program offers these options:</p><ul><li><p>Behaviour Support</p></li><li><p>Curriculum</p></li><li><p>Guidance, Counselling and Careers</p></li><li><p>Inclusive Education</p></li></ul><p><a href="#majors">See all fields of study</a></p> <p> <h5> How you''ll learn </h5> </p> <p>Your learning experiences are designed to best suit the learning outcomes of the courses you choose.</p><ul><li>Lectures</li><li>Tutorials</li><li>Work placements</li><li>Overseas study</li><li>Research experience</li><li>Fieldwork</li><li>Seminars</li></ul> <p> <h5> What you''ll study </h5> </p> <p>At UQ, degrees are called ''programs'' and subjects are called ''courses''. Here''s a sample of the courses you could study in this program:</p><ul><li>Introduction to Educational Studies</li><li>Global Indigenous Knowledge and Education</li><li>Foundation of the Science of Learning [part of Science of Learning field of study]</li><li>Student Behaviour in Educational Contexts [part of Behaviour Support field of study]</li></ul><p><a href="https://programs-courses.uq.edu.au/requirements/program/5448/2027">See courses and program structure</a></p> <p> <h5> Career possibilities </h5> </p> <p>Postgraduate study can take you anywhere. Depending on which field you choose, here are some of the careers you could be on your way to:</p><ul><li>Behaviour management counsellor</li><li>Special needs teacher</li><li>Curriculum planner</li><li>School curriculum adviser</li><li>Career development practitioner</li><li>Guidance counsellor</li><li>Educational administrator</li><li>Multicultural teacher</li><li>School principal</li></ul> <p>Average annual salary range</p><h5>Guidance Counsellor</h5>$125–$130K<p>seek.com.au</p> <p> <h5> Next steps after graduation </h5> </p> <p>After completing the Graduate Certificate in Educational Studies, you’ll be well positioned to strengthen your leadership capabilities and advance your career in a range of education settings.</p><p>You will build expertise in areas such as Leadership, Curriculum, Behaviour Support, Inclusive Education and more, enabling you to move into or progress within teaching, administrative and specialist roles.</p><p>Depending on your chosen field and practicum experience, you may gain specific qualifications or a strong professional advantage for career advancement or transition into new education-focused roles.</p><p>You may also choose to continue further study, applying your enhanced knowledge of teaching, learning and educational practice across diverse professional contexts.</p> <p><a href="/events">See all events</a></p> <a href="/events/uq-open-day"> UQ Open Day </a><p>2 August </p><h5> UQ Open Day </h5><p>St Lucia</p><a href="/events/master-teaching-information-webinar"> Master of Teaching information webinar </a><p>20 October </p><h5> Master of Teaching information webinar </h5><p>Online</p><a href="/events/postgraduate-educational-studies-information-webinar"> Postgraduate educational studies information webinar </a><p>3 November </p><h5> Postgraduate educational studies information webinar </h5><p>Online</p> <p><a href="/stories">See all stories</a></p> <a href="/stories/education-without-borders-claudias-vision-inclusive-education-starts-uq"> Education without borders: Claudia’s vision for inclusive education starts at UQ </a><p>UQ people</p><h5> Education without borders: Claudia’s vision for inclusive education starts at UQ </h5><p>2-minute read</p><a href="/stories/alternative-careers-education"> Considering a career change from teaching? </a><p>Careers</p><h5> Considering a career change from teaching? </h5><p>5-minute read</p><a href="/stories/why-study-education-uq"> Why study education at UQ? </a><p>Study tips</p><h5> Why study education at UQ? </h5><p>4-minute read</p>',
    total_course_duration = '',
    offshore_tuition_fee = 24040,
    onshore_tuition_fee = 2520,
    enrolment_fee = NULL,
    materials_fee = NULL,
    entry_requirements = '<h4>Entry Requirements</h4> <h5>Entry requirements</h5> <p>To be eligible for entry, you''ll need:</p> <ul><li>a bachelor''s degree (or equivalent) in any discipline, or</li><li>have completed post-secondary study, plus 2 years full-time professional work experience in a relevant or comparable education setting (see below).</li></ul><br/> You must have a grade point average (GPA) of 4.0 on a 7-point scale in your previous qualification. <p> <h5> GPA equivalent </h5> </p> <p>Select where you studied and your qualification to see the GPA equivalent you need to be considered for this program.</p><p>Use the GPA equivalent as a guide. When you apply, we’ll calculate your GPA using the UQ grading scale. Any failing grades will be included. Entry requirements are subject to change.</p> <h5>Equivalent subjects</h5> <table><thead><tr><th>Subject</th><th>Qualification equivalent</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table><p> <h5> Related programs </h5> </p> <p>Depending on your previous qualifications and current goals, you might want to consider<br/> one of these related programs:</p><ul><li><a href="/study-options/programs/master-educational-studies-5596">Master of Educational Studies</a></li></ul> <p> <h5> English language requirements </h5> </p> <p>IELTS overall 6.5; reading 6; writing 6; speaking 6; listening 6. For other English Language Proficiency Tests and Scores approved for UQ</p><p>TOEFL iBT (including Paper Edition) - Overall 87, listening 19, reading 19, writing 21 and speaking 19.</p><p>PTE Academic - Overall Score of 64 and 60 in all sub bands.</p><p>BE - A minimum overall grade of 4 plus a minimum grade of C in all macro skills.</p><p>CES - Overall 176 and 169 in all sub bands.</p><p>OET is not accepted.</p><p>There are other ways to meet the English language requirements. For some programs, additional conditions apply.</p><p><a href="/admissions/english-language-requirements">Learn how to meet the English language requirements</a></p> <p> <h5> Student visas </h5> </p> <p>International students who are accepted into full-time study in the Graduate Certificate in Educational Studies are eligible to apply for an Australian student visa (subclass 500).</p><p>There are a number of requirements you must satisfy before a visa is granted, including the Genuine Student (GS) requirement.</p><p><a href="/university-life/getting-prepared-to-come-to-australia/student-visas">Learn more about student visas</a></p> <p> <h5> Additional application information </h5> </p> <p> Relevant work experience is defined as employment in teaching and education (which can include youth work, teacher aide work, support personnel, music education, teaching English as a second language, allied health, and sport sciences). </p>',
    apply_form = 'https://study.uq.edu.au/study-options/programs/graduate-certificate-educational-studies-5448',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '061819G';

UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Overview</h4> <p> Strengthen your leadership expertise and get a professional advantage in your chosen area of education. </p><p>This program prepares you for a variety of employment opportunities in educational environments.</p><p>Choose a specialisation that will help you deepen your impact—whether supporting diverse learners, shaping curriculum, guiding student pathways, or contributing to evidence-based teaching practice.</p><p>You can specialise in one of 7 fields of study:</p><ul><li>Behaviour Support</li><li>Curriculum</li><li>Guidance, Counselling and Careers</li><li>Leadership</li><li>Psychology Education</li><li>Science of Learning; or</li><li>Inclusive Education.</li></ul><p>Depending on your area of specialisation (and which of over 50 courses you select), you can choose to complete all aspects of a practicum that focuses on advanced research and teaching interests.</p><p>Some pathways offer specific qualifications, while others offer significant professional advantage to educators interested in career advancement or broadening their career options.</p><p>UQ’s School of Education has prepared teachers for the world’s classrooms, industry, media and community leadership for 80 years, with programs and academics that lead the field.</p><p><a href="#tab1">Domestic</a><a href="#tab2">International</a></p><p><a href="#entry-requirements">See full entry requirements</a></p><p>LocationExternal, St LuciaDuration 1 Year full-time (or part-time equivalent) 1.5 Years full-time (or part-time equivalent) 2 Years full-time (or part-time equivalent) Start SemesterSemester 1 (22 Feb, 2027), Semester 2 (26 Jul, 2027)Program Code5596AQFLevel 9</p><p><a href="#fees-scholarships">Scholarships available</a></p><p><a href="#entry-requirements">See full entry requirements</a></p><p>LocationExternal, St LuciaFees<a href="#fees-scholarships">A$48080</a>Duration 1 Year full-time (only available as full-time study) 1.5 Years full-time (only available as full-time study) 2 Years full-time (only available as full-time study) Start Semester Semester 1 (22 Feb, 2027), Semester 2 (26 Jul, 2027) Semester dates for 2028 are yet to be confirmed Program Code5596CRICOS Code082608MAQFLevel 9</p><p><a href="#fees-scholarships">Scholarships available</a></p> <p> <h5> Program highlights </h5> </p> <p> <h5> Program highlights </h5> </p> <ul><li>Strengthen your leadership expertise in educational practice, policy and theory.</li><li>Obtain the knowledge and skills required for specialised fields of work.</li><li>Gain qualifications that enhance career advancement and options.</li><li>Improve your research skills by engaging in an extended research-based project.</li></ul> <p>41 in the world for education</p><p>QS World University Rankings 2026</p> <p>1 in Queensland for education and training</p><p>QS World University Rankings 2026</p> <p> <h5> Fields of study </h5> </p> <p>Tailor your studies to suit your goals. This program offers these options:</p><ul><li><p>Behaviour Support</p></li><li><p>Curriculum</p></li><li><p>Guidance, Counselling and Careers</p></li><li><p>Inclusive Education</p></li></ul><p><a href="#majors">See all fields of study</a></p> <p> <h5> How you''ll learn </h5> </p> <p>Your learning experiences are designed to best suit the learning outcomes of the courses you choose.</p><ul><li>Lectures</li><li>Tutorials</li><li>Work placements</li><li>Overseas study</li><li>Research experience</li><li>Fieldwork</li><li>Seminars</li></ul> <p> <h5> Placements and work experience </h5> </p> <p> Students studying Guidance, Counselling and Careers Field of Study may choose to complete EDUC7073 Practicum in Guidance, Counselling and Careers that involves approximately 50 contact hours of practicum experience. Enrolment in this practicum course is restricted to students who are registered teachers with the Queensland College of Teachers (QCT), and holders of a current Blue Card (Working with Children Check) or Exemption Card. Students can apply for a Blue Card or Exemption Card through the School of Education and should do so three months before their practicum is due to commence. Students may incur costs associated with the practicum (e.g. travel, parking, stationery). Enrolment in a practicum course may extend the length of the program. For further information please contact the School of Education. </p> <p> <h5> What you''ll study </h5> </p> <p>At UQ, degrees are called ''programs'' and subjects are called ''courses''. Here''s a sample of the courses you could study in this program:</p><ul><li>Educational Research Methods [Core course]</li><li>"Globalisation, Educational Policy and Change [Elective]</li><li>Introduction to Educational Studies</li><li>Global Indigenous Knowledge and Education</li><li>Mediation and Conflict Management [Elective]</li></ul><p><a href="https://programs-courses.uq.edu.au/requirements/program/5596/2027">See courses and program structure</a></p> <p> <h5> Career possibilities </h5> </p> <p>Postgraduate study can take you anywhere. Depending on which field you choose, here are some of the careers you could be on your way to:</p><ul><li>Behaviour management counsellor</li><li>Special needs teacher</li><li>Curriculum planner</li><li>School curriculum adviser</li><li>Career development practitioner</li><li>Guidance counsellor</li><li>School principal</li><li>Educational administrator</li><li>School counsellor</li><li>Multicultural teacher</li></ul> <p>Average annual salary range</p><h5>School Principal</h5>$150–$160K<p>seek.com.au</p> <p> <h5> Next steps after graduation </h5> </p> <p>As a graduate of the Master of Educational Studies, you’ll be well placed to advance your career across a range of educational settings, from schools and training organisations, to policy, leadership and specialist support roles.</p><p>Graduates often move into positions with greater responsibility, including leadership, advisory, or program development roles within their field of expertise.</p><p>If you wish to continue building your expertise and influence in education, the program also provides a platform for further professional development or research.</p> <p> <h5> Professional registration </h5> </p> <p>When you graduate, you may be eligible for registration with the following professional organisations. Contact the organisation to find out how to register.</p><ul><li>Australian Counselling Association</li><li>Queensland Guidance And Counselling Association</li></ul> <p>The Master of Educational Studies at UQ was one of the highlights of my entire career. I learnt to write, develop my opinions, and engage in stimulating research projects. </p><p> Susan Garson </p><p> Graduate, Master of Educational Studies </p><p>What really stands out from my time studying at UQ were the people and the relationships you formed. It was...an education in life itself, preparing your mind and character to lead and impact on the world in which you are a part for the rest of your life. </p><p> Philip Moulds </p><p> Graduate, Master of Educational Studies </p><p>My studies equipped me with the thinking, skills and confidence to thoughtfully navigate evolving educational landscapes, and to build a career grounded in teaching as intellectual, ethical work that makes a real difference in students’ lives.</p><p> Ryan Anspach </p><p> Graduate, Bachelors of Arts / Education (Secondary), Master of Educational Studies </p> <p><a href="/events">See all events</a></p> <a href="/events/uq-open-day"> UQ Open Day </a><p>2 August </p><h5> UQ Open Day </h5><p>St Lucia</p><a href="/events/master-teaching-information-webinar"> Master of Teaching information webinar </a><p>20 October </p><h5> Master of Teaching information webinar </h5><p>Online</p><a href="/events/postgraduate-educational-studies-information-webinar"> Postgraduate educational studies information webinar </a><p>3 November </p><h5> Postgraduate educational studies information webinar </h5><p>Online</p> <p><a href="/stories">See all stories</a></p> <a href="/stories/education-without-borders-claudias-vision-inclusive-education-starts-uq"> Education without borders: Claudia’s vision for inclusive education starts at UQ </a><p>UQ people</p><h5> Education without borders: Claudia’s vision for inclusive education starts at UQ </h5><p>2-minute read</p><a href="/stories/alternative-careers-education"> Considering a career change from teaching? </a><p>Careers</p><h5> Considering a career change from teaching? </h5><p>5-minute read</p><a href="/stories/why-study-education-uq"> Why study education at UQ? </a><p>Study tips</p><h5> Why study education at UQ? </h5><p>4-minute read</p>',
    total_course_duration = '1 Year full-time (or part-time equivalent) 1.5 Years full-time (or part-time equivalent) 2 Years full-time (or part-time equivalent)',
