UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Overview</h4> <p> This dual program enables you to choose a core engineering specialisation while learning a language alongside your engineering studies. </p><p>The Bachelor of Engineering (Honours) prepares you for a career addressing some of the key challenges of the 21st century, such as water resources, infrastructure and communication, food and health services supply, and sustainable energy development.<br/><br/>The Diploma in Languages component enables you to specialise in one language major or 2 language minors, providing a distinctive edge in the global engineering environment where demand for language and cultural capabilities is increasing.<br/><br/>This dual program enables you to choose a core engineering specialisation, with the opportunity to complement your engineering specialisation with a major or minor in one of the new and emerging areas of engineering, while learning a language alongside your engineering studies in each semester.<br/><br/>Graduates emerge as versatile, globally minded professional engineers ready to excel in diverse landscapes thanks to the expanded range of transferable skills delivered by this combination of study areas.</p><p><a href="#tab1">Domestic</a><a href="#tab2">International</a></p><p><a href="#entry-requirements">See full entry requirements</a></p>LocationSt LuciaDuration 5 Years (or part time equivalent)Start SemesterSemester 1 (22 Feb, 2027), Semester 2 (26 Jul, 2027)QTAC Code<p>717801</p>Program Code2544AQFLevel 8<p><a href="#how-to-apply">Admission schemes available</a></p><p><a href="#fees-scholarships">Scholarships available</a></p><p><a href="#entry-requirements">See full entry requirements</a></p>LocationSt LuciaFees<a href="#fees-scholarships">A$58376</a>Duration 5 Years Start Semester Semester 1 (22 Feb, 2027), Semester 2 (26 Jul, 2027) Semester dates for 2028 are yet to be confirmed QTAC Code<p>717801</p>Program Code2544CRICOS Code117053DAQFLevel 8<p><a href="#fees-scholarships">Scholarships available</a></p> <p> <h5> Program highlights </h5> </p> <p> <h5> Program highlights </h5> </p> <ul><li>More study options for greater career opportunities. UQ is home to the largest number of engineering study options in Queensland, with 6 core specialisations, 12 majors and 3 minors to choose from.</li><li>Study one language course per semester alongside engineering courses.</li><li>Benefit from a program designed in collaboration with your future employers and gain hands-on experience from day one, with industry contact and projects embedded throughout your studies.</li><li>Enhance your international employability and develop language and cultural skills to set you up for a global career.</li></ul> <p>1 in Queensland for engineering</p><p>Times Higher Education World University Rankings 2026</p> <p>1 in Queensland for modern languages</p><p>QS World University Rankings 2026</p> <p> <h5> Majors </h5> </p> <p>Tailor your studies to suit your goals. This program offers these options:</p><ul><li><p>Aerospace Engineering</p></li><li><p>Ancient Greek</p></li><li><p>Ancient Greek</p></li><li><p>Artificial Intelligence</p></li></ul><p><a href="#majors">See all majors</a></p> <p> <h5> How you''ll learn </h5> </p> <p>Your learning experiences are designed to best suit the learning outcomes of the courses you choose.</p><ul><li>Lectures</li><li>Tutorials</li><li>Work placements</li><li>Online study</li><li>Overseas study</li><li>Research experience</li><li>Laboratory work</li><li>Fieldwork</li></ul> <p> <h5> What you''ll study </h5> </p> <p>At UQ, degrees are called ''programs'' and subjects are called ''courses''.</p><p><a href="https://programs-courses.uq.edu.au/requirements/program/2544/2027">See courses and program structure</a></p><p><a href="https://www.uq.edu.au/study/docs/dual-degree-planners-2027/2027-Bachelor-of-Engineering-Honours-Diploma-in-Languages-2544.pdf">View dual degree planner (PDF)</a></p> <p> <h5> Career possibilities </h5> </p> <p>Our programs prepare you for your first job and beyond. Depending on which major you choose, here are some of the careers you could be on your way to:</p><ul><li>Chemical engineer</li><li>Civil engineer</li><li>Mechanical engineer</li><li>Mechatronic engineer</li><li>Electrical engineer</li><li>Software engineer</li></ul> <p>Average annual salary range</p><h5>Electrical Engineer</h5>$105–$125K<p>seek.com.au</p> <p> <h5> Professional memberships </h5> </p> <p>When you graduate, you may be eligible for memberships with the following professional organisations. Contact the organisation to find out how to become a member.</p><ul><li>Australian Computer Society</li><li>Australasian Institute of Mining and Metallurgy</li><li>Engineers Australia</li><li>Institution of Chemical Engineers</li></ul> <p> <h5> Program accreditation </h5> </p> <p>The Bachelor of Engineering (Honours) / Diploma in Languages is accredited by:</p><ul><li>Engineers Australia</li></ul> <p><a href="/events">See all events</a></p> <a href="/events/ancient-history-experience-day"> Ancient History Experience Day </a><p>15 July </p><h5> Ancient History Experience Day </h5><p>St Lucia</p><a href="/events/world-religions-experience-day-2026"> World Religions Experience Day 2026 </a><p>22 July - 23 July </p><h5> World Religions Experience Day 2026 </h5><p>St Lucia</p><a href="/events/uq-open-day"> UQ Open Day </a><p>2 August </p><h5> UQ Open Day </h5><p>St Lucia</p> <p><a href="/stories">See all stories</a></p> <a href="/stories/whats-it-really-study-engineering-uq"> What''s it really like to study engineering at UQ? </a><p>Uni life</p><h5> What''s it really like to study engineering at UQ? </h5><p>6-minute read</p><a href="/stories/phd-story-girish-hebbani"> Girish''s PhD story: the pursuit of pitstop perfection </a><p>UQ people</p><h5> Girish''s PhD story: the pursuit of pitstop perfection </h5><p>6-minute read</p><a href="/stories/studying-postgraduate-mining-resource-development"> What’s it like to study resource development (mining) as a postgraduate? </a><p>Uni life</p><h5> What’s it like to study resource development (mining) as a postgraduate? </h5><p>6-minute read</p>',
