UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Overview</h4> <p> Enhance your engineering expertise with advanced mathematics skills, creating a solid foundation for both research opportunities and a versatile career. </p><p>This dual degree program allows you to apply advanced mathematical principles to engineering while also preparing you for a research-focused honours degree in mathematics.</p><p>Over 5 years, you’ll earn a Bachelor of Engineering (Honours) alongside a selection of mathematics courses. You can specialise in areas such as Mathematical Artificial Intelligence or Optimisation and Operations Research, equipping you to tackle complex challenges in engineering and other industries.</p><p>Graduating with this dual qualification gives you a strong competitive edge in engineering, whether you''re working in infrastructure, healthcare, energy, or software development. Your mathematics studies will enhance your engineering expertise and offer opportunities for advanced research, including honours in mathematics.</p><p>With Queensland’s most comprehensive range of engineering disciplines, including chemical, civil, electrical, mechanical, mechatronic and software engineering, you''ll have the flexibility to complement your specialisation with emerging fields.</p><p>Upon completion, you’ll be equipped with the knowledge and skills to excel in the competitive job market, holding 2 respected qualifications that open doors to a wide range of career paths.</p><p><a href="#tab1">Domestic</a><a href="#tab2">International</a></p><p><a href="#entry-requirements">See full entry requirements</a></p>LocationSt LuciaDuration 5 Years (or part time equivalent)Start SemesterSemester 1 (22 Feb, 2027), Semester 2 (26 Jul, 2027)QTAC Code<p>717901</p>Program Code2492AQFLevel 8<p><a href="#how-to-apply">Admission schemes available</a></p><p><a href="#fees-scholarships">Scholarships available</a></p><p><a href="#entry-requirements">See full entry requirements</a></p>LocationSt LuciaFees<a href="#fees-scholarships">A$60952</a>Duration 5 Years Start Semester Semester 1 (22 Feb, 2027), Semester 2 (26 Jul, 2027) Semester dates for 2028 are yet to be confirmed QTAC Code<p>717901</p>Program Code2492CRICOS Code088353CAQFLevel 8<p><a href="#fees-scholarships">Scholarships available</a></p> <p> <h5> Program highlights </h5> </p> <p> <h5> Program highlights </h5> </p> <ul><li>UQ is home to the largest number of engineering study options in Queensland.</li><li>Graduate with 2 qualifications, boosting your skills and opening pathways to research.</li><li>Benefit from programs designed in collaboration with your future employers and gain hands-on experience from day one, with industry contact and projects embedded throughout your studies.</li></ul> <p>1 in Queensland for mathematics</p><p>QS World University Rankings 2026</p> <p>1 in Queensland for engineering and technology</p><p>QS World University Rankings 2026</p> <p> <h5> Majors </h5> </p> <p>Tailor your studies to suit your goals. This program offers these options:</p><ul><li><p>Aerospace Engineering</p></li><li><p>Applied Mathematics</p></li><li><p>Artificial Intelligence</p></li><li><p>Biomedical Engineering</p></li></ul><p><a href="#majors">See all majors</a></p> <p> <h5> How you''ll learn </h5> </p> <p>Your learning experiences are designed to best suit the learning outcomes of the courses you choose.</p><ul><li>Lectures</li><li>Tutorials</li><li>Work placements</li><li>Fieldwork</li><li>Seminars</li></ul> <p> <h5> What you''ll study </h5> </p> <p>At UQ, degrees are called ''programs'' and subjects are called ''courses''.</p><p><a href="https://programs-courses.uq.edu.au/requirements/program/2492/2027">See courses and program structure</a></p><p><a href="https://www.uq.edu.au/study/docs/dual-degree-planners-2027/2027-Bachelors-of-Engineering-Honours-Mathematics-2492.pdf">View dual degree planner (PDF)</a></p> <p> <h5> Career possibilities </h5> </p> <p>Our programs prepare you for your first job and beyond. Depending on which major you choose, here are some of the careers you could be on your way to:</p><ul><li>Chemical engineer</li><li>Civil engineer</li><li>Environmental engineer</li><li>Electrical engineer</li><li>Aerospace engineer</li><li>Mechanical engineer</li><li>Mechatronic engineer</li><li>Mining engineer</li><li>Software engineer</li></ul> <p>Average annual salary range</p><h5>Mining Engineer</h5>$145–$165K<p>seek.com.au</p><p>Average annual salary range</p><h5>Software Engineer</h5>$105–$125K<p>seek.com.au</p> <p> <h5> Program accreditation </h5> </p> <p>The Bachelors of Engineering (Honours) / Mathematics is accredited by:</p><ul><li>Engineers Australia</li></ul> <p>All through high school, I loved maths and physics, but I also really liked engaging with people, and working in teams. I knew I wanted to work in a role that worked with practical, real world problems. Engineering was the perfect combination of all these things!</p><p> Jennifer Ross </p><p> Graduate, Bachelor of Engineering (Honours) (Chemical) / Bachelor of Mathematics </p> <p><a href="/events">See all events</a></p> <a href="/events/uq-open-day"> UQ Open Day </a><p>2 August </p><h5> UQ Open Day </h5><p>St Lucia</p> <p><a href="/stories">See all stories</a></p> <a href="/stories/why-study-mathematics-uq"> Why study mathematics at UQ? </a><p>Study tips</p><h5> Why study mathematics at UQ? </h5><p>5-minute read</p><a href="/stories/why-study-engineering-uq"> Why study engineering at UQ? </a><p>Study tips</p><h5> Why study engineering at UQ? </h5><p>5-minute read</p><a href="/stories/beyond-scholarships-support-youll-receive-uq"> Beyond scholarships: the support you’ll receive at UQ </a><p>Uni life</p><h5> Beyond scholarships: the support you’ll receive at UQ </h5><p>5-minute read</p>',
