UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Overview</h4> <p> Interested in strengthening your capacity to design, develop, and implement complex systems and engineering projects? This program offers flexibility across a range of engineering disciplines, so you can develop your technical expertise in areas specific to your career aspirations. </p><p>The Graduate Certificate in Engineering Science is designed for applicants with a background in engineering.</p><p>Your future is in industry – as a professional engineer with deeper technical skills in your engineering field.</p><p><a href="#tab1">Domestic</a><a href="#tab2">International</a></p><p><a href="#entry-requirements">See full entry requirements</a></p><p>LocationSt LuciaDuration Half Year (or part time equivalent)Start SemesterSemester 1 (22 Feb, 2027), Semester 2 (26 Jul, 2027)Program Code5527AQFLevel 8</p><p><a href="#fees-scholarships">Scholarships available</a></p><p><a href="#entry-requirements">See full entry requirements</a></p><p>LocationSt LuciaFees<a href="#fees-scholarships">A$30476</a>Duration Half Year Start Semester Semester 1 (22 Feb, 2027), Semester 2 (26 Jul, 2027) Semester dates for 2028 are yet to be confirmed Program Code5527CRICOS Code075745EAQFLevel 8</p><p><a href="#fees-scholarships">Scholarships available</a></p> <p> <h5> Program highlights </h5> </p> <p> <h5> Program highlights </h5> </p> <ul><li>Benefit from a program that offers a flexible study plan. Tailor your studies to suit your interests, your industry, or your career goals.</li><li>Students will develop professional engineering skills and technical expertise in their discipline through advanced and master''s level courses. You''ll graduate with the skills required to solve complex engineering challenges in a changing world.</li><li>Undertake a supervised research project relevant to your engineering field. You''ll be expected to systematically plan and manage all aspects of your project, and to clearly explain your findings and what they contribute to your field.</li></ul> <p>5 in the world for mineral and mining engineering</p><p>QS World University Rankings 2026</p> <p>1 in Queensland for engineering and technology</p><p>QS World University Rankings 2026</p> <p> <h5> Fields of study </h5> </p> <p>Tailor your studies to suit your goals. This program offers these options:</p><ul><li><p>Bioprocess Engineering</p></li><li><p>Chemical Engineering</p></li><li><p>Civil Engineering</p></li><li><p>Electrical Engineering</p></li></ul><p><a href="#majors">See all fields of study</a></p> <p> <h5> How you''ll learn </h5> </p> <p>Your learning experiences are designed to best suit the learning outcomes of the courses you choose.</p><ul><li>Lectures</li><li>Tutorials</li><li>Research experience</li><li>Laboratory work</li><li>Fieldwork</li></ul> <p> <h5> What you''ll study </h5> </p> <p>At UQ, degrees are called ''programs'' and subjects are called ''courses''.</p><p><a href="https://programs-courses.uq.edu.au/requirements/program/5527/2027">See courses and program structure</a></p> <p>Graduate salary</p><h5>Engineering (postgraduate)</h5>$89K–$120K<p>compared.edu.au</p> <p>If you like to embrace challenge, become a professional with overall development in leadership, communication, planning, technical expertise, increasing your research capabilities and employability skills then UQ is the perfect place to study. </p><p> Sushil Eswara Subramanian </p><p> Graduate, Master of Engineering Science </p> <p><a href="/events">See all events</a></p> <a href="/events/uq-open-day"> UQ Open Day </a><p>2 August </p><h5> UQ Open Day </h5><p>St Lucia</p> <p><a href="/stories">See all stories</a></p> <a href="/stories/phd-story-girish-hebbani"> Girish''s PhD story: the pursuit of pitstop perfection </a><p>UQ people</p><h5> Girish''s PhD story: the pursuit of pitstop perfection </h5><p>6-minute read</p><a href="/stories/studying-postgraduate-mining-resource-development"> What’s it like to study resource development (mining) as a postgraduate? </a><p>Uni life</p><h5> What’s it like to study resource development (mining) as a postgraduate? </h5><p>6-minute read</p><a href="/stories/firefighting-robots-rocket-science-vennkkatas-uq-experience"> From firefighting robots to rocket science: Vennkkata’s UQ experience </a><p>UQ people</p><h5> From firefighting robots to rocket science: Vennkkata’s UQ experience </h5><p>5-minute read</p>',
