UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Overview</h4> <p> Develop the advanced analytical skills and industry-relevant expertise needed to tackle complex financial challenges and drive innovation in a rapidly evolving global economy. </p><p>Delve into topics like financial contract pricing, portfolio management, capital adequacy, firm valuation, and optimal capital and contract management.</p><p>This one-year full-time program offers a diverse range of courses tailored to your field, allowing you to customise your studies to align with your interests and career goals.</p><p>Boost your career prospects with roles in investment banks, corporate risk units, insurance firms, fund managers, regulatory bodies and trading companies.</p><p><a href="#tab1">Domestic</a><a href="#tab2">International</a></p><p><a href="#entry-requirements">See full entry requirements</a></p><p>LocationSt LuciaDuration 1 Year full-time (or part-time equivalent) Start SemesterSemester 1 (22 Feb, 2027), Semester 2 (26 Jul, 2027)Program Code5734AQFLevel 8</p><p><a href="#fees-scholarships">Scholarships available</a></p><p><a href="#entry-requirements">See full entry requirements</a></p><p>LocationSt LuciaFees<a href="#fees-scholarships">A$56800</a>Duration 1 Year full-time Start Semester Semester 1 (22 Feb, 2027), Semester 2 (26 Jul, 2027) Semester dates for 2028 are yet to be confirmed Program Code5734CRICOS Code105700KAQFLevel 8</p><p><a href="#fees-scholarships">Scholarships available</a></p> <p> <h5> Program highlights </h5> </p> <p> <h5> Program highlights </h5> </p> <ul><li>Enhance your foundation in mathematics, commerce, or economics/econometrics.</li><li>Customise your studies with a choice of 22 courses to suit your goals.</li><li>Master advanced computational, mathematical and stochastic finance methods to identify opportunities, manage portfolios and price financial products.</li></ul> <p>1 in Queensland for accounting and finance</p><p>QS World University Rankings 2026</p> <p>1 in Queensland for mathematics</p><p>QS World University Rankings 2026</p> <p> <h5> How you''ll learn </h5> </p> <p>Your learning experiences are designed to best suit the learning outcomes of the courses you choose.</p><ul><li>Lectures</li><li>Tutorials</li><li>Online study</li></ul> <p> <h5> What you''ll study </h5> </p> <p>At UQ, degrees are called ''programs'' and subjects are called ''courses''. Here''s a sample of the courses you could study in this program:</p><ul><li>Financial Calculus [Core course] </li><li>Computation in Financial Mathematics [Core course] </li><li>Corporate Finance [Elective]</li><li>Applied Econometrics for Macroeconomics and Finance [Elective]</li><li>Portfolio Management [Elective]</li><li>Scientific Computing: Advanced Techniques and Applications [Elective]</li><li>Optimisation Theory [Elective]</li></ul><p><a href="https://programs-courses.uq.edu.au/requirements/program/5734/2027">See courses and program structure</a></p> <p> <h5> Career possibilities </h5> </p> <p>Postgraduate study can take you anywhere. Here are some of the careers you could be on your way to:</p><ul><li>Investment banker</li><li>Retail banker</li><li>Market risk manager</li><li>Data scientist</li><li>Financial planning manager</li><li>Stockbroker</li><li>Financial product developer</li><li>Credit risk analyst</li><li>Business intelligence manager</li><li>Funds manager</li></ul> <p>Annual average salary range</p><h5>Financial Analyst</h5>$100–$120K<p>seek.com.au</p><p>Average annual salary range</p><h5>Business Analyst</h5>$110–$130K<p>seek.com.au</p> <p> <h5> Next steps after graduation </h5> </p> <p>Completing this program can pave the way to UQ’s <a href="/study-options/programs/master-financial-mathematics-5573?year=2027">Master of Financial Mathematics</a>.</p><p><a href="http://career-profiles.science.uq.edu.au/">Find out more about careers that started in science</a></p> <p>I was provided with so many great opportunities to gain comprehensive professional industry experiences.</p><p> April Zhang </p><p> Master of Financial Mathematics </p> <p><a href="/events">See all events</a></p> <a href="/events/uq-open-day"> UQ Open Day </a><p>2 August </p><h5> UQ Open Day </h5><p>St Lucia</p> <p><a href="/stories">See all stories</a></p> <a href="/stories/why-study-mathematics-uq"> Why study mathematics at UQ? </a><p>Study tips</p><h5> Why study mathematics at UQ? </h5><p>5-minute read</p><a href="/stories/there-limit-challenges-we-can-solve-maths"> Making the greatest mathematical discoveries </a><p>UQ people</p><h5> Making the greatest mathematical discoveries </h5><p>3-minute read</p><a href="/stories/enduring-value-commerce-degree"> The enduring value of a commerce degree </a><p>Careers</p><h5> The enduring value of a commerce degree </h5><p>5-minute read</p>',
    total_course_duration = '1 Year full-time (or part-time equivalent)',
    offshore_tuition_fee = 56800,
    onshore_tuition_fee = 9175,
    enrolment_fee = NULL,
    materials_fee = NULL,
    entry_requirements = '<h4>Entry Requirements</h4> <h5>Entry requirements</h5> <p>To be eligible for entry, you''ll need:</p> <ul><li>a bachelor''s degree (or equivalent) in any discipline with first-year, university-level mathematics (including single-variable and multi-variable calculus, ordinary differential equations, and linear algebra), or</li><li>5 years of full-time equivalent, relevant work experience in data science, financial mathematics, mathematics, engineering or information technology.</li></ul><br/>You must have a grade point average (GPA) of 4.5 on a 7-point scale in your previous qualification. <p> <h5> GPA equivalent </h5> </p> <p>Select where you studied and your qualification to see the GPA equivalent you need to be considered for this program.</p><p>Use the GPA equivalent as a guide. When you apply, we’ll calculate your GPA using the UQ grading scale. Any failing grades will be included. Entry requirements are subject to change.</p> <h5>Equivalent subjects</h5> <table><thead><tr><th>Subject</th><th>Qualification equivalent</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table><p> <h5> Related programs </h5> </p> <p>Depending on your previous qualifications and current goals, you might want to consider<br/> one of these related programs:</p><ul><li><a href="/study-options/programs/master-financial-mathematics-5573">Master of Financial Mathematics</a></li></ul> <p> <h5> English language requirements </h5> </p> <p>IELTS overall 6.5; reading 6; writing 6; speaking 6; listening 6. For other English Language Proficiency Tests and Scores approved for UQ</p><p>TOEFL iBT (including Paper Edition) - Overall 87, listening 19, reading 19, writing 21 and speaking 19.</p><p>PTE Academic - Overall Score of 64 and 60 in all sub bands.</p><p>BE - A minimum overall grade of 4 plus a minimum grade of C in all macro skills.</p><p>CES - Overall 176 and 169 in all sub bands.</p><p>OET is not accepted.</p><p>There are other ways to meet the English language requirements. For some programs, additional conditions apply.</p><p><a href="/admissions/english-language-requirements">Learn how to meet the English language requirements</a></p> <p> <h5> Student visas </h5> </p> <p>International students who are accepted into full-time study in the Graduate Diploma in Financial Mathematics are eligible to apply for an Australian student visa (subclass 500).</p><p>There are a number of requirements you must satisfy before a visa is granted, including the Genuine Student (GS) requirement.</p><p><a href="/university-life/getting-prepared-to-come-to-australia/student-visas">Learn more about student visas</a></p>',
    apply_form = 'https://study.uq.edu.au/study-options/programs/graduate-diploma-financial-mathematics-5734',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '105700K';

UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Overview</h4> <p> Develop the advanced analytical skills and industry-relevant expertise needed to tackle complex financial challenges and drive innovation in a rapidly evolving global economy. </p><p>You''ll explore topics such as financial contract pricing, investment portfolio management, capital adequacy, firm valuation, and optimal capital and contract management.</p><p>Choose from a diverse range of courses tailored to your field, allowing you to customise your studies to align with your interests and career goals.</p><p>Gain real-world experience through a research project at UQ or in industry, working in sectors like banking, energy trading or superannuation.</p><p><a href="#tab1">Domestic</a><a href="#tab2">International</a></p><p><a href="#entry-requirements">See full entry requirements</a></p><p>LocationSt LuciaDuration 1.5 Years full-time (or part-time equivalent) 2 Years full-time (or part-time equivalent) Start SemesterSemester 1 (22 Feb, 2027), Semester 2 (26 Jul, 2027)Program Code5573AQFLevel 9</p><p><a href="#fees-scholarships">Scholarships available</a></p><p><a href="#entry-requirements">See full entry requirements</a></p><p>LocationSt LuciaFees<a href="#fees-scholarships">A$56800</a>Duration 1.5 Years full-time (only available as full-time study) 2 Years full-time (only available as full-time study) Start Semester Semester 1 (22 Feb, 2027), Semester 2 (26 Jul, 2027) Semester dates for 2028 are yet to be confirmed Program Code5573CRICOS Code079389KAQFLevel 9</p><p><a href="#fees-scholarships">Scholarships available</a></p> <p> <h5> Program highlights </h5> </p> <p> <h5> Program highlights </h5> </p> <ul><li>Master advanced computational, mathematical and stochastic finance methods to identify opportunities, manage portfolios and price financial products.</li><li>Leverage UQ’s industry and government links, gaining hands-on financial market experience through placements.</li><li>Enhance your expertise in mathematics, commerce, or economics/econometrics.</li></ul> <p>3 in Australia for business and economics</p><p>Times Higher Education World University Rankings 2026</p> <p>1 in Queensland for mathematics</p><p>QS World University Rankings 2026</p> <p> <h5> How you''ll learn </h5> </p> <p>Your learning experiences are designed to best suit the learning outcomes of the courses you choose.</p><ul><li>Lectures</li><li>Tutorials</li><li>Work placements</li><li>Research experience</li></ul> <p> <h5> What you''ll study </h5> </p> <p>At UQ, degrees are called ''programs'' and subjects are called ''courses''. Here''s a sample of the courses you could study in this program:</p><ul><li>Computation in Financial Mathematics [Core course]</li><li>Financial Calculus [Core course]</li><li>Programming of Simulation, Analysis, &amp; Learning Systems [Elective]</li><li>Optimisation Theory [Elective]</li><li>Statistical Modelling &amp; Analysis [Elective]</li><li>Operations Research &amp; Mathematical Planning [Elective]</li><li>Machine Learning [Elective] </li></ul><p><a href="https://programs-courses.uq.edu.au/requirements/program/5573/2027">See courses and program structure</a></p> <p> <h5> Career possibilities </h5> </p> <p>Postgraduate study can take you anywhere. Here are some of the careers you could be on your way to:</p><ul><li>Investment banker</li><li>Retail banker</li><li>Market risk manager</li><li>Financial planning manager</li><li>Data scientist</li><li>Quantitative analyst</li><li>Financial product developer</li><li>Credit risk analyst</li><li>Revenue manager</li><li>Stockbroker</li></ul> <p>Annual average salary range</p><h5>Financial Analyst</h5>$100–$120K<p>seek.com.au</p><p>Annual average salary range</p><h5>Risk Manager</h5>$140–$160K<p>seek.com.au</p> <p> <h5> Next steps after graduation </h5> </p> <p>Graduates are highly sought after by investment banks, corporate risk units, insurance companies, fund managers, financial regulators and trading firms.</p><p><a href="http://career-profiles.science.uq.edu.au/">Find out more about careers that started in science</a></p> <p>I was fortunate to conduct my industry research project at Suncorp Group, where I applied the techniques I was learning in the classroom to develop machine-learning models to assess retail credit risk. UQ has lots of opportunities for students to meet and network. </p><p> April Zhang </p><p> Graduate, Master of Financial Mathematics </p> <p><a href="/events">See all events</a></p> <a href="/events/uq-open-day"> UQ Open Day </a><p>2 August </p><h5> UQ Open Day </h5><p>St Lucia</p> <p><a href="/stories">See all stories</a></p> <a href="/stories/there-limit-challenges-we-can-solve-maths"> Making the greatest mathematical discoveries </a><p>UQ people</p><h5> Making the greatest mathematical discoveries </h5><p>3-minute read</p><a href="/stories/why-study-mathematics-uq"> Why study mathematics at UQ? </a><p>Study tips</p><h5> Why study mathematics at UQ? </h5><p>5-minute read</p><a href="/stories/enduring-value-commerce-degree"> The enduring value of a commerce degree </a><p>Careers</p><h5> The enduring value of a commerce degree </h5><p>5-minute read</p>',
    total_course_duration = '1.5 Years full-time (or part-time equivalent) 2 Years full-time (or part-time equivalent)',
    offshore_tuition_fee = 85200,
    onshore_tuition_fee = 13762,
    enrolment_fee = NULL,
    materials_fee = NULL,
    entry_requirements = '<h4>Entry Requirements</h4> <h5>Entry requirements</h5> <p>It''s possible to complete this degree in 2 years or 1.5 years depending on your qualifications and experience.</p><p>You can apply for any duration as long as you meet the entry requirements. You may also be eligible to apply for <a href="/admissions/postgraduate-coursework/check-credit-eligibility">credit or exemptions</a> to shorten your degree further. You''ll graduate with the same qualification no matter how long you take to complete the degree.</p> <h5>2-year degree (32 units of study)</h5><p>To be eligible to complete the degree in 2 years full-time (only available as full-time study), you''ll need:</p><ul><li>a bachelor''s degree (or equivalent) in any discipline with first-year, university-level mathematics (including single-variable and multi-variable calculus, ordinary differential equations, and linear algebra), or</li><li>a graduate diploma (or equivalent) in financial mathematics, or</li><li>to have successfully completed 3 years of study towards an approved qualification at an overseas partner institution, with a formal pathway to the Master of Financial Mathematics.</li></ul><p>You must have a grade point average (GPA) of 5.0 on a 7-point scale in your previous qualification.</p><h5>1.5-year degree (24 units of study)</h5><p>If you have relevant prior learning or experience, you can reduce the number of courses you need to complete and graduate in less time.</p><p>To be eligible to complete the degree in 1.5 years full-time (only available as full-time study), you''ll need:</p><ul><li>a bachelor''s degree (or equivalent) in mathematics, or</li><li>a bachelor''s degree (or equivalent) majoring in mathematics, or</li><li>to have successfully completed 3.5 years of study towards an approved qualification at an overseas partner institution, including research requirements, with a formal pathway to the Master of Financial Mathematics.</li></ul><p>You must have a grade point average (GPA) of 5.0 on a 7-point scale in your previous qualification.</p> <p> <h5> GPA equivalent </h5> </p> <p>Select where you studied and your qualification to see the GPA equivalent you need to be considered for this program.</p><p>Use the GPA equivalent as a guide. When you apply, we’ll calculate your GPA using the UQ grading scale. Any failing grades will be included. Entry requirements are subject to change.</p> <h5>Equivalent subjects</h5> <table><thead><tr><th>Subject</th><th>Qualification equivalent</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table><p> <h5> Related programs </h5> </p> <p>Depending on your previous qualifications and current goals, you might want to consider<br/> one of these related programs:</p><ul><li><a href="/study-options/programs/graduate-diploma-financial-mathematics-5734">Graduate Diploma in Financial Mathematics</a></li></ul> <p> <h5> English language requirements </h5> </p> <p>IELTS overall 6.5; reading 6; writing 6; speaking 6; listening 6. For other English Language Proficiency Tests and Scores approved for UQ</p><p>TOEFL iBT (including Paper Edition) - Overall 87, listening 19, reading 19, writing 21 and speaking 19.</p><p>PTE Academic - Overall Score of 64 and 60 in all sub bands.</p><p>BE - A minimum overall grade of 4 plus a minimum grade of C in all macro skills.</p><p>CES - Overall 176 and 169 in all sub bands.</p><p>OET is not accepted.</p><p>There are other ways to meet the English language requirements. For some programs, additional conditions apply.</p><p><a href="/admissions/english-language-requirements">Learn how to meet the English language requirements</a></p> <p> <h5> Student visas </h5> </p> <p>International students who are accepted into full-time study in the Master of Financial Mathematics are eligible to apply for an Australian student visa (subclass 500).</p><p>There are a number of requirements you must satisfy before a visa is granted, including the Genuine Student (GS) requirement.</p><p><a href="/university-life/getting-prepared-to-come-to-australia/student-visas">Learn more about student visas</a></p>',
    apply_form = 'https://study.uq.edu.au/study-options/programs/master-financial-mathematics-5573',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '079389K';

UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Overview</h4> <p> Expand your career prospects in a rapidly advancing industry and be part of the solution to global challenges like food security, nutrition and sustainability. </p><p>UQ is a key research provider in food science and technology — our teachers are active researchers who share the latest knowledge in food safety and quality management, food chemistry and microbiology, food processing and new food product development.</p><p>This program is ideal for professionals seeking to expand their career prospects into a wide range of government, commercial, community-based or research roles in the broad field of food science and technology.</p><p>During your 6-month of full-time study (or part-time equivalent), you''ll develop theoretical and practical knowledge and skills to meet the many global challenges associated with feeding the world, maintaining our environment, biosecurity concerns, and competition for limited resources.</p><p>You''ll analyse critically, evaluate and transform information within the discipline, generate solutions to complex problems, and be able to communicate with professional and non-professional audiences.</p><p><a href="#tab1">Domestic</a><a href="#tab2">International</a></p><p><a href="#entry-requirements">See full entry requirements</a></p><p>LocationSt LuciaDuration Half Year (or part time equivalent)Start SemesterSemester 1 (22 Feb, 2027), Semester 2 (26 Jul, 2027)Program Code5566AQFLevel 8</p><p><a href="#fees-scholarships">Scholarships available</a></p><p><a href="#entry-requirements">See full entry requirements</a></p><p>LocationSt LuciaFees<a href="#fees-scholarships">A$30476</a>Duration Half Year Start Semester Semester 1 (22 Feb, 2027), Semester 2 (26 Jul, 2027) Semester dates for 2028 are yet to be confirmed Program Code5566CRICOS Code079378BAQFLevel 8</p><p><a href="#fees-scholarships">Scholarships available</a></p> <p> <h5> Program highlights </h5> </p> <p> <h5> Program highlights </h5> </p> <ul><li>Refine your laboratory skills during practicals and research courses.</li><li>Tailor your studies to your interests and career goals with specialised electives.</li><li>Enhance your professional standing in fields such as quality control, product development, research and innovation.</li><li>Access the Food Science Innovation Precinct – a world-class teaching, research, training and development unit.</li></ul> <p>2 in Australia for food science and technology</p><p>Global Ranking of Academic Subjects 2025</p> <p>28 in the world for food science and technology</p><p>Global Ranking of Academic Subjects 2025</p> <p> <h5> How you''ll learn </h5> </p> <p>Your learning experiences are designed to best suit the learning outcomes of the courses you choose.</p><ul><li>Lectures</li><li>Tutorials</li><li>Laboratory work</li></ul> <p> <h5> What you''ll study </h5> </p> <p>At UQ, degrees are called ''programs'' and subjects are called ''courses''. Here''s a sample of the courses you could study in this program:</p><ul><li>Food Sensory &amp; Physical Assessment [Core course]</li><li>Food Product Development [Core course] </li><li>Food Processing Technology [Core course]</li><li>Advanced Functional Foods [Core course]</li><li>Nutrition and Health [Core course]</li><li>Advanced Food Materials Science [Core course]</li><li>Food Microbiology &amp; Biotechnology [Core course]</li></ul><p><a href="https://programs-courses.uq.edu.au/requirements/program/5566/2027">See courses and program structure</a></p> <p> <h5> Career possibilities </h5> </p> <p>Postgraduate study can take you anywhere. Here are some of the careers you could be on your way to:</p><ul><li>Food technologist</li><li>Food chemist</li><li>Food microbiologist</li><li>Laboratory supervisor</li><li>Process and product development manager</li><li>Quality control manager</li><li>Food process engineer</li><li>Agribusiness consultant</li><li>Food security adviser</li><li>Sustainable food production specialist</li></ul> <p>Average annual salary range</p><h5>Food Technologist</h5>$75K–$90K<p>seek.com.au</p><p>Average annual salary range</p><h5>Quality Assurance Coordinator</h5>$85K–$90K<p>seek.com.au</p> <p> <h5> Next steps after graduation </h5> </p> <p>The food industry is Australia’s largest manufacturing sector and has unmet demand for highly qualified graduates.</p><p>As a graduate, you''ll be able to explain and demonstrate advanced theoretical and technical knowledge in food science and technology.</p><p><a href="http://career-profiles.science.uq.edu.au/">Find out more about careers that started in science</a></p> <p><a href="/events">See all events</a></p> <a href="/events/uq-open-day"> UQ Open Day </a><p>2 August </p><h5> UQ Open Day </h5><p>St Lucia</p> <p><a href="/stories">See all stories</a></p> <a href="/stories/food-science-careers"> Food science career paths </a><p>Careers</p><h5> Food science career paths </h5><p>3-minute read</p><a href="/stories/what-can-you-do-with-food-science-degree"> What can you do with a food science degree? </a><p>Careers</p><h5> What can you do with a food science degree? </h5><p>4-minute read</p><a href="/stories/food-science-programs-what-you-will-learn"> How to study food science at UQ </a><p>Study tips</p><h5> How to study food science at UQ </h5><p>5-minute read</p>',
    total_course_duration = '',
    offshore_tuition_fee = 30476,
    onshore_tuition_fee = 4765,
    enrolment_fee = NULL,
    materials_fee = NULL,
    entry_requirements = '<h4>Entry Requirements</h4> <h5>Entry requirements</h5> <p>To be eligible for entry, you''ll need:</p> <ul><li>a bachelor''s degree (or equivalent) in any discipline, with first-year, university-level chemistry or biology, or</li><li>2 years full-time equivalent, relevant work experience in food science, food technology or food engineering.</li></ul>You must have a grade point average (GPA) of 4.0 on a 7-point scale in your previous qualification. <p> <h5> GPA equivalent </h5> </p> <p>Select where you studied and your qualification to see the GPA equivalent you need to be considered for this program.</p><p>Use the GPA equivalent as a guide. When you apply, we’ll calculate your GPA using the UQ grading scale. Any failing grades will be included. Entry requirements are subject to change.</p> <h5>Equivalent subjects</h5> <table><thead><tr><th>Subject</th><th>Qualification equivalent</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table><p> <h5> Related programs </h5> </p> <p>Depending on your previous qualifications and current goals, you might want to consider<br/> one of these related programs:</p><ul><li><a href="/study-options/programs/master-food-science-and-technology-5576">Master of Food Science and Technology</a></li><li><a href="/study-options/programs/master-food-science-and-technology-research-extensive-5753">Master of Food Science and Technology Research Extensive</a></li></ul> <p> <h5> English language requirements </h5> </p> <p>IELTS overall 6.5; reading 6; writing 6; speaking 6; listening 6. For other English Language Proficiency Tests and Scores approved for UQ</p><p>TOEFL iBT (including Paper Edition) - Overall 87, listening 19, reading 19, writing 21 and speaking 19.</p><p>PTE Academic - Overall Score of 64 and 60 in all sub bands.</p><p>BE - A minimum overall grade of 4 plus a minimum grade of C in all macro skills.</p><p>CES - Overall 176 and 169 in all sub bands.</p><p>OET is not accepted.</p><p>There are other ways to meet the English language requirements. For some programs, additional conditions apply.</p><p><a href="/admissions/english-language-requirements">Learn how to meet the English language requirements</a></p> <p> <h5> Student visas </h5> </p> <p>International students who are accepted into full-time study in the Graduate Certificate in Food Science and Technology are eligible to apply for an Australian student visa (subclass 500).</p><p>There are a number of requirements you must satisfy before a visa is granted, including the Genuine Student (GS) requirement.</p><p><a href="/university-life/getting-prepared-to-come-to-australia/student-visas">Learn more about student visas</a></p>',
    apply_form = 'https://study.uq.edu.au/study-options/programs/graduate-certificate-food-science-and-technology-5566',
