UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Overview</h4> <p> Combine your passion for physical activity, sport, exercise and nutrition with business acumen in this dual program. </p><p>You''ll graduate with the knowledge to improve health outcomes, manage teams and create new opportunities in a rapidly growing field.</p><p>Develop the knowledge and skills to address 2 of the most important modifiable risk factors for chronic disease – physical activity and nutrition – while gaining a deep understanding of a broad range of concepts relevant across the business world. You''ll study topics including accounting, economics, leadership, marketing, business information systems and strategy.</p><p>Through the Human Movement and Nutrition Sciences program, you’ll explore human movement and nutrition across the lifespan. You''ll discover the roles that food, physical activity, exercise and sleep play in our health, the prevention of chronic disease and sporting performance. </p><p>During your business management studies, you''ll learn from industry guest lecturers and real-life case studies, with the opportunity to undertake projects and placements with leading businesses.</p><p>The dual degree provides a broad range of employment pathways, including entrepreneurship and sports management.</p><p><a href="#tab1">Domestic</a><a href="#tab2">International</a></p><p><a href="#entry-requirements">See full entry requirements</a></p>LocationSt LuciaDuration 4 Years (or part time equivalent)Start SemesterSemester 1 (22 Feb, 2027), Semester 2 (26 Jul, 2027)QTAC Code<p>720402</p>Program Code2527AQFLevel 7<p><a href="#how-to-apply">Admission schemes available</a></p><p><a href="#fees-scholarships">Scholarships available</a></p><p><a href="#entry-requirements">See full entry requirements</a></p>LocationSt LuciaFees<a href="#fees-scholarships">A$56800</a>Duration 4 Years Start Semester Semester 1 (22 Feb, 2027), Semester 2 (26 Jul, 2027) Semester dates for 2028 are yet to be confirmed QTAC Code<p>720402</p>Program Code2527CRICOS Code113793MAQFLevel 7<p><a href="#fees-scholarships">Scholarships available</a></p> <p> <h5> Program highlights </h5> </p> <p> <h5> Program highlights </h5> </p> <ul><li>Graduate career ready, having completed 50 hours of placements, gaining practical skills and business management techniques for the nutrition, sport and physical activity industries. </li><li>Join one of the world''s top business schools and learn from award-winning researchers and staff who are leaders in their fields.</li><li>Learn alongside a cohort of like-minded future health professionals at a world-leading university for sports-related subjects.</li><li>Tailor your studies to align with your interests and goals. Choose to specialise in one business major from 7 diverse options. </li></ul> <p>2 in the world for sports-related subjects</p><p>QS World University Rankings 2026</p> <p>1 in Queensland for business and management studies</p><p>QS World University Rankings 2026</p> <p> <h5> Majors </h5> </p> <p>Tailor your studies to suit your goals. This program offers these options:</p><ul><li><p>Business Economics</p></li><li><p>Business Information Systems</p></li><li><p>Human Resources</p></li><li><p>Innovation and Entrepreneurship</p></li></ul><p><a href="#majors">See all majors</a></p> <p> <h5> How you''ll learn </h5> </p> <p>Your learning experiences are designed to best suit the learning outcomes of the courses you choose.</p><ul><li>Lectures</li><li>Tutorials</li><li>Work placements</li><li>Online study</li><li>Research experience</li><li>Seminars</li><li>Studios</li><li>Workshops</li></ul> <p> <h5> Placements and work experience </h5> </p> <p> HMST3103 Nutrition, Sport and Physical Activity Management - Industry Placement has been developed to provide final year Human Movement and Nutrition Sciences students with hands-on experience in a related work environment. Students may be required to hold a current Blue Card (Working with Children Check). This is dependent on the requirements of their placement provider. <a href="https://my.uq.edu.au/information-and-services/manage-my-program/placements/hmbs">Learn more about placement requirements</a></p> <p> <h5> What you''ll study </h5> </p> <p>At UQ, degrees are called ''programs'' and subjects are called ''courses''.</p><p><a href="https://programs-courses.uq.edu.au/requirements/program/2527/2027">See courses and program structure</a></p><p><a href="https://www.uq.edu.au/study/docs/dual-degree-planners-2027/2027-Bachelors-of-Human-Movement-and-Nutrition-Sciences-Business-Management-2527.pdf">View dual degree planner (PDF)</a></p> <p> <h5> Career possibilities </h5> </p> <p>Our programs prepare you for your first job and beyond. Depending on which major you choose, here are some of the careers you could be on your way to:</p><ul><li>Business entrepreneur</li><li>Sports centre manager</li><li>Business development manager</li><li>Marketing manager</li></ul> <p>Average annual salary range</p><h5>Business Development Manager</h5>$105–$125K<p>seek.com.au</p> <p><a href="/events">See all events</a></p> <a href="/events/uq-open-day"> UQ Open Day </a><p>2 August </p><h5> UQ Open Day </h5><p>St Lucia</p><a href="/events/master-teaching-information-webinar"> Master of Teaching information webinar </a><p>20 October </p><h5> Master of Teaching information webinar </h5><p>Online</p><a href="/events/postgraduate-educational-studies-information-webinar"> Postgraduate educational studies information webinar </a><p>3 November </p><h5> Postgraduate educational studies information webinar </h5><p>Online</p> <p><a href="/stories">See all stories</a></p> <a href="/stories/what-can-you-do-bachelor-human-movement-and-nutrition-sciences"> What can you do with a Bachelor of Human Movement and Nutrition Sciences? </a><p>Careers</p><h5> What can you do with a Bachelor of Human Movement and Nutrition Sciences? </h5><p>7-minute read</p><a href="/stories/how-to-become-dietitian"> How to become a dietitian in Australia </a><p>Careers</p><h5> How to become a dietitian in Australia </h5><p>6-minute read</p><a href="/stories/why-study-business-uq"> Why study business at UQ? </a><p>Study tips</p><h5> Why study business at UQ? </h5><p>7-minute read</p>',
