p> <p>Graduates of the Master of Interaction Design have advanced understanding of usability problems and how to solve them. They also have diverse skills relevant to a range of industries, sectors and discipline areas.</p><p>Graduates typically work across the public and private sectors. Employers include technology companies, banking and financial services, digital agencies, media companies, government agencies, and health providers.</p> <p> <h5> Program accreditation </h5> </p> <p>The Master of Interaction Design is accredited by:</p><ul><li>Australian Computer Society</li></ul> <p>This program helped me build skills by creating an interactive user interface for a computer application. I worked with 3 other students from different backgrounds to design and build our project, culminating in presenting our concept at a public exhibit.</p><p> Trevor Hunter </p><p> Current student, Master of Interaction Design </p> <p><a href="/events">See all events</a></p> <a href="/events/uq-open-day"> UQ Open Day </a><p>2 August </p><h5> UQ Open Day </h5><p>St Lucia</p> <p><a href="/stories">See all stories</a></p> <a href="/stories/emerging-careers-arts-communication"> Emerging careers in the arts and communication industries </a><p>Careers</p><h5> Emerging careers in the arts and communication industries </h5><p>5-minute read</p><a href="/stories/meet-expert-exploring-computer-science-dr-paul-vrbik"> Meet the expert: exploring computer science with Dr Paul Vrbik </a><p>UQ people</p><h5> Meet the expert: exploring computer science with Dr Paul Vrbik </h5><p>3-minute read</p><a href="/stories/meet-jojo-environmental-management-student-china"> Meet JoJo, an Environmental Management student from China </a><p>UQ people</p><h5> Meet JoJo, an Environmental Management student from China </h5><p>5-minute</p>',
