UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Overview</h4> <p> Equip yourself with an outstanding education, transportable knowledge, and the industry know-how to capitalise on today’s commercial opportunities and succeed in globally competitive legal and business environments. </p><p>UQ''s Master of Laws program is designed to give practitioners and law graduates a rigorous set of knowledge and skills that will enable them to excel in their chosen specialities.</p><p>As the premier law school in Queensland, we offer world-class teaching quality and a suite of law courses relevant to the legal profession in Australia and internationally.</p><p>Our LLM (Master of Laws) coursework program inspires independent and critical thinking about the law and legal methods, the application of law in contemporary practice, and how the future of law and legal practice may be impacted by digital disruption and new technologies.</p><p>You''ll undertake courses predominantly driven by the needs of contemporary legal practice, including those in highly specialised areas, where the principles underpinning study are complex and require a depth of understanding.</p><p>Enriching your time at UQ Law is the impressive list of lecturers who are experts in their fields. The program’s teaching staff includes outstanding academics and honoured professionals, visiting lecturers, legal practitioners, judges and international scholars. They will expose you to diverse backgrounds, experiences and perspectives, and challenge your way of thinking about law and legal practice.</p><p><a href="#tab1">Domestic</a><a href="#tab2">International</a></p><p><a href="#entry-requirements">See full entry requirements</a></p><p>LocationSt LuciaDuration 1 Year full-time (or part-time equivalent) 1.5 Years full-time (or part-time equivalent) Start SemesterSemester 1 (22 Feb, 2027), Semester 2 (26 Jul, 2027)Program Code5591AQFLevel 9</p><p><a href="#fees-scholarships">Scholarships available</a></p><p><a href="#entry-requirements">See full entry requirements</a></p><p>LocationSt LuciaFees<a href="#fees-scholarships">A$56800</a>Duration 1 Year full-time (only available as full-time study) 1.5 Years full-time (only available as full-time study) Start Semester Semester 1 (22 Feb, 2027), Semester 2 (26 Jul, 2027) Semester dates for 2028 are yet to be confirmed Program Code5591CRICOS Code082603EAQFLevel 9</p><p><a href="#fees-scholarships">Scholarships available</a></p> <p> <h5> Program highlights </h5> </p> <p> <h5> Program highlights </h5> </p> <ul><li>Learn at the oldest law school in Queensland, with a reputation for producing outstanding graduates.</li><li>Gain deep knowledge in specialty areas of growing importance to legal practice and your future goals sooner than by learning on the job.</li><li>Engage with a passionate cohort that includes local, interstate and international lawyers drawing on their professional experiences to deepen class discussions. Establish valuable personal and professional connections.</li><li>Optionally, write a dissertation on a topic that is of interest and relevance to you and your career. </li></ul> <p>1 in Queensland for law and legal studies</p><p>QS World University Rankings 2026</p> <p>60 in the world for law and legal studies</p><p>QS World University Rankings 2026</p> <p> <h5> How you''ll learn </h5> </p> <p>Your learning experiences are designed to best suit the learning outcomes of the courses you choose.</p><ul><li>Lectures</li><li>Research experience</li><li>Seminars</li></ul> <p> <h5> What you''ll study </h5> </p> <p>At UQ, degrees are called ''programs'' and subjects are called ''courses''. Here''s a sample of the courses you could study in this program:</p><ul><li>Fundamentals of the Common Law [Core course]</li><li>Intellectual Property Law [Elective]</li><li>AI and Internet Law [Elective]</li><li>Law, Terrorism and Human Rights [Elective]</li><li>Cultural Heritage Law [Elective]</li><li>Law of the World Trade Organization [Elective]</li><li>Supervised Research Project [Elective]</li></ul><p><a href="https://programs-courses.uq.edu.au/requirements/program/5591/2027">See courses and program structure</a></p> <p>Average annual salary range</p><h5>Barrister</h5>$90K–$110K<p>seek.com.au</p><p>Average annual salary range</p><h5>Solicitor</h5>$100–$120K<p>seek.com.au</p> <p>I chose this program with the hope of broadening my understanding of different practice areas. My lecturers were very encouraging in allowing us to pursue various research projects and topics within our assessment, while providing incredible guidance. I now feel more prepared and confident for my next challenge.</p><p> Theresa Shaw </p><p> Graduate, Master of Laws </p><p>The opportunity to choose courses that you personally find interesting and useful lets you independently define your specialisation and tailor your very own degree. </p><p> Olga Nosova </p><p> Graduate, Master of Laws </p><p>The UQ Law School show a great deal of support for its students and their success. I had great lecturers and professors who were very knowledgeable, and our lectures featured guest speakers who were highly accomplished within the topics we studied.</p><p> Israa Hamed E Alharbi </p><p> Graduate, Master of Laws </p> <p><a href="/events">See all events</a></p> <a href="/events/uq-open-day"> UQ Open Day </a><p>2 August </p><h5> UQ Open Day </h5><p>St Lucia</p> <p><a href="/stories">See all stories</a></p> <a href="/stories/whats-it-study-postgraduate-law-degree-uq"> What’s it like to study a postgraduate law degree at UQ? </a><p>Uni life</p><h5> What’s it like to study a postgraduate law degree at UQ? </h5><p>7-minute read</p><a href="/stories/best-law-courses-australia-practitioners"> Practical legal training in Queensland </a><p>Study tips</p><h5> Practical legal training in Queensland </h5><p>3-minute read</p><a href="/stories/areas-law-explore-postgraduate"> Areas of law to explore </a><p>Careers</p><h5> Areas of law to explore </h5><p>4-minute read</p>',
    total_course_duration = '1 Year full-time (or part-time equivalent) 1.5 Years full-time (or part-time equivalent)',
    offshore_tuition_fee = 56800,
    onshore_tuition_fee = 44344,
    enrolment_fee = NULL,
    materials_fee = NULL,
    entry_requirements = '<h4>Entry Requirements</h4> <h5>Entry requirements</h5> <p>It''s possible to complete this degree in 1.5 years or 1 year depending on your qualifications and experience.</p><p>You can apply for any duration as long as you meet the entry requirements. You may also be eligible to apply for <a href="/admissions/postgraduate-coursework/check-credit-eligibility">credit or exemptions</a> to shorten your degree further. You''ll graduate with the same qualification no matter how long you take to complete the degree.</p> <h5>1.5-year degree (24 units of study)</h5><p>To be eligible to complete the degree in 1.5 years full-time (only available as full-time study), you''ll need:</p><ul><li>a degree in law leading to admission to legal practice (eg LLB or equivalent), or</li><li>an equivalent academic or professional qualification in law and be able to demonstrate to the satisfaction of the Executive Dean that you have the requisite knowledge and experience to complete the program.</li></ul><p><br/></p><p>You must have a grade point average (GPA) of 4.0 on a 7-point scale in your previous qualification.</p><h5>1-year degree (16 units of study)</h5><p>If you have relevant prior learning or experience, you can reduce the number of courses you need to complete and graduate in less time.</p><p>To be eligible to complete the degree in 1 year full-time (only available as full-time study), you''ll need:</p><ul><li>an honours or master''s degree in law leading to admission to legal practice (eg LLB(Hons), JD or equivalent), or</li><li>a degree in law leading to admission to legal practice (eg LLB or equivalent), and either - a Graduate Diploma in Legal Practice or equivalent qualification, or 2 years of professional full-time equivalent relevant work experience (see below), or</li><li>an equivalent academic or professional qualification in law and be able to demonstrate to the satisfaction of the Executive Dean that you have the requisite knowledge and experience to complete the program.</li></ul><p><br/></p><p>You must have a grade point average (GPA) of 4.0 on a 7-point scale in your previous qualification.</p> <p> <h5> Relevant work experience </h5> </p> <p>Relevant work experience includes work as a solicitor; barrister; in-house legal practitioner; legal consultant with a major consulting firm; patent attorney; judge’s associate or clerk; court registrar or judge; contracts officer or claims manager within a commercial entity; bank, finance or insurance officer; research officer within a legal practice, law reform commission or public advocacy organisation; legal studies teacher or legal academic.</p> <p> <h5> GPA equivalent </h5> </p> <p>Select where you studied and your qualification to see the GPA equivalent you need to be considered for this program.</p><p>Use the GPA equivalent as a guide. When you apply, we’ll calculate your GPA using the UQ grading scale. Any failing grades will be included. Entry requirements are subject to change.</p> <h5>Equivalent subjects</h5> <table><thead><tr><th>Subject</th><th>Qualification equivalent</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table><p> <h5> English language requirements </h5> </p> <p>IELTS overall 6.5; reading 6; writing 6; speaking 6; listening 6. For other English Language Proficiency Tests and Scores approved for UQ</p><p>TOEFL iBT (including Paper Edition) - Overall 87, listening 19, reading 19, writing 21 and speaking 19.</p><p>PTE Academic - Overall Score of 64 and 60 in all sub bands.</p><p>BE - A minimum overall grade of 4 plus a minimum grade of C in all macro skills.</p><p>CES - Overall 176 and 169 in all sub bands.</p><p>OET is not accepted.</p><p>There are other ways to meet the English language requirements. For some programs, additional conditions apply.</p><p><a href="/admissions/english-language-requirements">Learn how to meet the English language requirements</a></p> <p> <h5> Student visas </h5> </p> <p>International students who are accepted into full-time study in the Master of Laws are eligible to apply for an Australian student visa (subclass 500).</p><p>There are a number of requirements you must satisfy before a visa is granted, including the Genuine Student (GS) requirement.</p><p><a href="/university-life/getting-prepared-to-come-to-australia/student-visas">Learn more about student visas</a></p> <p> <h5> Need help meeting the entry requirements? </h5> </p> <p>We can help you meet the academic or English language requirements for your preferred program.</p><p><a href="/admissions/postgraduate-coursework/consider-your-pathway-options">Learn about pathway options</a></p> <p> <h5> Additional application information </h5> </p> <p>Classes may be held at the St Lucia campus, and on occasion, at Brisbane city venues.</p><p>Not all courses listed are offered each year; applicants should contact the School of Law for up-to-date information in relation to course offerings.</p><p>International students are strongly encouraged to register in Orientation Week to attend an optional English for Academic Communication (EAC) program. The program is conducted jointly by staff of UQ College and the Law School. International students are given a brief overview of the Australian legal framework and the common law system. The program also provides an opportunity for new students to meet each other socially.</p>',
    apply_form = 'https://study.uq.edu.au/study-options/programs/master-laws-5591',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '082603E';

UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Overview</h4> <p> Help shape future legal practice in an era of advanced digital disruption and global transformation. </p><p>In this rigorous 4-year program, you''ll develop a deep understanding of different facets of law, outstanding critical and analytical skills, and professional networks. You''ll learn from scholars at the forefront of their fields, with content informed by current research and practice.</p><p>The transferable personal and professional skills you''ll develop can be applied across a wide range of careers.</p><p>You can tailor your studies through your choice of electives, or by combining law with one of 8 different dual programs across science, business and the humanities.</p><p>During your studies, you''ll gain practical experience in areas of law you''re passionate about through our placement courses and the Pro Bono Centre roster. You can also gain mock courtroom experience through debating hypothetical cases in UQ’s dedicated moot court, and through domestic and international mooting competitions.</p><p>You''ll graduate with an internationally respected honours qualification with advanced knowledge and skills that will set you apart in a competitive job market and provide a pathway to future research or learning.</p><p><a href="#tab1">Domestic</a><a href="#tab2">International</a></p><p><a href="#entry-requirements">See full entry requirements</a></p>LocationSt LuciaDuration 4 Years (or part time equivalent)Start SemesterSemester 1 (22 Feb, 2027)QTAC Code<p>718001</p>Program Code2471AQFLevel 8<p><a href="#overview">Dual programs available</a></p><p><a href="#how-to-apply">Admission schemes available</a></p><p><a href="#fees-scholarships">Scholarships available</a></p><p><a href="#entry-requirements">See full entry requirements</a></p>LocationSt LuciaFees<a href="#fees-scholarships">A$56800</a>Duration 4 Years Start Semester Semester 1 (22 Feb, 2027) Semester dates for 2028 are yet to be confirmed QTAC Code<p>718001</p>Program Code2471CRICOS Code082613CAQFLevel 8<p><a href="#overview">Dual programs available</a></p><p><a href="#fees-scholarships">Scholarships available</a></p> <p> <h5> Program highlights </h5> </p> <p> <h5> Program highlights </h5> </p> <ul><li>Enjoy small class sizes, which allow for collaboration and debating face-to-face via interactive seminars and tutorials.</li><li>Enhance your research, advocacy and communication skills by volunteering with the UQ Pro Bono Centre. Provide support to a range of legal organisations and improve access to justice in our community.</li><li>Get support from a life and wellbeing officer just for law students, as well as other academic and career support.</li></ul> <p>1 in Queensland for law and legal studies</p><p>QS World University Rankings 2026</p> <p>60 in the world for law and legal studies</p><p>QS World University Rankings 2026</p> <p> <h5> How you''ll learn </h5> </p> <p>Your learning experiences are designed to best suit the learning outcomes of the courses you choose.</p><ul><li>Lectures</li><li>Tutorials</li><li>Research experience</li><li>Seminars</li></ul> <p> <h5> What you''ll study </h5> </p> <p>At UQ, degrees are called ''programs'' and subjects are called ''courses''. Here''s a sample of the courses you could study in this program:</p><ul><li>Foundations of Law [Core course]</li><li>Trusts and Equity [Core course] </li><li>Ethics and the Legal Profession [Core course]</li><li>Advanced Crime and Criminology [Core course]</li><li>The Law of Estate Planning and Wealth Management [Core course]</li><li>AI and the Law [Core course]</li><li>Legal Internships [Core course]</li></ul><p><a href="https://programs-courses.uq.edu.au/requirements/program/2471/2027">See courses and program structure</a></p> <p> <h5> Dual programs </h5> </p> <p>Double your skills and your opportunities with a dual degree. You can study the Bachelor of Laws (Honours) as a part of these dual programs:</p><ul><li><a href="/study-options/programs/bachelors-journalism-laws-honours-2512">Bachelors of Journalism / Laws (Honours)</a></li><li><a href="/study-options/programs/bachelors-business-management-laws-honours-2334">Bachelors of Business Management / Laws (Honours)</a></li><li><a href="/study-options/programs/bachelors-arts-laws-honours-2142">Bachelors of Arts / Laws (Honours)</a></li><li><a href="/study-options/programs/bachelors-humanities-laws-honours-2511">Bachelors of Humanities / Laws (Honours)</a></li><li><a href="/study-options/programs/bachelors-economics-laws-honours-2469">Bachelors of Economics / Laws (Honours)</a></li><li><a href="/study-options/programs/bachelors-commerce-laws-honours-2465">Bachelors of Commerce / Laws (Honours)</a></li><li><a href="/study-options/programs/bachelors-computer-science-laws-honours-2568">Bachelors of Computer Science / Laws (Honours)</a></li><li><a href="/study-options/programs/bachelors-science-laws-honours-2472">Bachelors of Science / Laws (Honours)</a></li></ul> <p> <h5> Career possibilities </h5> </p> <p>Our programs prepare you for your first job and beyond. Here are some of the careers you could be on your way to:</p><ul><li>Solicitor</li><li>Barrister</li><li>Judge’s associate</li><li>Legal officer</li><li>Social and government researcher</li><li>Negotiation and dispute resolution specialist</li><li>NGO adviser</li><li>Community laws officer</li><li>Compliance manager</li><li>Company secretary</li></ul> <p>Average annual salary range</p><h5>Legal Counsel</h5>$145–$165K<p>seek.com.au</p><p>Average annual salary range</p><h5>Barrister</h5>$90K–$110K<p>seek.com.au</p> <p> <h5> Next steps after graduation </h5> </p> <p>You''ll graduate with an internationally respected honours qualification that satisfies the academic requirements for admission as a legal practitioner in Australia. </p><p>Graduates wishing to practise law must also complete practical legal training and meet the admission requirements set by the relevant legal practitioners admissions board.</p><p>As admission requirements may change, students should refer to the current advice issued by the relevant admissions board.</p><p>A law degree also opens pathways beyond legal practice. Graduates use their legal knowledge, analytical skills and understanding of institutions in a wide range of careers, working in:</p><ul><li>government</li><li>business</li><li>policy and regulation</li><li>consulting</li><li>advocacy</li><li>diplomacy</li><li>community organisations and the not-for-profit sector.</li></ul> <p> <h5> Professional memberships </h5> </p> <p>When you graduate, you may be eligible for memberships with the following professional organisations. Contact the organisation to find out how to become a member.</p><ul><li>Bar Association of Queensland</li><li>Queensland Law Society</li></ul> <p> <h5> Program accreditation </h5> </p> <p>The Bachelor of Laws (Honours) is accredited by:</p><ul><li>Legal Practitioners Admissions Board</li></ul> <p>Participating in mooting and client competitions allowed me to apply legal knowledge to practical scenarios. They challenged me to think critically under pressure, deepened my understanding of the legal profession and strengthened my commitment to a career in law.</p><p> Priscilla Gyasi-Agyei </p><p> Graduate, Bachelors of Commerce / Laws (Honours) </p><p>I’m grateful to have the support of such excellent teaching staff. I’m consistently amazed by the level of knowledge and understanding my tutors demonstrate. They regularly go above and beyond in providing specific, relevant and insightful feedback on my work.</p><p> Charlie Hoare </p><p> Current student, Bachelors of Humanities / Laws (Honours) </p><p>My placement through the Clinical Legal Education subject gave me invaluable experience to shadow a Human Rights Lawyer as she provided legal advice to highly vulnerable homeless individuals. I saw how empathetic lawyers and accessible legal advice can change lives.</p><p> Annabelle (Annie) Khoo </p><p> Graduate, Bachelor of Laws (Honours) </p> <p><a href="/events">See all events</a></p> <a href="/events/ancient-history-experience-day"> Ancient History Experience Day </a><p>15 July </p><h5> Ancient History Experience Day </h5><p>St Lucia</p><a href="/events/world-religions-experience-day-2026"> World Religions Experience Day 2026 </a><p>22 July - 23 July </p><h5> World Religions Experience Day 2026 </h5><p>St Lucia</p><a href="/events/uq-open-day"> UQ Open Day </a><p>2 August </p><h5> UQ Open Day </h5><p>St Lucia</p> <p><a href="/stories">See all stories</a></p> <a href="/stories/why-study-law-uq"> Why study law at UQ? </a><p>UQ people</p><h5> Why study law at UQ? </h5><p>5-minute read</p><a href="/stories/extracurricular-activities-and-opportunities-law-students"> Extracurricular activities and opportunities for law students </a><p>Uni life</p><h5> Extracurricular activities and opportunities for law students </h5><p>5-minute read</p><a href="/stories/prepare-courtroom-mooting-uq"> Prepare for the courtroom: mooting at UQ </a><p>Uni life</p><h5> Prepare for the courtroom: mooting at UQ </h5><p>4-minute read</p>',
    total_course_duration = '4 Years (or part time equivalent)',
    offshore_tuition_fee = 227200,
    onshore_tuition_fee = 65620,
    enrolment_fee = NULL,
    materials_fee = NULL,
    entry_requirements = '<h4>Entry Requirements</h4> <p> <h5> Prerequisites </h5> </p> Queensland Year 12 (or equivalent):<ul><li>General English subject (Units 3 &amp; 4, C)</li></ul> <h5> Minimum entry score </h5> <p>Select where you studied and your qualification to see the minimum entry score you need to be considered for this program.</p><p>Use the minimum entry score as a guide. Your score must be at least equivalent to the required Australian Year 12 ATAR score. Entry requirements are subject to change.</p> <h5>Equivalent subjects</h5> <table><thead><tr><th>Subject</th><th>Qualification equivalent</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table><p> <h5> English language requirements </h5> </p> <p>IELTS overall 7; writing 7; speaking 7; reading 6; listening 6. For other English Language Proficiency Tests and Scores approved for UQ</p><p>TOEFL iBT (including Paper Edition) - Overall 100, listen 19, read 19, write 27, speak 23</p><p>PTE Academic - Overall 72, listen 60, read 60, write 72, speak 72</p><p>BE - A minimum overall grade of 5 plus a minimum grade of A in Writing and Speaking</p><p>CES - Overall 185, listening 169, reading 169, writing 185, speaking 185</p><p>OET is not accepted</p><p>There are other ways to meet the English language requirements. For some programs, additional conditions apply.</p><p><a href="/admissions/english-language-requirements">Learn how to meet the English language requirements</a></p> <p> <h5> Student visas </h5> </p> <p>International students who are accepted into full-time study in the Bachelor of Laws (Honours) are eligible to apply for an Australian student visa (subclass 500).</p><p>There are a number of requirements you must satisfy before a visa is granted, including the Genuine Student (GS) requirement.</p><p><a href="/university-life/getting-prepared-to-come-to-australia/student-visas">Learn more about student visas</a></p> <p> <h5> Need help meeting the entry requirements? </h5> </p> <p>We can help you meet the minimum entry score, subject prerequisites or English language requirements for your preferred program.</p><p><a href="/admissions/undergraduate/consider-your-pathway-options">Learn about pathway options</a></p>',
    apply_form = 'https://study.uq.edu.au/study-options/programs/bachelor-laws-honours-2471',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '082613C';

UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Overview</h4> <p> Gain an understanding of the physics and technology surrounding magnetic resonance, and be in demand here and overseas. </p><p>This program covers the fundamentals of magnetic resonance technology, including the physics of magnetic resonance and image formation, the components of modern-day magnetic resonance imaging (MRI) scanners, and safety considerations within this specialised field. It''s ideal if you are seeking formal qualifications in this rapidly expanding field.</p><p>In a multidisciplinary environment, you''ll learn from experienced radiographers, medical practitioners, medical physicists, chemists and engineers.</p><p>You''ll have access to the most comprehensive and advanced range of magnetic resonance instrumentation in the Southern Hemisphere, including:</p><ul><li>whole-body scanners</li><li>high resolution nuclear magnetic resonance (NMR) spectrometers</li><li>solid state and electron paramagnetic resonance (EPR) instruments</li><li>micro-imaging and animal imaging systems.</li></ul><p>Apply your knowledge to use magnetic resonance equipment and be exposed to new techniques that are not yet part of standard clinical practice.</p><p>You''ll gain the skills to assess the needs of a radiography practice and the capability to meet these needs with equipment from various manufacturers.</p><p><a href="#tab1">Domestic</a><a href="#tab2">International</a></p><p><a href="#entry-requirements">See full entry requirements</a></p><p>LocationExternal, St LuciaDuration Half Year (or part time equivalent)Start SemesterSemester 1 (22 Feb, 2027), Semester 2 (26 Jul, 2027)Program Code5036AQFLevel 8</p><p><a href="#fees-scholarships">Scholarships available</a></p><p><a href="#entry-requirements">See full entry requirements</a></p><p>LocationExternal, St LuciaFees<a href="#fees-scholarships">A$28400</a>Duration Half Year Start Semester Semester 1 (22 Feb, 2027), Semester 2 (26 Jul, 2027) Semester dates for 2028 are yet to be confirmed Program Code5036CRICOS Code114808AAQFLevel 8</p><p><a href="#fees-scholarships">Scholarships available</a></p> <p> <h5> Program highlights </h5> </p> <p> <h5> Program highlights </h5> </p> <ul><li>Access the most advanced range of magnetic resonance instrumentation in the Southern Hemisphere.</li><li>Learn the latest techniques from leading experts in the field.</li><li>Be eligible for Australian Society of Medical Imaging and Radiation Therapy continuing professional development (CPD) points accrual.</li><li>Organise your study around professional and personal commitments, with all courses in this program able to be completed online.</li></ul> <p>1 in Queensland for life sciences and medicine</p><p>QS World University Rankings 2026</p> <p>33 in the world for life sciences and medicine</p><p>QS World University Rankings 2026</p> <p> <h5> How you''ll learn </h5> </p> <p>Your learning experiences are designed to best suit the learning outcomes of the courses you choose.</p><ul><li>Lectures</li><li>Tutorials</li><li>Online study</li><li>Seminars</li></ul> <p> <h5> What you''ll study </h5> </p> <p>At UQ, degrees are called ''programs'' and subjects are called ''courses''. Here''s a sample of the courses you could study in this program:</p><ul><li>Magnetic Resonance Imaging: Fundamentals [Core course]</li><li>Magnetic Resonance Instrumentation [Core course] </li><li>MR Safety &amp; Monitoring [Core course]</li><li>MRI Pulse Sequence Construction &amp; Image Contrast [Core course]</li></ul><p><a href="https://programs-courses.uq.edu.au/requirements/program/5036/2027">See courses and program structure</a></p> <p> <h5> Career possibilities </h5> </p> <p>Postgraduate study can take you anywhere. Here are some of the careers you could be on your way to:</p><ul><li>Magnetic resonance technologist</li><li>Magnetic resonance imaging physicist</li><li>Image processor</li><li>Biomedical researcher</li><li>Senior radiographer</li></ul> <p>Average annual salary range</p><h5>Radiographer</h5>$95K–$110K<p>seek.com.au</p><p>Average annual salary range</p><h5>Medical Imaging Technologist</h5>$90K–$105K<p>seek.com.au</p> <p> <h5> Next steps after graduation </h5> </p> <p>MRI physicists, MR technologists, image processors, engineers and biomedical engineers are in strong demand within Australia and internationally. UQ graduates have found employment in leadership positions in hospitals, private practice and research facilities.</p><p>This qualification alone does not provide eligibility for Australian Health Practitioner Regulation Agency (AHPRA) registration as a radiographer or medical imaging technologist. <a href="https://www.medicalradiationpracticeboard.gov.au/Registration/Registration-requirements-and-your-obligations.aspx">Visit the AHPRA website for more information</a>.</p> <p>I really wanted to broaden my education and was able to learn a lot... The theoretical and practical knowledge has helped not just in the day-to-day running of an MRI unit, but also in selecting, purchasing and installing new systems. </p><p> Mark Denham </p><p> Graduate, Master of Magnetic Resonance Technology </p> <p><a href="/events">See all events</a></p> <a href="/events/uq-open-day"> UQ Open Day </a><p>2 August </p><h5> UQ Open Day </h5><p>St Lucia</p> <p><a href="/stories">See all stories</a></p> <a href="/stories/uq-postgraduate-study-top-5-reasons"> Top 5 reasons to choose UQ for postgraduate study </a><p>Careers</p><h5> Top 5 reasons to choose UQ for postgraduate study </h5><p>3-minute read</p><a href="/stories/why-uq-world-top-50-university"> Why is UQ a world top 50 university? </a><p>Uni life</p><h5> Why is UQ a world top 50 university? </h5><p>4-minute read</p><a href="/stories/turning-her-curiosity-healthcare-career"> Turning her curiosity into a healthcare career </a><p>UQ people</p><h5> Turning her curiosity into a healthcare career </h5><p>4-minute read</p>',
    total_course_duration = '',
    offshore_tuition_fee = 28400,
    onshore_tuition_fee = 4770,
    enrolment_fee = NULL,
    materials_fee = NULL,
    entry_requirements = '<h4>Entry Requirements</h4> <h5>Entry requirements</h5> <p>To be eligible for entry, you''ll need:</p> <ul><li>a bachelor''s degree (or equivalent) in a relevant discipline (see below), or</li><li>2 years full-time equivalent, relevant work experience in medical imaging, physics or molecular imaging.</li></ul>You must have a grade point average (GPA) of 4.0 on a 7-point scale in your previous qualification. <p> <h5> Relevant disciplines for previous qualifications </h5> </p> <p>Relevant disciplines include mathematics, physics, chemistry, biology, medical imaging, medical radiation, radiography, allied health, biomedical engineering, engineering and computer science. </p> <p> <h5> GPA equivalent </h5> </p> <p>Select where you studied and your qualification to see the GPA equivalent you need to be considered for this program.</p><p>Use the GPA equivalent as a guide. When you apply, we’ll calculate your GPA using the UQ grading scale. Any failing grades will be included. Entry requirements are subject to change.</p> <h5>Equivalent subjects</h5> <table><thead><tr><th>Subject</th><th>Qualification equivalent</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table><p> <h5> Related programs </h5> </p> <p>Depending on your previous qualifications and current goals, you might want to consider<br/> one of these related programs:</p><ul><li><a href="/study-options/programs/master-magnetic-resonance-technology-5193">Master of Magnetic Resonance Technology</a></li><li><a href="/study-options/programs/graduate-diploma-magnetic-resonance-technology-5096">Graduate Diploma in Magnetic Resonance Technology</a></li></ul> <p> <h5> English language requirements </h5> </p> <p>IELTS overall 6.5; reading 6; writing 6; speaking 6; listening 6. For other English Language Proficiency Tests and Scores approved for UQ</p><p>TOEFL iBT (including Paper Edition) - Overall 87, listening 19, reading 19, writing 21 and speaking 19.</p><p>PTE Academic - Overall Score of 64 and 60 in all sub bands.</p><p>BE - A minimum overall grade of 4 plus a minimum grade of C in all macro skills.</p><p>CES - Overall 176 and 169 in all sub bands.</p><p>OET is not accepted.</p><p>There are other ways to meet the English language requirements. For some programs, additional conditions apply.</p><p><a href="/admissions/english-language-requirements">Learn how to meet the English language requirements</a></p> <p> <h5> Student visas </h5> </p> <p>International students who are accepted into full-time study in the Graduate Certificate in Magnetic Resonance Technology are eligible to apply for an Australian student visa (subclass 500).</p><p>There are a number of requirements you must satisfy before a visa is granted, including the Genuine Student (GS) requirement.</p><p><a href="/university-life/getting-prepared-to-come-to-australia/student-visas">Learn more about student visas</a></p>',
    apply_form = 'https://study.uq.edu.au/study-options/programs/graduate-certificate-magnetic-resonance-technology-5036',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '114808A';

UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Overview</h4> <p> Gain an advanced understanding of the physics and technology surrounding magnetic resonance, and be in demand here and overseas. </p><p>This program is designed for health professionals working with magnetic resonance imaging (MRI) equipment who are seeking formal qualifications in this rapidly expanding field.</p><p>In a multidisciplinary environment, you''ll learn from experienced radiographers, medical practitioners, medical physicists, chemists and engineers about the physics of magnetic resonance and image formation, the components of modern MRI scanners and essential specialist practical skills.</p><p>You''ll have access to the most comprehensive and advanced range of magnetic resonance instrumentation in the Southern Hemisphere, including:</p><ul><li>whole-body scanners</li><li>high resolution nuclear magnetic resonance (NMR) spectrometers</li><li>solid state and electron paramagnetic resonance (EPR) instruments</li><li>micro-imaging and animal imaging systems.</li></ul><p>Apply your knowledge to projects that make innovative use of magnetic resonance, and be exposed to new techniques that are not yet part of standard clinical practice.</p><p>You''ll gain the skills to assess the needs of a radiography practice and the capability to meet these needs with equipment from various manufacturers.</p><p><a href="#tab1">Domestic</a><a href="#tab2">International</a></p><p><a href="#entry-requirements">See full entry requirements</a></p><p>LocationExternal, St LuciaDuration 1 Year full-time (or part-time equivalent) Start SemesterSemester 1 (22 Feb, 2027), Semester 2 (26 Jul, 2027)Program Code5096AQFLevel 8</p><p><a href="#fees-scholarships">Scholarships available</a></p><p><a href="#entry-requirements">See full entry requirements</a></p><p>LocationExternal, St LuciaFees<a href="#fees-scholarships">A$56800</a>Duration 1 Year full-time Start Semester Semester 1 (22 Feb, 2027), Semester 2 (26 Jul, 2027) Semester dates for 2028 are yet to be confirmed Program Code5096CRICOS Code034046EAQFLevel 8</p><p><a href="#fees-scholarships">Scholarships available</a></p> <p> <h5> Program highlights </h5> </p> <p> <h5> Program highlights </h5> </p> <ul><li>Access the most advanced range of magnetic resonance instrumentation in the Southern Hemisphere.</li><li>Learn the latest techniques from leading experts in the field.</li><li>Be eligible for Australian Society of Medical Imaging and Radiation Therapy continuing professional development (CPD) points accrual.</li><li>Organise your study around professional and personal commitments, with all courses in this program able to be completed online.</li></ul> <p>1 in Queensland for life sciences and medicine</p><p>QS World University Rankings 2026</p> <p>33 in the world for life sciences and medicine</p><p>QS World University Rankings 2026</p> <p> <h5> How you''ll learn </h5> </p> <p>Your learning experiences are designed to best suit the learning outcomes of the courses you choose.</p><ul><li>Lectures</li><li>Tutorials</li><li>Online study</li><li>Seminars</li></ul> <p> <h5> What you''ll study </h5> </p> <p>At UQ, degrees are called ''programs'' and subjects are called ''courses''. Here''s a sample of the courses you could study in this program:</p><ul><li>MR Safety &amp; Monitoring [Core course] </li><li>MRI Pulse Sequence Construction &amp; Image Contrast [Core course]</li><li>Fundamental MRI of the Brain &amp; Spine [Elective]</li><li>Fundamental Abdominal and Pelvic MRI [Elective]</li><li>Magnetic Resonance Spectroscopy &amp; Applications [Elective]</li><li>Magnetic Resonance Clinical Practice [Elective]</li><li>Strategic Human Resources Management [Elective] </li></ul><p><a href="https://programs-courses.uq.edu.au/requirements/program/5096/2027">See courses and program structure</a></p> <p> <h5> Career possibilities </h5> </p> <p>Postgraduate study can take you anywhere. Here are some of the careers you could be on your way to:</p><ul><li>Magnetic resonance technologist</li><li>Magnetic resonance imaging physicist</li><li>Image processor</li><li>Biomedical researcher</li><li>Senior radiographer</li></ul> <p>Average annual salary range</p><h5>Radiographer</h5>$95K–$110K<p>seek.com.au</p><p>Average annual salary range</p><h5>Medical Imaging Technologist</h5>$90K–$105K<p>seek.com.au</p> <p> <h5> Next steps after graduation </h5> </p> <p>MRI physicists, MR technologists, image processors, engineers and biomedical engineers are in strong demand within Australia and internationally. UQ graduates have found employment in leadership positions in hospitals, private practice and research facilities.</p><p>This qualification alone does not provide eligibility for Australian Health Practitioner Regulation Agency (AHPRA) registration as a radiographer or medical imaging technologist. <a href="https://www.medicalradiationpracticeboard.gov.au/Registration/Registration-requirements-and-your-obligations.aspx">Visit the AHPRA website for more information</a>.</p> <p>I really wanted to broaden my education and was able to learn a lot... The theoretical and practical knowledge has helped not just in the day-to-day running of an MRI unit, but also in selecting, purchasing and installing new systems. </p><p> Mark Denham </p><p> Graduate, Master of Magnetic Resonance Technology </p> <p><a href="/events">See all events</a></p> <a href="/events/uq-open-day"> UQ Open Day </a><p>2 August </p><h5> UQ Open Day </h5><p>St Lucia</p> <p><a href="/stories">See all stories</a></p> <a href="/stories/why-uq-world-top-50-university"> Why is UQ a world top 50 university? </a><p>Uni life</p><h5> Why is UQ a world top 50 university? </h5><p>4-minute read</p><a href="/stories/uq-postgraduate-study-top-5-reasons"> Top 5 reasons to choose UQ for postgraduate study </a><p>Careers</p><h5> Top 5 reasons to choose UQ for postgraduate study </h5><p>3-minute read</p><a href="/stories/turning-her-curiosity-healthcare-career"> Turning her curiosity into a healthcare career </a><p>UQ people</p><h5> Turning her curiosity into a healthcare career </h5><p>4-minute read</p>',
    total_course_duration = '1 Year full-time (or part-time equivalent)',
    offshore_tuition_fee = 56800,
    onshore_tuition_fee = 9540,
    enrolment_fee = NULL,
    materials_fee = NULL,
    entry_requirements = '<h4>Entry Requirements</h4> <h5>Entry requirements</h5> <p>To be eligible for entry, you''ll need:</p> <ul><li>a bachelor''s degree (or equivalent) in a relevant discipline (see below); or</li><li>2 years full-time equivalent, relevant work experience in medical imaging, physics or molecular imaging.</li></ul>You must have a grade point average (GPA) of 4.0 on a 7-point scale in your previous qualifications. <p> <h5> Relevant disciplines for previous qualifications </h5> </p> <p>Relevant disciplines include mathematics, physics, chemistry, biology, medical imaging, medical radiation, radiography, allied health, biomedical engineering, engineering, and computer science.</p> <p> <h5> GPA equivalent </h5> </p> <p>Select where you studied and your qualification to see the GPA equivalent you need to be considered for this program.</p><p>Use the GPA equivalent as a guide. When you apply, we’ll calculate your GPA using the UQ grading scale. Any failing grades will be included. Entry requirements are subject to change.</p> <h5>Equivalent subjects</h5> <table><thead><tr><th>Subject</th><th>Qualification equivalent</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table><p> <h5> Related programs </h5> </p> <p>Depending on your previous qualifications and current goals, you might want to consider<br/> one of these related programs:</p><ul><li><a href="/study-options/programs/master-magnetic-resonance-technology-5193">Master of Magnetic Resonance Technology</a></li><li><a href="/study-options/programs/graduate-certificate-magnetic-resonance-technology-5036">Graduate Certificate in Magnetic Resonance Technology</a></li></ul> <p> <h5> English language requirements </h5> </p> <p>IELTS overall 6.5; reading 6; writing 6; speaking 6; listening 6. For other English Language Proficiency Tests and Scores approved for UQ</p><p>TOEFL iBT (including Paper Edition) - Overall 87, listening 19, reading 19, writing 21 and speaking 19.</p><p>PTE Academic - Overall Score of 64 and 60 in all sub bands.</p><p>BE - A minimum overall grade of 4 plus a minimum grade of C in all macro skills.</p><p>CES - Overall 176 and 169 in all sub bands.</p><p>OET is not accepted.</p><p>There are other ways to meet the English language requirements. For some programs, additional conditions apply.</p><p><a href="/admissions/english-language-requirements">Learn how to meet the English language requirements</a></p> <p> <h5> Student visas </h5> </p> <p>International students who are accepted into full-time study in the Graduate Diploma in Magnetic Resonance Technology are eligible to apply for an Australian student visa (subclass 500).</p><p>There are a number of requirements you must satisfy before a visa is granted, including the Genuine Student (GS) requirement.</p><p><a href="/university-life/getting-prepared-to-come-to-australia/student-visas">Learn more about student visas</a></p>',
    apply_form = 'https://study.uq.edu.au/study-options/programs/graduate-diploma-magnetic-resonance-technology-5096',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '034046E';

UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Overview</h4> <p> Gain an advanced understanding of the physics and technology surrounding magnetic resonance, and be in demand here and overseas. </p><p>This program is designed for qualified radiographers wanting to expand their knowledge in magnetic resonance imaging (MRI), as well as biomedical engineers and other health professionals who work with MRI equipment.</p><p>In a multidisciplinary environment, you''ll learn from experienced radiographers, medical practitioners, medical physicists, chemists and engineers. You''ll study the physics of magnetic resonance and image formation, the components of modern MRI scanners, and specialist practical skills essential for a dynamic career in this field.</p><p>Access the most comprehensive and advanced range of magnetic resonance instrumentation in the Southern Hemisphere, including:</p><ul><li>whole-body scanners</li><li>high-resolution nuclear magnetic resonance (NMR) spectrometers</li><li>solid state and electron paramagnetic resonance (EPR) instruments</li><li>micro-imaging and animal imaging systems.</li></ul><p>Apply your knowledge to projects that make innovative use of magnetic resonance, and be exposed to new techniques that are not yet part of standard clinical practice.</p><p>You''ll gain the skills to assess the needs of a radiography practice and the capability to meet these needs with equipment from various manufacturers.</p><p><a href="#tab1">Domestic</a><a href="#tab2">International</a></p><p><a href="#entry-requirements">See full entry requirements</a></p><p>LocationExternal, St LuciaDuration 1.5 Years (or part time equivalent)Start SemesterSemester 1 (22 Feb, 2027), Semester 2 (26 Jul, 2027)Program Code5193AQFLevel 9</p><p><a href="#fees-scholarships">Scholarships available</a></p><p><a href="#entry-requirements">See full entry requirements</a></p><p>LocationExternal, St LuciaFees<a href="#fees-scholarships">A$56800</a>Duration 1.5 Years Start Semester Semester 1 (22 Feb, 2027), Semester 2 (26 Jul, 2027) Semester dates for 2028 are yet to be confirmed Program Code5193CRICOS Code034047DAQFLevel 9</p><p><a href="#fees-scholarships">Scholarships available</a></p> <p> <h5> Program highlights </h5> </p> <p> <h5> Program highlights </h5> </p> <ul><li>Learn the latest techniques from leading experts in the field.</li><li>Apply your knowledge and skills during a week-long on-campus practical immersion.</li><li>Be eligible for Australian Society of Medical Imaging and Radiation Therapy continuing professional development (CPD) points accrual.</li><li>Organise your study around professional and personal commitments, with all courses in this program able to be completed online.</li></ul> <p>1 in Queensland for life sciences and medicine</p><p>QS World University Rankings 2026</p> <p>33 in the world for life sciences and medicine</p><p>QS World University Rankings 2026</p> <p> <h5> How you''ll learn </h5> </p> <p>Your learning experiences are designed to best suit the learning outcomes of the courses you choose.</p><ul><li>Lectures</li><li>Tutorials</li><li>Online study</li><li>Seminars</li></ul> <p> <h5> What you''ll study </h5> </p> <p>At UQ, degrees are called ''programs'' and subjects are called ''courses''. Here''s a sample of the courses you could study in this program:</p><ul><li>Magnetic Resonance Instrumentation [Core course]</li><li>MR Safety &amp; Monitoring [Core course]</li><li>Functional Musculoskeletal MRI [Elective]</li><li>Breast MRI [Elective]</li><li>Analysis of Scientific Data [Elective]</li><li>Diffusion &amp; Perfusion Imaging [Elective]</li><li>Cardiac MRI - Techniques and Applications [Elective]</li></ul><p><a href="https://programs-courses.uq.edu.au/requirements/program/5193/2027">See courses and program structure</a></p> <p> <h5> Career possibilities </h5> </p> <p>Postgraduate study can take you anywhere. Here are some of the careers you could be on your way to:</p><ul><li>Magnetic resonance technologist</li><li>Image processor</li><li>Magnetic resonance imaging physicist</li><li>Biomedical researcher</li><li>Senior radiographer</li></ul> <p>Average annual salary range</p><h5>Radiographer</h5>$95K–$110K<p>seek.com.au</p><p>Average annual salary range</p><h5>Medical Imaging Technologist</h5>$90K–$105K<p>seek.com.au</p> <p> <h5> Next steps after graduation </h5> </p> <p>MRI physicists, MR technologists, image processors, engineers and biomedical engineers are in strong demand within Australia and internationally. UQ graduates have found employment in leadership positions in hospitals, private practice and research facilities.</p><p>This qualification alone does not provide eligibility for Australian Health Practitioner Regulation Agency (AHPRA) registration as a radiographer or medical imaging technologist. <a href="https://www.medicalradiationpracticeboard.gov.au/Registration/Registration-requirements-and-your-obligations.aspx">Visit the AHPRA website for more information</a>.</p> <p>I really wanted to broaden my education and was able to learn a lot... The theoretical and practical knowledge has helped not just in the day-to-day running of an MRI unit, but also in selecting, purchasing and installing new systems. </p><p> Mark Denham </p><p> Graduate, Master of Magnetic Resonance Technology </p> <p><a href="/events">See all events</a></p> <a href="/events/uq-open-day"> UQ Open Day </a><p>2 August </p><h5> UQ Open Day </h5><p>St Lucia</p> <p><a href="/stories">See all stories</a></p> <a href="/stories/it-worth-doing-masters-degree"> Is it worth doing a master’s degree? </a><p>Careers</p><h5> Is it worth doing a master’s degree? </h5><p>4-minute read</p><a href="/stories/why-uq-world-top-50-university"> Why is UQ a world top 50 university? </a><p>Uni life</p><h5> Why is UQ a world top 50 university? </h5><p>4-minute read</p><a href="/stories/turning-her-curiosity-healthcare-career"> Turning her curiosity into a healthcare career </a><p>UQ people</p><h5> Turning her curiosity into a 