UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Overview</h4> <p> Develop specialist knowledge in new and sustainable materials to meet the demands of the future and further your career possibilities. </p><p>The Master of Materials and Manufacturing Engineering (Professional) combines professional engineering and leadership courses with advanced technical courses in composites, materials, manufacturing and mechanics.</p><p>You’ll develop a comprehensive understanding of new and sustainable materials and how they can be used in applications as diverse as aerospace, medical devices and novel functional applications.</p><p>As part of this program, you’ll complete a research project or industry placement.</p><p>Our graduates have the practical and advanced theoretical knowledge needed to step into roles that lead machinery development across the globe.</p><p>Mechanical and materials engineers find employment in dynamic environments where machines are designed, developed, tested and manufactured.</p><p>They’re employed by companies such as:</p><ul><li>AlumniTech</li><li>TechExpo</li><li>Integra LifeSciences Corp.</li></ul><p><a href="#tab1">Domestic</a><a href="#tab2">International</a></p><p><a href="#entry-requirements">See full entry requirements</a></p><p>LocationSt LuciaDuration 2 Years (or part time equivalent)Start SemesterSemester 1 (22 Feb, 2027), Semester 2 (26 Jul, 2027)Program Code5745AQFLevel 9</p><p><a href="#fees-scholarships">Scholarships available</a></p><p><a href="#entry-requirements">See full entry requirements</a></p><p>LocationSt LuciaFees<a href="#fees-scholarships">A$60952</a>Duration 2 Years Start Semester Semester 1 (22 Feb, 2027), Semester 2 (26 Jul, 2027) Semester dates for 2028 are yet to be confirmed Program Code5745CRICOS Code108882HAQFLevel 9</p><p><a href="#fees-scholarships">Scholarships available</a></p> <p> <h5> Program highlights </h5> </p> <p> <h5> Program highlights </h5> </p> <ul><li>Develop your ability to understand, manage and deliver complex professional projects.</li><li>You’ll undertake a research project as part of this program.</li><li>The Master of Materials and Manufacturing Engineering (Professional) is provisionally accredited by Engineers Australia.</li></ul> <p>1 in Queensland for engineering and technology</p><p>QS World University Rankings 2026</p> <p>1 in Queensland for mechanical, aeronautical and manufacturing engineering</p><p>QS World University Rankings 2026</p> <p> <h5> How you''ll learn </h5> </p> <p>Your learning experiences are designed to best suit the learning outcomes of the courses you choose.</p><ul><li>Lectures</li><li>Tutorials</li><li>Research experience</li><li>Seminars</li></ul> <p> <h5> What you''ll study </h5> </p> <p>At UQ, degrees are called ''programs'' and subjects are called ''courses''. Here''s a sample of the courses you could study in this program:</p><ul><li>Environmental Performance of Materials</li><li>Additive Manufacturing</li><li>Advanced Manufacturing</li><li>Nanomaterials</li></ul><p><a href="https://programs-courses.uq.edu.au/requirements/program/5745/2027">See courses and program structure</a></p> <p> <h5> Career possibilities </h5> </p> <p>Postgraduate study can take you anywhere. Here are some of the careers you could be on your way to:</p><ul><li>Manufacturing engineer</li><li>Consultant/facilitator</li><li>Researcher</li><li>Design engineer</li></ul> <p>Average annual salary range</p><h5>Manufacturing Engineer</h5>$90K–$110K<p>seek.com.au</p> <p> <h5> Professional memberships </h5> </p> <p>When you graduate, you may be eligible for memberships with the following professional organisations. Contact the organisation to find out how to become a member.</p><ul><li>Engineers Australia</li></ul> <p> <h5> Program accreditation </h5> </p> <p>The Master of Materials and Manufacturing Engineering (Professional) is provisionally accredited by:</p><ul><li>Engineers Australia</li></ul> <p><a href="/events">See all events</a></p> <a href="/events/uq-open-day"> UQ Open Day </a><p>2 August </p><h5> UQ Open Day </h5><p>St Lucia</p> <p><a href="/stories">See all stories</a></p> <a href="/stories/firefighting-robots-rocket-science-vennkkatas-uq-experience"> From firefighting robots to rocket science: Vennkkata’s UQ experience </a><p>UQ people</p><h5> From firefighting robots to rocket science: Vennkkata’s UQ experience </h5><p>5-minute read</p><a href="/stories/why-study-engineering-uq"> Why study engineering at UQ? </a><p>Study tips</p><h5> Why study engineering at UQ? </h5><p>5-minute read</p><a href="/stories/studying-overseas-a-uq-engineering-student-experience"> Studying overseas: a UQ engineering student experience </a><p>UQ people</p><h5> Studying overseas: a UQ engineering student experience </h5><p>3-minute read</p>',
    total_course_duration = '2 Years (or part time equivalent)',
    offshore_tuition_fee = 121904,
    onshore_tuition_fee = 19080,
    enrolment_fee = NULL,
    materials_fee = NULL,
    entry_requirements = '<h4>Entry Requirements</h4> <h5>Entry requirements</h5> <p>To be eligible for entry, you''ll need:</p> <ul><li>a 4-year bachelor''s degree (or equivalent) in a relevant engineering discipline (see below), or</li><li>a 4-year bachelor''s degree in engineering (or equivalent) which includes all of the relevant discipline content (see below), or</li><li>to have successfully completed 3 years of study towards an approved qualification at an overseas partner institution, with a formal pathway to the Master of Materials and Manufacturing Engineering (Professional).</li></ul><br/>You must have a grade point average (GPA) of 5.0 on a 7-point scale in your previous qualification. <p> <h5> Relevant disciplines for previous qualifications </h5> </p> <p>Relevant disciplines include materials engineering, materials science and engineering, or mechanical and manufacturing engineering.</p><p>If your bachelor''s degree in engineering was not awarded in these disciplines, you must have successfully completed all of the following discipline content in your tertiary studies:</p><ul><li>advanced/higher/engineering mathematics</li><li>statistics</li><li>programming</li><li>mechanics of materials OR structures and materials </li><li>basic manufacturing techniques</li><li>fundamentals of materials science OR engineering materials</li></ul> <p> <h5> GPA equivalent </h5> </p> <p>Select where you studied and your qualification to see the GPA equivalent you need to be considered for this program.</p><p>Use the GPA equivalent as a guide. When you apply, we’ll calculate your GPA using the UQ grading scale. Any failing grades will be included. Entry requirements are subject to change.</p> <h5>Equivalent subjects</h5> <table><thead><tr><th>Subject</th><th>Qualification equivalent</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table><p> <h5> English language requirements </h5> </p> <p>IELTS overall 6.5; reading 6; writing 6; speaking 6; listening 6. For other English Language Proficiency Tests and Scores approved for UQ</p><p>TOEFL iBT (including Paper Edition) - Overall 87, listening 19, reading 19, writing 21 and speaking 19.</p><p>PTE Academic - Overall Score of 64 and 60 in all sub bands.</p><p>BE - A minimum overall grade of 4 plus a minimum grade of C in all macro skills.</p><p>CES - Overall 176 and 169 in all sub bands.</p><p>OET is not accepted.</p><p>There are other ways to meet the English language requirements. For some programs, additional conditions apply.</p><p><a href="/admissions/english-language-requirements">Learn how to meet the English language requirements</a></p> <p> <h5> Inherent requirements </h5> </p> <p>To complete this degree, you have to meet its inherent requirements by demonstrating essential skills and attributes. Read the inherent requirements before you apply.</p><p><a href="/admissions/inherent-requirements/inherent-requirements-engineering-programs">Learn about inherent requirements</a></p> <p> <h5> Student visas </h5> </p> <p>International students who are accepted into full-time study in the Master of Materials and Manufacturing Engineering (Professional) are eligible to apply for an Australian student visa (subclass 500).</p><p>There are a number of requirements you must satisfy before a visa is granted, including the Genuine Student (GS) requirement.</p><p><a href="/university-life/getting-prepared-to-come-to-australia/student-visas">Learn more about student visas</a></p> <p> <h5> Need help meeting the entry requirements? </h5> </p> <p>We can help you meet the academic or English language requirements for your preferred program.</p><p><a href="/admissions/postgraduate-coursework/consider-your-pathway-options">Learn about pathway options</a></p>',
    apply_form = 'https://study.uq.edu.au/study-options/programs/master-materials-and-manufacturing-engineering-professional-5745',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '108882H';

UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Overview</h4> <p> Modern mathematics has its own intrinsic value and beauty, and is key to solving complex challenges in science, engineering, business and technology. </p><p>In the Bachelor of Mathematics, you’ll develop the skills to address abstract and real-world problems, and open doors to careers in academia, industry, teaching and government.</p><p>UQ offers tailored study options, with specialisations that equip you for high-demand roles in industries such as finance, healthcare, technology and consulting.</p><p>In the Mathematical Artificial Intelligence major, you''ll dive into machine learning, data science and algorithm development.</p><p>The Optimisation and Operations Research major is focused on enhancing efficiency and solving complex logistical challenges.</p><p>Beyond academia, you’ll have the chance to gain hands-on experience through programs like the Summer Industry Experience Program, where you’ll work on real-world projects with leading organisations. Or, you can join the Summer and Winter Research Programs and collaborate with our top researchers.</p><p>These experiences provide valuable networking opportunities and prepare you for a smooth transition into your career.</p><p>Studying mathematics at UQ not only hones your quantitative reasoning, but also positions you as a problem solver, ready to make an impact in a fast-changing world. Combine academic excellence, innovation and industry engagement to unlock your potential.</p><p><a href="#tab1">Domestic</a><a href="#tab2">International</a></p><p><a href="#entry-requirements">See full entry requirements</a></p>LocationSt LuciaDuration 3 Years (or part time equivalent)Start SemesterSemester 1 (22 Feb, 2027), Semester 2 (26 Jul, 2027)QTAC Code<p>714401</p>Program Code2460AQFLevel 7<p><a href="#overview">Dual programs available</a></p><p><a href="#how-to-apply">Admission schemes available</a></p><p><a href="#fees-scholarships">Scholarships available</a></p><p><a href="#entry-requirements">See full entry requirements</a></p>LocationSt LuciaFees<a href="#fees-scholarships">A$56800</a>Duration 3 Years Start Semester Semester 1 (22 Feb, 2027), Semester 2 (26 Jul, 2027) Semester dates for 2028 are yet to be confirmed QTAC Code<p>714401</p>Program Code2460CRICOS Code088347AAQFLevel 7<p><a href="#overview">Dual programs available</a></p><p><a href="#fees-scholarships">Scholarships available</a></p> <p> <h5> Program highlights </h5> </p> <p> <h5> Program highlights </h5> </p> <ul><li>Hone your skills in areas that are in demand in today’s data-driven economy. </li><li>Explore advanced problem solving, logical thinking, conceptual ability, communication systems, data handling and interpretation, and research. </li><li>Choose from more than 60 mathematics and statistics courses – more than any other Queensland university.</li><li>Learn from some of Australia’s leading mathematics educators and researchers, gaining insights from professionals who are shaping the future of the field. </li></ul> <p>1 in Queensland for physical sciences, including maths and statistics</p><p>Times Higher Education World University Rankings 2026</p> <p>1 in Queensland for computer science and information systems</p><p>QS World University Rankings 2026</p> <p> <h5> Majors </h5> </p> <p>Tailor your studies to suit your goals. This program offers these options:</p><ul><li><p>Applied Mathematics</p></li><li><p>Bioinformatics</p></li><li><p>Computational Science</p></li><li><p>Computer Science</p></li></ul><p><a href="#majors">See all majors</a></p> <p> <h5> How you''ll learn </h5> </p> <p>Your learning experiences are designed to best suit the learning outcomes of the courses you choose.</p><ul><li>Lectures</li><li>Tutorials</li><li>Overseas study</li><li>Research experience</li><li>Laboratory work</li><li>Seminars</li><li>Workshops</li></ul> <p> <h5> What you''ll study </h5> </p> <p>At UQ, degrees are called ''programs'' and subjects are called ''courses''. Here''s a sample of the courses you could study in this program:</p><ul><li>Calculus &amp; Linear Algebra II [Core course]</li><li>Methods &amp; Models of Applied Mathematics [part of Applied Mathematics major]</li><li>Operations Research &amp; Mathematical Planning [part of Optimisation and Operations Research major]</li><li>Algebraic Methods of Mathematical Physics [part of Mathematical Physics major]</li><li>Deep Learning [part of Mathematical Artificial Intelligence major]</li><li>Abstract Algebra &amp; Number Theory [part of Pure Mathematics major]</li><li>Problems &amp; Applications in Modern Statistics [part of Statistics and Mathematical Data Science major]</li></ul><p><a href="https://programs-courses.uq.edu.au/requirements/program/2460/2027">See courses and program structure</a></p> <p> <h5> Dual programs </h5> </p> <p>Double your skills and your opportunities with a dual degree. You can study the Bachelor of Mathematics as a part of these dual programs:</p><ul><li><a href="/study-options/programs/bachelors-mathematics-economics-2498">Bachelors of Mathematics / Economics</a></li><li><a href="/study-options/programs/bachelors-mathematics-business-management-2500">Bachelors of Mathematics / Business Management</a></li><li><a href="/study-options/programs/bachelors-mathematics-arts-2503">Bachelors of Mathematics / Arts</a></li><li><a href="/study-options/programs/bachelors-music-mathematics-2548">Bachelors of Music / Mathematics</a></li><li><a href="/study-options/programs/bachelors-mathematics-science-2502">Bachelors of Mathematics / Science</a></li><li><a href="/study-options/programs/bachelors-mathematics-commerce-2499">Bachelors of Mathematics / Commerce</a></li><li><a href="/study-options/programs/bachelors-engineering-honours-mathematics-2492">Bachelors of Engineering (Honours) / Mathematics</a></li><li><a href="/study-options/programs/bachelors-mathematics-education-secondary-2501">Bachelors of Mathematics / Education (Secondary)</a></li><li><a href="/study-options/programs/bachelor-mathematics-master-data-science-2557">Bachelor of Mathematics / Master of Data Science</a></li><li><a href="/study-options/programs/bachelors-mathematics-computer-science-2567">Bachelors of Mathematics / Computer Science</a></li></ul> <p> <h5> Career possibilities </h5> </p> <p>Our programs prepare you for your first job and beyond. Depending on which major you choose, here are some of the careers you could be on your way to:</p><ul><li>Data scientist</li><li>Statistician</li><li>Data analyst</li><li>Quantitative analyst</li><li>Bioinformatician</li><li>Research analyst</li><li>Cryptographer</li><li>Software engineer</li><li>Cyber security analyst</li><li>Biostatistician</li></ul> <p>Average annual salary range</p><h5>Meteorologist</h5>$95K–$105K<p>seek.com.au</p><p>Average annual salary range</p><h5>Mathematician</h5>$130–$140K<p>seek.com.au</p> <p> <h5> Next steps after graduation </h5> </p> <p>The Bachelor of Mathematics provides quantitative training that will set you apart in the job market and see you excel in mathematics or one of the many disciplines it influences.</p><p>With a degree in mathematics, you''ll be sought by industry for your excellent quantitative and problem-solving abilities, and gain a wide range of rewarding positions in the public and private sectors. This includes roles in:</p><ul><li>finance</li><li>economics</li><li>mathematical research</li><li>statistics</li><li>actuarial studies</li><li>quantitative finance</li><li>meteorology</li><li>information technology</li><li>data science.</li></ul><p><a href="http://career-profiles.science.uq.edu.au/">Find out more about careers that started in science</a></p> <p>The problem-solving skills I developed during my mathematics degree have been so widely applicable to the range of projects I have worked on in my undergraduate research and in my role as a Data Analyst Consultant.</p><p> Pantea Konn </p><p> Graduate, Bachelor of Mathematics </p> <p><a href="/events">See all events</a></p> <a href="/events/uq-open-day"> UQ Open Day </a><p>2 August </p><h5> UQ Open Day </h5><p>St Lucia</p> <p><a href="/stories">See all stories</a></p> <a href="/stories/whats-it-really-study-mathematics-uq"> What''s it really like to study mathematics at UQ? </a><p>Uni life</p><h5> What''s it really like to study mathematics at UQ? </h5><p>10-minute read</p><a href="/stories/there-limit-challenges-we-can-solve-maths"> Making the greatest mathematical discoveries </a><p>UQ people</p><h5> Making the greatest mathematical discoveries </h5><p>3-minute read</p><a href="/stories/enduring-value-commerce-degree"> The enduring value of a commerce degree </a><p>Careers</p><h5> The enduring value of a commerce degree </h5><p>5-minute read</p>',
    total_course_duration = '3 Years (or part time equivalent)',
    offshore_tuition_fee = 170400,
