UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Overview</h4> <p> Set yourself up for a wide range of career opportunities with a dual degree that combines economic insight and advanced mathematical expertise. </p><p>The Bachelor of Economics provides a strong foundation in areas such as public policy, financial markets, econometrics, international trade and environmental economics, enabling you to understand and influence the key forces shaping business, industry and society.</p><p>In the Bachelor of Mathematics, you’ll have the chance to specialise in cutting-edge fields like Mathematical Artificial Intelligence or Optimisation and Operations Research, or gain a comprehensive understanding of mathematics applications.</p><p>Under the guidance of some of Australia’s leading mathematics educators, you''ll build advanced analytical and quantitative skills that are in high demand in today’s data-driven world.</p><p>With the rapid advancements in computation and technology, the role of mathematics has expanded across industries, opening opportunities in fields like finance, IT and molecular biology.</p><p>Graduates of these programs are uniquely equipped to lead and innovate, addressing complex challenges in both emerging and established sectors.</p><p><a href="#tab1">Domestic</a><a href="#tab2">International</a></p><p><a href="#entry-requirements">See full entry requirements</a></p>LocationSt LuciaDuration 4 Years (or part time equivalent)Start SemesterSemester 1 (22 Feb, 2027), Semester 2 (26 Jul, 2027)QTAC Code<p>714701</p>Program Code2498AQFLevel 7<p><a href="#how-to-apply">Admission schemes available</a></p><p><a href="#fees-scholarships">Scholarships available</a></p><p><a href="#entry-requirements">See full entry requirements</a></p>LocationSt LuciaFees<a href="#fees-scholarships">A$56800</a>Duration 4 Years Start Semester Semester 1 (22 Feb, 2027), Semester 2 (26 Jul, 2027) Semester dates for 2028 are yet to be confirmed QTAC Code<p>714701</p>Program Code2498CRICOS Code088350FAQFLevel 7<p><a href="#fees-scholarships">Scholarships available</a></p> <p> <h5> Program highlights </h5> </p> <p> <h5> Program highlights </h5> </p> <ul><li>Specialise in a mathematics field or master broad applications.</li><li>Build statistical and analytical tools for solving policy challenges.</li><li>Graduate with advanced quantitative skills for diverse industries.</li></ul> <p>3 in Australia for business and economics</p><p>Times Higher Education World University Rankings 2026</p> <p>1 in Queensland for mathematics</p><p>QS World University Rankings 2026</p> <p> <h5> Majors </h5> </p> <p>Tailor your studies to suit your goals. This program offers these options:</p><ul><li><p>Applied Mathematics</p></li><li><p>Economics and Public Policy</p></li><li><p>Economics of Strategy and Behaviour</p></li><li><p>International and Financial Economics</p></li></ul><p><a href="#majors">See all majors</a></p> <p> <h5> How you''ll learn </h5> </p> <p>Your learning experiences are designed to best suit the learning outcomes of the courses you choose.</p><ul><li>Lectures</li><li>Tutorials</li><li>Online study</li><li>Research experience</li><li>Workshops</li></ul> <p> <h5> What you''ll study </h5> </p> <p>At UQ, degrees are called ''programs'' and subjects are called ''courses''.</p><p><a href="https://programs-courses.uq.edu.au/requirements/program/2498/2027">See courses and program structure</a></p><p><a href="https://www.uq.edu.au/study/docs/dual-degree-planners-2027/2027-Bachelors-of-Mathematics-Economics-2498.pdf">View dual degree planner (PDF)</a></p> <p> <h5> Career possibilities </h5> </p> <p>Our programs prepare you for your first job and beyond. Depending on which major you choose, here are some of the careers you could be on your way to:</p><ul><li>Risk modeller</li><li>Senior analyst</li><li>Economic consultant</li><li>Business development manager</li><li>Data analyst</li><li>Investment analyst</li><li>Algorithm specialist</li><li>Quantitative analyst</li></ul> <p>Annual average salary range</p><h5>Financial Analyst</h5>$100–$120K<p>seek.com.au</p><p>Average annual salary range</p><h5>Mathematician</h5>$130–$140K<p>seek.com.au</p> <p> <h5> Next steps after graduation </h5> </p> <p>After graduating with 2 highly respected degrees, you’ll have the pick of a broad range of career possibilities around the world.</p><p>You''ll be in high demand by employers for your excellent quantitative and problem-solving abilities, and your advanced technical, communication and independent thinking skills.</p><p><a href="http://career-profiles.science.uq.edu.au/">Find out more about careers that started in science</a></p> <p>The best things about the Bachelor of Economics would be the practicality and the versatility – how it further prepares us to be analytical individuals ready for the corporate world. The program ensures all students obtain a holistic understanding of economics; be it macro, micro, or analytical skills and so much more.</p><p> Ivory Law </p><p> Graduate, Bachelor of Economics </p><p>The problem-solving skills I developed during my mathematics degree have been so widely applicable to the range of projects I have worked on in my undergraduate research and in my role as a Data Analyst Consultant.</p><p> Pantea Konn </p><p> Graduate, Bachelor of Mathematics </p><p>Discussing real case studies at UQ has helped me understand current economic and policy challenges. I’ve attended guest lectures from industry professionals, including economists from Queensland Treasury, who shared how policies are designed and implemented in practice.</p><p> Kinaura Maisha Sugiarto </p><p> Graduate, Bachelor of Economics </p> <p><a href="/events">See all events</a></p> <a href="/events/ancient-history-experience-day"> Ancient History Experience Day </a><p>15 July </p><h5> Ancient History Experience Day </h5><p>St Lucia</p><a href="/events/world-religions-experience-day-2026"> World Religions Experience Day 2026 </a><p>22 July - 23 July </p><h5> World Religions Experience Day 2026 </h5><p>St Lucia</p><a href="/events/uq-open-day"> UQ Open Day </a><p>2 August </p><h5> UQ Open Day </h5><p>St Lucia</p> <p><a href="/stories">See all stories</a></p> <a href="/stories/what-can-you-do-economics-degree"> What can you do with an economics degree? </a><p>Careers</p><h5> What can you do with an economics degree? </h5><p>14-minute read</p><a href="/stories/why-study-mathematics-uq"> Why study mathematics at UQ? </a><p>Study tips</p><h5> Why study mathematics at UQ? </h5><p>5-minute read</p><a href="/stories/why-study-economics"> Why study economics? </a><p>Careers</p><h5> Why study economics? </h5><p>5-minute read</p>',
    total_course_duration = '4 Years (or part time equivalent)',
    offshore_tuition_fee = 227200,
    onshore_tuition_fee = 44280,
