UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Overview</h4> <p> Make a real difference in people''s physical health and wellbeing by becoming a qualified physiotherapist. </p><p>In the Bachelor of Physiotherapy (Honours) you’ll develop advanced diagnostic and clinical skills to help individuals recover from injuries, manage chronic conditions and optimise their physical function.</p><p>You''ll study the theory and practice behind physiotherapy, exploring key areas including:</p><ul><li>injury prevention</li><li>health promotion</li><li>clinical reasoning and diagnosis</li><li>therapeutic interventions</li><li>exercise prescription</li><li>optimising function.</li></ul><p>You’ll learn techniques to reduce pain, improve movement and restore mobility and function across a range of clinical populations spanning musculoskeletal, neurological and respiratory conditions.</p><p>You’ll develop the skills and knowledge to educate, lead and support healthcare teams, making a lasting impact in the community and shaping the future of healthcare practices.</p><p>You''ll also gain hands-on experience through supervised clinical practice in diverse settings, including hospitals, educational facilities, healthcare organisations, aged and community care, private practice and UQ’s Physiotherapy Clinics.</p><p>Join a long tradition of international leaders in physiotherapy teaching, research and graduate excellence at one of Australia’s largest schools for health and rehabilitation sciences.</p><p><a href="#tab1">Domestic</a><a href="#tab2">International</a></p><p><a href="#entry-requirements">See full entry requirements</a></p>LocationSt LuciaDuration 4 Years full-time Start SemesterSemester 1 (22 Feb, 2027)QTAC Code<p>726002</p>Program Code2369AQFLevel 8<p><a href="#how-to-apply">Admission schemes available</a></p><p><a href="#fees-scholarships">Scholarships available</a></p><p><a href="#entry-requirements">See full entry requirements</a></p>LocationSt LuciaFees<a href="#fees-scholarships">A$60952</a>Duration 4 Years Start Semester Semester 1 (22 Feb, 2027) Semester dates for 2028 are yet to be confirmed QTAC Code<p>726002</p>Program Code2369CRICOS Code082622BAQFLevel 8<p><a href="#fees-scholarships">Scholarships available</a></p> <p> <h5> Program highlights </h5> </p> <p> <h5> Program highlights </h5> </p> <ul><li>Build a strong knowledge foundation of applied study in physiotherapy practice, anatomy, professional ethics, psychology, interprofessional practice and therapeutic exercise.</li><li>Benefit from a diverse range of learning approaches, including clinical visits, seminars, skill-teaching sessions, practical classes and supervised clinical practice.</li><li>Participate in an extensive, award-winning simulated patient program in the School’s hospital simulation ward and the UQ Physiotherapy Clinics.</li><li>Graduate with a highly respected honours qualification, with advanced knowledge and skills that will set you apart in a competitive job market and provide a pathway to future research and learning.</li></ul> <p>2 in the world for sports-related subjects</p><p>QS World University Rankings 2026</p> <p>1 in Australia for sports-related subjects</p><p>QS World University Rankings 2026</p> <p> <h5> How you''ll learn </h5> </p> <p>Your learning experiences are designed to best suit the learning outcomes of the courses you choose.</p><ul><li>Lectures</li><li>Tutorials</li><li>Work placements</li><li>Online study</li><li>Overseas study</li></ul> <p> <h5> What you''ll study </h5> </p> <p>At UQ, degrees are called ''programs'' and subjects are called ''courses''. Here''s a sample of the courses you could study in this program:</p><ul><li>Physiotherapy Foundations I: Physiotherapy Profession &amp; Basic Processes</li><li>Introduction to Principles of Physiotherapy Assessment and Management</li><li>Principles of Exercise in Physiotherapy Practice</li><li>Foundations of Physiotherapy Practice</li></ul><p><a href="https://programs-courses.uq.edu.au/requirements/program/2369/2027">See courses and program structure</a></p> <p> <h5> Career possibilities </h5> </p> <p>Our programs prepare you for your first job and beyond. Here are some of the careers you could be on your way to:</p><ul><li>Physiotherapist</li><li>Rehabilitation therapist</li><li>Researcher</li><li>Community physiotherapist</li><li>Sports physiotherapist</li></ul> <p>Graduate salary</p><h5>Rehabilitation (postgraduate)</h5>$63K–$71K<p>compared.edu.au</p> <p> <h5> Program accreditation </h5> </p> <p>The Bachelor of Physiotherapy (Honours) is accredited by:</p><ul><li>Australian Physiotherapy Council</li></ul> <p>The programs versatility allowed me to explore my strengths and build a well-rounded skillset for a diverse career. The honours component also gives an opportunity to develop advanced research skills and work alongside leading physiotherapy academics.</p><p> Ashleigh McKeon </p><p> Current student, Bachelor of Physiotherapy (Honours) </p><p>The honours component of this program helped build my confidence and clinical skills. I also appreciated the flexibility to choose between research or additional placement opportunities, allowing me to tailor my experience to align with my passions.</p><p> Benjamin Eo </p><p> Current student, Bachelor of Physiotherapy (Honours) </p><p>The simulated patient program was a highlight. It provided a safe and supportive environment to build confidence, and refine my clinical and interpersonal skills. It equipped me with the essential skills to step into my career ready to make a difference.</p><p> Jianqi (Jackie) Li </p><p> Current student, Bachelor of Physiotherapy (Honours) </p> <p><a href="/events">See all events</a></p> <a href="/events/uq-open-day"> UQ Open Day </a><p>2 August </p><h5> UQ Open Day </h5><p>St Lucia</p> <p><a href="/stories">See all stories</a></p> <a href="/stories/whats-it-like-studying-physiotherapy"> What’s it like to study physiotherapy at UQ? </a><p>Uni life</p><h5> What’s it like to study physiotherapy at UQ? </h5><p>7-minute read</p><a href="/stories/meet-expert-instilling-confidence-future-physiotherapists-dr-roma-forbes"> Meet the expert: instilling confidence in future physiotherapists with Dr Roma Forbes </a><p>UQ people</p><h5> Meet the expert: instilling confidence in future physiotherapists with Dr Roma Forbes </h5><p>3-minute read</p><a href="/stories/turning-her-curiosity-healthcare-career"> Turning her curiosity into a healthcare career </a><p>UQ people</p><h5> Turning her curiosity into a healthcare career </h5><p>4-minute read</p>',
    total_course_duration = '4 Years full-time',
    offshore_tuition_fee = 243808,
    onshore_tuition_fee = 42100,
    enrolment_fee = NULL,
