UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Overview</h4> <p> Build a strong scientific foundation while gaining the skills and flexibility to explore your passions and shape your own career path in science. </p><p>Challenge your scientific thinking and explore one of the broadest selections of science disciplines in Australia with this flexible and dynamic program.</p><p>Tailor your studies to your interests with an extensive range of specialist fields, gaining interdisciplinary knowledge and hands-on skills that prepare you for real-world impact.</p><p>Go beyond science by integrating skills from areas like languages, communication and design to expand your expertise and career options.</p><p>Gain practical experience across all years of your degree in a range of laboratories, including wet, dry, clinical and PC2/PC3 facilities, as well as animal diagnostic and training labs.</p><p>Build industry connections through internships, placements and global study experiences, or take your learning into the field with opportunities to study in iconic locations like:</p><ul><li>Heron Island Research Station on the Great Barrier Reef</li><li>Moreton Bay Research Station on Minjerribah (North Stradbroke Island)</li><li>Hidden Vale Wildlife Research Station</li><li>K’gari (Fraser Island).</li></ul><p>Graduate with a highly respected, globally recognised qualification, equipped with expert knowledge, technical proficiency, and the confidence to lead in your chosen field.</p><p><a href="#tab1">Domestic</a><a href="#tab2">International</a></p><p><a href="#entry-requirements">See full entry requirements</a></p>LocationSt LuciaDuration 3 Years (or part time equivalent)Start SemesterSemester 1 (22 Feb, 2027), Semester 2 (26 Jul, 2027)QTAC Code<p>731001</p>Program Code2461AQFLevel 7<p><a href="#overview">Dual programs available</a></p><p><a href="#how-to-apply">Admission schemes available</a></p><p><a href="#fees-scholarships">Scholarships available</a></p><p><a href="#entry-requirements">See full entry requirements</a></p>LocationSt LuciaFees<a href="#fees-scholarships">A$56800</a>Duration 3 Years Start Semester Semester 1 (22 Feb, 2027), Semester 2 (26 Jul, 2027) Semester dates for 2028 are yet to be confirmed QTAC Code<p>731001</p>Program Code2461CRICOS Code001961JAQFLevel 7<p><a href="#overview">Dual programs available</a></p><p><a href="#fees-scholarships">Scholarships available</a></p> <p> <h5> Program highlights </h5> </p> <p> <h5> Program highlights </h5> </p> <ul><li>Design your own study path by mixing science and non-science courses in your first year.</li><li>Explore 16 extended majors, 26 majors and 35 minors, all backed by cutting-edge research and industry insights.</li><li>Expand your expertise beyond science, with 46 minors in areas like languages, communication, design and economics.</li><li>Boost your career prospects by combining your degree with one of 13 programs, including law, education, arts, engineering, or business management.</li></ul> <p>18 in the world for environmental sciences</p><p>QS World University Rankings 2026</p> <p>26 in the world for agriculture and forestry</p><p>QS World University Rankings 2026</p> <p> <h5> Majors </h5> </p> <p>Tailor your studies to suit your goals. This program offers these options:</p><ul><li><p>Applied Mathematics</p></li><li><p>Applied Mathematics</p></li><li><p>Archaeological Science</p></li><li><p>Archaeological Science</p></li></ul><p><a href="#majors">See all majors</a></p> <p> <h5> How you''ll learn </h5> </p> <p>Your learning experiences are designed to best suit the learning outcomes of the courses you choose.</p><ul><li>Lectures</li><li>Tutorials</li><li>Work placements</li><li>Online study</li><li>Overseas study</li><li>Research experience</li><li>Laboratory work</li><li>Fieldwork</li><li>Seminars</li><li>Workshops</li></ul> <p> <h5> What you''ll study </h5> </p> <p>At UQ, degrees are called ''programs'' and subjects are called ''courses''. Here''s a sample of the courses you could study in this program:</p><ul><li>Theory &amp; Practice in Science [Core course]</li><li>Analysis of Scientific Data [Core course]</li><li>Nanomaterials &amp; Self-Assembled Systems [part of Chemistry major]</li><li>Environmental Bioanalytics [part of Environmental Science major] </li><li>Principles of Food Preservation [Part of Food Science and Nutrition major]</li><li>Thermodynamics &amp; Condensed Matter Physics [Part of Physics major]</li><li>Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Studies [Elective]</li></ul><p><a href="https://programs-courses.uq.edu.au/requirements/program/2461/2027">See courses and program structure</a></p> <p> <h5> Dual programs </h5> </p> <p>Double your skills and your opportunities with a dual degree. You can study the Bachelor of Science as a part of these dual programs:</p><ul><li><a href="/study-options/programs/bachelors-business-management-science-2335">Bachelors of Business Management / Science</a></li><li><a href="/study-options/programs/bachelors-commerce-science-2466">Bachelors of Commerce / Science</a></li><li><a href="/study-options/programs/bachelors-biomedical-science-science-2547">Bachelors of Biomedical Science / Science</a></li><li><a href="/study-options/programs/bachelors-science-education-secondary-2479">Bachelors of Science / Education (Secondary)</a></li><li><a href="/study-options/programs/bachelors-economics-science-2470">Bachelors of Economics / Science</a></li><li><a href="/study-options/programs/bachelors-computer-science-science-2566">Bachelors of Computer Science / Science</a></li><li><a href="/study-options/programs/bachelors-music-science-2538">Bachelors of Music / Science</a></li><li><a href="/study-options/programs/bachelors-mathematics-science-2502">Bachelors of Mathematics / Science</a></li><li><a href="/study-options/programs/bachelors-science-laws-honours-2472">Bachelors of Science / Laws (Honours)</a></li><li><a href="/study-options/programs/bachelors-science-arts-2478">Bachelors of Science / Arts</a></li><li><a href="/study-options/programs/bachelors-science-journalism-2496">Bachelors of Science / Journalism</a></li><li><a href="/study-options/programs/bachelors-engineering-honours-science-2493">Bachelors of Engineering (Honours) / Science</a></li></ul> <p> <h5> Career possibilities </h5> </p> <p>Our programs prepare you for your first job and beyond. Depending on which major you choose, here are some of the careers you could be on your way to:</p><ul><li>Sustainability adviser</li><li>Food chemist</li><li>Conservation officer</li><li>Bioinformatician</li><li>Meteorologist</li><li>Marine biologist</li><li>Bioanalytical scientist</li><li>Research officer</li><li>Materials scientist</li><li>Environment and resource manager</li></ul> <p>Average annual salary range</p><h5>Data Scientist</h5>$115–$135K<p>seek.com.au</p><p>Average annual salary range</p><h5>Environmental Scientist</h5>$90K–$110K<p>seek.com.au</p> <p> <h5> Next steps after graduation </h5> </p> <p>When you graduate, you''ll be in high demand by employers for your advanced technical, communication, independent thinking and problem-solving skills.</p><p>Depending on your major, you''ll have the pick of a broad range of career possibilities in areas including:</p><ul><li>academia and research</li><li>government</li><li>industry</li><li>finance</li><li>hospitals and health</li><li>marine preservation</li><li>environmental planning and site assessment</li><li>operations research and logistics</li><li>animal welfare and management.</li></ul><p>Alternatively, you can further your research ambitions by applying for the 12-month <a href="/study-options/programs/bachelor-science-honours-2031?year=2027">Bachelor of Science (Honours)</a> program.</p><p><a href="http://career-profiles.science.uq.edu.au/">Find out more about careers that started in science</a></p> <p>I absolutely loved the field trips that were part of my degree – especially the trip to UQ’s Research Station at Heron Island on the Great Barrier Reef.</p><p> Taylor Winckle </p><p> Graduate, Bachelor of Science </p><p>My degree gave me an appreciation that there are many things I don''t know or understand and encouraged me to hone the necessary skills for learning and problem solving.</p><p> Emily Jones </p><p> Graduate, Bachelor of Science (Mathematics) </p> <p><a href="/events">See all events</a></p> <a href="/events/uq-open-day"> UQ Open Day </a><p>2 August </p><h5> UQ Open Day </h5><p>St Lucia</p> <p><a href="/stories">See all stories</a></p> <a href="/stories/whats-it-really-study-science-uq"> What''s it really like to study science at UQ? </a><p>Uni life</p><h5> What''s it really like to study science at UQ? </h5><p>9-minute read</p><a href="/stories/what-jobs-can-you-do-bachelor-science"> What can you do with a Bachelor of Science? </a><p>Careers</p><h5> What can you do with a Bachelor of Science? </h5><p>7-minute read</p><a href="/stories/phd-story-florian-bachmann"> Florian’s PhD story: a new avenue for prostate cancer research </a><p>UQ people</p><h5> Florian’s PhD story: a new avenue for prostate cancer research </h5><p>4-minute read</p>',
    total_course_duration = '3 Years (or part time equivalent)',
    offshore_tuition_fee = 170400,
    onshore_tuition_fee = 29070,
    enrolment_fee = NULL,
    materials_fee = NULL,
    entry_requirements = '<h4>Entry Requirements</h4> <p> <h5> Prerequisites </h5> </p> Queensland Year 12 (or equivalent):<ul><li>General English subject (Units 3 &amp; 4, C)</li><li>Mathematical Methods (Units 3 &amp; 4, C); and,</li><li>one of Biology, Chemistry, Earth and Environmental Science or Physics (Units 3 &amp; 4, C)</li><li><strong>From Semester 1, 2028</strong>, Earth and Environmental Science will no longer be accepted.</li></ul> <h5> Minimum entry score </h5> <p>Select where you studied and your qualification to see the minimum entry score you need to be considered for this program.</p><p>Use the minimum entry score as a guide. Your score must be at least equivalent to the required Australian Year 12 ATAR score. Entry requirements are subject to change.</p> <h5>Equivalent subjects</h5> <table><thead><tr><th>Subject</th><th>Qualification equivalent</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table><p> <h5> English language requirements </h5> </p> <p>IELTS overall 6.5; reading 6; writing 6; speaking 6; listening 6. For other English Language Proficiency Tests and Scores approved for UQ</p><p>TOEFL iBT (including Paper Edition) - Overall 87, listening 19, reading 19, writing 21 and speaking 19.</p><p>PTE Academic - Overall Score of 64 and 60 in all sub bands.</p><p>BE - A minimum overall grade of 4 plus a minimum grade of C in all macro skills.</p><p>CES - Overall 176 and 169 in all sub bands.</p><p>OET is not accepted.</p><p>There are other ways to meet the English language requirements. For some programs, additional conditions apply.</p><p><a href="/admissions/english-language-requirements">Learn how to meet the English language requirements</a></p> <p> <h5> Student visas </h5> </p> <p>International students who are accepted into full-time study in the Bachelor of Science are eligible to apply for an Australian student visa (subclass 500).</p><p>There are a number of requirements you must satisfy before a visa is granted, including the Genuine Student (GS) requirement.</p><p><a href="/university-life/getting-prepared-to-come-to-australia/student-visas">Learn more about student visas</a></p> <p> <h5> Need help meeting the entry requirements? </h5> </p> <p>We can help you meet the minimum entry score, subject prerequisites or English language requirements for your preferred program.</p><p><a href="/admissions/undergraduate/consider-your-pathway-options">Learn about pathway options</a></p>',
    apply_form = 'https://study.uq.edu.au/study-options/programs/bachelor-science-2461',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '001961J';

-- ⚠️ Skipped (no CRICOS course code): Diploma in Science | https://study.uq.edu.au/study-options/programs/diploma-science-2476

UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Overview</h4> <p> Expand your expertise in mathematics, physics or statistics and meet the growing demand for high-level scientific skills. </p><p>The Graduate Diploma in Science is designed for graduates who have majored in mathematics, physics or statistics and want to deepen their knowledge.</p><p>In one year of full-time (or part-time equivalent) study, you’ll choose from a variety of courses, gaining specialised knowledge and valuable skills in your field.</p><p>UQ’s science program equips you for a rewarding career. </p><p>Many mathematics graduates pursue higher degrees and research roles at major institutions. Physics graduates develop sought-after analytical and problem-solving skills, valued across industries. Statistics graduates are in high demand in business, industry, research and government.</p><p><a href="#tab1">Domestic</a><a href="#tab2">International</a></p><p><a href="#entry-requirements">See full entry requirements</a></p><p>LocationSt LuciaDuration 1 Year full-time (or part-time equivalent) Start SemesterSemester 1 (22 Feb, 2027), Semester 2 (26 Jul, 2027)Program Code5240AQFLevel 8</p><p><a href="#fees-scholarships">Scholarships available</a></p><p><a href="#entry-requirements">See full entry requirements</a></p><p>LocationSt LuciaFees<a href="#fees-scholarships">A$60952</a>Duration 1 Year full-time Start Semester Semester 1 (22 Feb, 2027), Semester 2 (26 Jul, 2027) Semester dates for 2028 are yet to be confirmed Program Code5240CRICOS Code008585EAQFLevel 8</p><p><a href="#fees-scholarships">Scholarships available</a></p> <p> <h5> Program highlights </h5> </p> <p> <h5> Program highlights </h5> </p> <ul><li>Study at UQ''s Faculty of Science, renowned for teaching and research excellence.</li><li>Leverage UQ’s strong industry and government partnerships.</li><li>Apply your knowledge through collaborations, research projects, commercial ventures and industry placements. </li></ul> <p>1 in Queensland for physics and astronomy</p><p>QS World University Rankings 2026</p> <p>1 in Queensland for statistics and operational research</p><p>QS World University Rankings 2026</p> <p> <h5> Fields of study </h5> </p> <p>Tailor your studies to suit your goals. This program offers these options:</p><ul><li><p>Applied Mathematics</p></li><li><p>Mathematics</p></li><li><p>Physics</p></li><li><p>Statistics</p></li></ul><p><a href="#majors">See all fields of study</a></p> <p> <h5> How you''ll learn </h5> </p> <p>Your learning experiences are designed to best suit the learning outcomes of the courses you choose.</p><ul><li>Lectures</li><li>Tutorials</li><li>Laboratory work</li><li>Workshops</li></ul> <p> <h5> What you''ll study </h5> </p> <p>At UQ, degrees are called ''programs'' and subjects are called ''courses''. Here''s a sample of the courses you could study in this program:</p><ul><li>Statistical Analysis of Genetic Data [Elective]</li><li>Condensed Matter Physics [Elective]</li><li>Quantum Technologies [Elective]</li><li>Financial Calculus [Elective]</li><li>Machine Learning [Elective]</li></ul><p><a href="https://programs-courses.uq.edu.au/requirements/program/5240/2027">See courses and program structure</a></p> <p> <h5> Career possibilities </h5> </p> <p>Postgraduate study can take you anywhere. Depending on which field you choose, here are some of the careers you could be on your way to:</p><ul><li>Nuclear physicist</li><li>Industry researcher</li><li>Banking analyst</li><li>University academic</li><li>Health researcher</li><li>Computing specialist</li><li>Financial product developer</li><li>Asset and liability manager</li><li>Risk assessor</li><li>Quality control technician</li></ul> <p>Annual average salary range</p><h5>Risk Manager</h5>$140–$160K<p>seek.com.au</p><p>Average annual salary range</p><h5>Research Analyst</h5>$105–$120K<p>seek.com.au</p> <p> <h5> Next steps after graduation </h5> </p> <p>Your high-level knowledge and technical skills will be relevant to a range of modern careers.</p><p>You''ll be sought by industry for your excellent quantitative and problem-solving abilities, and gain a wide range of rewarding positions in the public and private sectors.</p><p>Alternatively, you can further your research ambitions and continue into the <a href="https://study.uq.edu.au/study-options/programs/master-science-5712?year=2027">Master of Science</a>.</p><p><a href="http://career-profiles.science.uq.edu.au/">Find out more about careers that started in science</a></p> <p>My science degree gave me a unique lens to look at the world. Critical thinking in a post-truth world has become a precious skill. Scientific literacy is more important than ever.</p><p> Karina Holden </p><p> Graduate, Graduate Diploma in Science </p> <p><a href="/events">See all events</a></p> <a href="/events/uq-open-day"> UQ Open Day </a><p>2 August </p><h5> UQ Open Day </h5><p>St Lucia</p> <p><a href="/stories">See all stories</a></p> <a href="/stories/graduate-diploma-vs-masters-degree"> Graduate diploma vs master’s degree </a><p>Study tips</p><h5> Graduate diploma vs master’s degree </h5><p>4-minute read</p><a href="/stories/uq-postgraduate-study-top-5-reasons"> Top 5 reasons to choose UQ for postgraduate study </a><p>Careers</p><h5> Top 5 reasons to choose UQ for postgraduate study </h5><p>3-minute read</p><a href="/stories/there-limit-challenges-we-can-solve-maths"> Making the greatest mathematical discoveries </a><p>UQ people</p><h5> Making the greatest mathematical discoveries </h5><p>3-minute read</p>',
    total_course_duration = '1 Year full-time (or part-time equivalent)',
    offshore_tuition_fee = 60952,
    onshore_tuition_fee = 5910,
    enrolment_fee = NULL,
    materials_fee = NULL,
    entry_requirements = '<h4>Entry Requirements</h4> <h5>Entry requirements</h5> <p>To be eligible for entry, you''ll need:</p> For the <strong>Mathematics</strong>, <strong>Applied Mathematics</strong>,and<strong> Statistics</strong> fields of study<strong>:</strong><ul><li>a bachelor''s degree (or equivalent) in any discipline with first-year university-level mathematics (including calculus, multi-variable calculus, linear algebra, and ordinary differential equations), or</li><li>5 years full-time equivalent, relevant work experience (see below).</li></ul><br/>You must have a grade point average (GPA) of 4.5 on a 7-point scale in your previous qualification.<br/>For the <strong>Physics </strong>field of study:<ul><li>a bachelor''s degree (or equivalent) in any discipline with first-year, university-level physics (including mechanics, thermal physics, electromagnetism, and modern physics), and first-year university-level mathematics (including calculus, multi-variable calculus, linear algebra, and ordinary differential equations), or</li><li>5 years full-time equivalent, relevant work experience (see below).</li></ul><br/>You must have a grade point average (GPA) of 4.5 on a 7-point scale in your previous qualification.<br/>Relevant work experience includes work in a related discipline, including data science, engineering or information technology.An assessment is made of the applicant''s background covering completion of, and performance in, relevant courses in their prior institution which provide the relevant pre-requisite knowledge. Students can provide further evidence in the form of a CV of their background.Final approval by the program coordinator. <p> <h5> GPA equivalent </h5> </p> <p>Select where you studied and your qualification to see the GPA equivalent you need to be considered for this program.</p><p>Use the GPA equivalent as a guide. When you apply, we’ll calculate your GPA using the UQ grading scale. Any failing grades will be included. Entry requirements are subject to change.</p> <h5>Equivalent subjects</h5> <table><thead><tr><th>Subject</th><th>Qualification equivalent</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table><p> <h5> Related programs </h5> </p> <p>Depending on your previous qualifications and current goals, you might want to consider<br/> one of these related programs:</p><ul><li><a href="/study-options/programs/master-science-5712">Master of Science</a></li></ul> <p> <h5> English language requirements </h5> </p> <p>IELTS overall 6.5; reading 6; writing 6; speaking 6; listening 6. For other English Language Proficiency Tests and Scores approved for UQ</p><p>TOEFL iBT (including Paper Edition) - Overall 87, listening 19, reading 19, writing 21 and speaking 19.</p><p>PTE Academic - Overall Score of 64 and 60 in all sub bands.</p><p>BE - A minimum overall grade of 4 plus a minimum grade of C in all macro skills.</p><p>CES - Overall 176 and 169 in all sub bands.</p><p>OET is not accepted.</p><p>There are other ways to meet the English language requirements. For some programs, additional conditions apply.</p><p><a href="/admissions/english-language-requirements">Learn how to meet the English language requirements</a></p> <p> <h5> Student visas </h5> </p> <p>International students who are accepted into full-time study in the Graduate Diploma in Science are eligible to apply for an Australian student visa (subclass 500).</p><p>There are a number of requirements you must satisfy before a visa is granted, including the Genuine Student (GS) requirement.</p><p><a href="/university-life/getting-prepared-to-come-to-australia/student-visas">Learn more about student visas</a></p>',
    apply_form = 'https://study.uq.edu.au/study-options/programs/graduate-diploma-science-5240',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '008585E';

UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Overview</h4> <p> Expand your expertise in mathematics, physics or statistics, and capitalise on the growing demand for advanced scientific skills. </p><p>The Master of Science is designed for graduates with first-year university-level knowledge in mathematics, physics or statistics.</p><p>Choose from a diverse range of courses tailored to your field, allowing you to customise your studies to align with your interests and career goals.</p><p>Apply your knowledge through collaborations on external research projects, industry placements, internships and commercial ventures.</p><p>You’ll also have opportunities to engage in research with leading centres, including Australian Research Council Centres of Excellence in:</p><ul><li>Engineered Quantum Systems (EQUS)</li><li>Quantum Biotechnology (QUBIC)</li><li>Gravitational Wave Discovery (OzGrav)</li><li>Plant Success in Nature and Agriculture</li><li>Quantum Computation and Communication Technology.</li></ul><p>Our graduates often pursue higher degrees and research roles at major institutions, with skills in high demand across various industries, business and government.</p><p><a href="#tab1">Domestic</a><a href="#tab2">International</a></p><p><a href="#entry-requirements">See full entry requirements</a></p><p>LocationSt LuciaDuration 1.5 Years full-time (or part-time equivalent) 2 Years full-time (or part-time equivalent) Start SemesterSemester 1 (22 Feb, 2027), Semester 2 (26 Jul, 2027)Program Code5712AQFLevel 9</p><p><a href="#fees-scholarships">Scholarships available</a></p><p><a href="#entry-requirements">See full entry requirements</a></p><p>LocationSt LuciaFees<a href="#fees-scholarships">A$60952</a>Duration 1.5 Years full-time (only available as full-time study) 2 Years full-time (only available as full-time study) Start Semester Semester 1 (22 Feb, 2027), Semester 2 (26 Jul, 2027) Semester dates for 2028 are yet to be confirmed Program Code5712CRICOS Code099432BAQFLevel 9</p><p><a href="#fees-scholarships">Scholarships available</a></p> <p> <h5> Program highlights </h5> </p> <p> <h5> Program highlights </h5> </p> <ul><li>Study at UQ''s Faculty of Science, globally recognised for teaching and research excellence.</li><li>Leverage UQ’s strong industry and government partnerships.</li><li>Apply your knowledge through collaborations, including external research projects, UQ research centres, commercial ventures and industry placements or internships.</li></ul> <p>1 in Queensland for statistics and operational research</p><p>QS World University Rankings 2026</p> <p>1 in Queensland for physics and astronomy</p><p>QS World University Rankings 2026</p> <p> <h5> Fields of study </h5> </p> <p>Tailor your studies to suit your goals. This program offers these options:</p><ul><li><p>Applied Mathematics</p></li><li><p>Mathematics</p></li><li><p>Physics</p></li><li><p>Statistics</p></li></ul><p><a href="#majors">See all fields of study</a></p> <p> <h5> How you''ll learn </h5> </p> <p>Your learning experiences are designed to best suit the learning outcomes of the courses you choose.</p><ul><li>Lectures</li><li>Tutorials</li><li>Work placements</li><li>Research experience</li><li>Laboratory work</li><li>Workshops</li></ul> <p> <h5> What you''ll study </h5> </p> <p>At UQ, degrees are called ''programs'' and subjects are called ''courses''. Here''s a sample of the courses you could study in this program:</p><ul><li>General Relativity [Core course]</li><li>Statistical Mechanics [Elective]</li><li>Coding &amp; Cryptography [Elective]</li><li>Natural Resource Mathematics [Elective]</li><li>Physics of Modern Technology [Elective]</li></ul><p><a href="https://programs-courses.uq.edu.au/requirements/program/5712/2027">See courses and program structure</a></p> <p> <h5> Career possibilities </h5> </p> <p>Postgraduate study can take you anywhere. Depending on which field you choose, here are some of the careers you could be on your way to:</p><ul><li>Scientific researcher</li><li>Banking analyst</li><li>University academic</li><li>Health researcher</li><li>Market risk manager</li><li>Investment analyst</li><li>Product developer</li><li>Quality controller</li><li>Finance analyst</li><li>Asset and liability manager</li></ul> <p>Annual average salary range</p><h5>Financial Analyst</h5>$100–$120K<p>seek.com.au</p><p>Average annual salary range</p><h5>Research Fellow</h5>$115–$135K<p>seek.com.au</p> <p> <h5> Next steps after graduation </h5> </p> <p>Your high-level knowledge and technical skills will be relevant to a range of careers.</p><p>You''ll be sought by industry for your excellent quantitative and problem-solving abilities, and gain a wide range of rewarding positions in the public and private sectors.</p><p>The Master of Science is also a pathway to PhD study.</p><p><a href="http://career-profiles.science.uq.edu.au/">Find out more about careers that started in science</a></p> <p>The lecturers and facilities here are outstanding, and the library is one of the best physical sciences libraries in the Southern Hemisphere. The course provided me with great preparation for a PhD. </p><p> Dr Jason Werry </p><p> Graduate, Master of Science in Mathematics </p> <p><a href="/events">See all events</a></p> <a href="/events/uq-open-day"> UQ Open Day </a><p>2 August </p><h5> UQ Open Day </h5><p>St Lucia</p> <p><a href="/stories">See all stories</a></p> <a href="/stories/it-worth-doing-masters-degree"> Is it worth doing a master’s degree? </a><p>Careers</p><h5> Is it worth doing a master’s degree? </h5><p>4-minute read</p><a href="/stories/uq-postgraduate-study-top-5-reasons"> Top 5 reasons to choose UQ for postgraduate study </a><p>Careers</p><h5> Top 5 reasons to choose UQ for postgraduate study </h5><p>3-minute read</p><a href="/stories/graduate-diploma-vs-masters-degree"> Graduate diploma vs master’s degree </a><p>Study tips</p><h5> Graduate diploma vs master’s degree </h5><p>4-minute read</p>',
    total_course_duration = '1.5 Years full-time (or part-time equivalent) 2 Years full-time (or part-time equivalent)',
    offshore_tuition_fee = 91428,
    onshore_tuition_fee = 8865,
    enrolment_fee = NULL,
    materials_fee = NULL,
    entry_requirements = '<h4>Entry Requirements</h4> <h5>Entry requirements</h5> <p>It''s possible to complete this degree in 2 years or 1.5 years depending on your qualifications and experience.</p><p>You can apply for any duration as long as you meet the entry requirements. You may also be eligible to apply for <a href="/admissions/postgraduate-coursework/check-credit-eligibility">credit or exemptions</a> to shorten your degree further. You''ll graduate with the same qualification no matter how long you take to complete the degree.</p> <h5>2-year degree (32 units of study)</h5><p>To be eligible to complete the degree in 2 years full-time (only available as full-time study), you''ll need:</p><p>For the <strong>Applied Mathematics</strong>, <strong>Mathematics</strong>, and <strong>Statistics</strong> field of study:</p><ul><li>a bachelor''s degree (or equivalent) in any discipline, with first-year university-level mathematics (including calculus, multi-variable calculus, linear algebra, and ordinary differential equations), or</li><li>a graduate diploma in science, or</li><li>to have successfully completed 3 years of study towards an approved qualification at an overseas partner institution, with a formal pathway to the Master of Science.</li></ul><p>For the <strong>Physics</strong> field of study:</p><ul><li>a bachelor''s degree (or equivalent) in any discipline, with first-year university-level physics (including mechanics, thermal physics, electromagnetism, and modern physics) and first-year university-level mathematics (including calculus, multi-variable calculus, linear algebra, and ordinary differential equations), or</li><li>a graduate diploma in science, or</li><li>to have successfully completed 3 years of study towards an approved qualification at an overseas partner institution, with a formal pathway to the Master of Science.</li></ul><p><br/></p><p>You must have a grade point average (GPA) of 5.0 on a 7-point scale in your previous qualification.</p><h5>1.5-year degree (24 units of study)</h5><p>If you have relevant prior learning or experience, you can reduce the number of courses you need to complete and graduate in less time.</p><p>To be eligible to complete the degree in 1.5 years full-time (only available as full-time study), you''ll need:</p><ul><li>a bachelor''s degree (or equivalent) in mathematics, statistics or physics, or</li><li>to have successfully completed at least 3.5 years of study towards an approved qualification at an overseas partner institution, including research requirements, with a formal pathway to the Master of Science.</li></ul><p><br/></p><p>You must have a grade point average (GPA) of 5.0 on a 7-point scale in your previous qualification.</p> <p> <h5> GPA equivalent </h5> </p> <p>Select where you studied and your qualification to see the GPA equivalent you need to be considered for this program.</p><p>Use the GPA equivalent as a guide. When you apply, we’ll calculate your GPA using the UQ grading scale. Any failing grades will be included. Entry requirements are subject to change.</p> <h5>Equivalent subjects</h5> <table><thead><tr><th>Subject</th><th>Qualification equivalent</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table><p> <h5> Related programs </h5> </p> <p>Depending on your previous qualifications and current goals, you might want to consider<br/> one of these related programs:</p><ul><li><a href="/study-options/programs/graduate-diploma-science-5240">Graduate Diploma in Science</a></li></ul> <p> <h5> English language requirements </h5> </p> <p>IELTS overall 6.5; reading 6; writing 6; speaking 6; listening 6. For other English Language Proficiency Tests and Scores approved for UQ</p><p>TOEFL iBT (including Paper Edition) - Overall 87, listening 19, reading 19, writing 21 and speaking 19.</p><p>PTE Academic - Overall Score of 64 and 60 in all sub bands.</p><p>BE - A minimum overall grade of 4 plus a minimum grade of C in all macro skills.</p><p>CES - Overall 176 and 169 in all sub bands.</p><p>OET is not accepted.</p><p>There are other ways to meet the English language requirements. For some programs, additional conditions apply.</p><p><a href="/admissions/english-language-requirements">Learn how to meet the English language requirements</a></p> <p> <h5> Student visas </h5> </p> <p>International students who are accepted into full-time study in the Master of Science are eligible to apply for an Australian student visa (subclass 500).</p><p>There are a number of requirements you must satisfy before a visa is granted, including the Genuine Student (GS) requirement.</p><p><a href="/university-life/getting-prepared-to-come-to-australia/student-visas">Learn more about student visas</a></p> <p> <h5> Additional application information </h5> </p> <p> Your prerequisite knowledge will be assessed by a review of your completion and performance in relevant courses in prior studies. You can provide further evidence of prerequisite knowledge by submitting a CV. The Program Coordinator is the final approver. </p>',
    apply_form = 'https://study.uq.edu.au/study-options/programs/master-science-5712',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '099432B';

UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Overview</h4> <p> Craft a degree as unique as your ambitions by combining arts and science specialisations in this flexible 4-year dual program. </p><p>With one of the broadest selections of majors in Australia—from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander studies to zoology—you can tailor your studies to match your interests and career goals.</p><p>Build expertise in foreign languages alongside science to unlock global career opportunities, or blend computational and environmental studies to tackle pressing issues like climate change and food security.</p><p>Enhance your studies further with a concurrent diploma in languages, and open the door to honours opportunities in science or arts after graduation.</p><p>Whatever path you choose, you''ll be in high demand by employers for your advanced technical, communication, independent thinking and problem-solving skills.</p><p><a href="#tab1">Domestic</a><a href="#tab2">International</a></p><p><a href="#entry-requirements">See full entry requirements</a></p>LocationSt LuciaDuration 4 Years (or part time equivalent)Start SemesterSemester 1 (22 Feb, 2027), Semester 2 (26 Jul, 2027)QTAC Code<p>731501</p>Program Code2478AQFLevel 7<p><a href="#how-to-apply">Admission schemes available</a></p><p><a href="#fees-scholarships">Scholarships available</a></p><p><a href="#entry-requirements">See full entry requirements</a></p>LocationSt LuciaFees<a href="#fees-scholarships">A$56800</a>Duration 4 Years Start Semester Semester 1 (22 Feb, 2027), Semester 2 (26 Jul, 2027) Semester dates for 2028 are yet to be confirmed QTAC Code<p>731501</p>Program Code2478CRICOS Code013827EAQFLevel 7<p><a href="#fees-scholarships">Scholarships available</a></p> <p> <h5> Program highlights </h5> </p> <p> <h5> Program highlights </h5> </p> <ul><li>Study at a university with more national teaching awards than any other Australian university..</li><li>Explore over 80 study areas across science, arts, humanities and languages.</li><li>Develop advanced creative and analytical skills to excel in diverse careers.</li><li>Discover endless opportunities with a dual degree that prepares you for any future.</li></ul> <p>3 in Australia for social sciences and humanities</p><p>CWTS Leiden Ranking 2025</p> <p>1 in Australia for environmental sciences</p><p>QS World University Rankings 2026</p> <p> <h5> Majors </h5> </p> <p>Tailor your studies to suit your goals. This program offers these options:</p><ul><li><p>Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Studies</p></li><li><p>Ancient Greek</p></li><li><p>Ancient History</p></li><li><p>Ancient History/History</p></li></ul><p><a href="#majors">See all majors</a></p> <p> <h5> How you''ll learn </h5> </p> <p>Your learning experiences are designed to best suit the learning outcomes of the courses you choose.</p><ul><li>Lectures</li><li>Tutorials</li><li>Overseas study</li><li>Laboratory work</li><li>Fieldwork</li><li>Workshops</li></ul> <p> <h5> What you''ll study </h5> </p> <p>At UQ, degrees are called ''programs'' and subjects are called ''courses''.</p><p><a href="https://programs-courses.uq.edu.au/requirements/program/2478/2027">See courses and program structure</a></p><p><a href="https://www.uq.edu.au/study/docs/dual-degree-planners-2027/2027-Bachelors-of-Science-Arts-2478.pdf">View dual degree planner (PDF)</a></p> <p> <h5> Career possibilities </h5> </p> <p>Our programs prepare you for your first job and beyond. Depending on which major you choose, here are some of the careers you could be on your way to:</p><ul><li>Environmental and science communicator</li><li>Museum administrator</li><li>Materials scientist</li><li>Heritage consultant</li><li>Quantitative researcher</li><li>Content producer</li><li>Marine research officer</li><li>Gallery curator</li><li>Sustainability adviser</li><li>Cultural heritage consultant</li></ul> <p>Average annual salary range</p><h5>Environmental Scientist</h5>$90K–$110K<p>seek.com.au</p><p>Average annual salary range</p><h5>Zoologist</h5>$95K–$115K<p>seek.com.au</p> <p> <h5> Next steps after graduation </h5> </p> <p>After graduating with 2 highly respected degrees, you’ll have the pick of a broad range of career possibilities around the world.</p><p><a href="http://career-profiles.science.uq.edu.au/">Find out more about careers that started in science</a></p> <p>My studies have provided me with the opportunity to explore many different areas that I am passionate about. The skills I have learnt in the arts are useful and transferable to my science courses and in everyday life. </p><p> Raluca Ghebosu </p><p> Graduate, Bachelors of Science / Arts </p><p>I chose to study at UQ because of its highly regarded reputation. I was accepted into UQ’s Advanced Study Program in Science where I had the opportunity to gain vital research experience during my undergraduate years. </p><p> Jasmine Ngo </p><p> Graduate, Bachelors of Science / Arts </p><p>I chose UQ because of the flexibility that was offered in terms of studies. This program allowed me to study both Biomedical Science and Psychology and choose from a wide range of interesting courses that I could not have done elsewhere.</p><p> Montana Samantzis </p><p> Graduate, Bachelor of Science/Bachelor of Arts (Biomedical Science and Psychology) </p><p>I chose UQ as it''s well known for offering great science education plus it offered a dual degree, allowing me to follow my curiosity in science and pursue my deep interest and fascination with Japanese language, literature and culture.</p><p> Susan May </p><p> Graduate, Bachelors of Science (Geological Science) / Arts (Japanese) </p> <p><a href="/events">See all events</a></p> <a href="/events/ancient-history-experience-day"> Ancient History Experience Day </a><p>15 July </p><h5> Ancient History Experience Day </h5><p>St Lucia</p><a href="/events/world-religions-experience-day-2026"> World Religions Experience Day 2026 </a><p>22 July - 23 July </p><h5> World Religions Experience Day 2026 </h5><p>St Lucia</p><a href="/events/uq-open-day"> UQ Open Day </a><p>2 August </p><h5> UQ Open Day </h5><p>St Lucia</p> <p><a href="/stories">See all stories</a></p> <a href="/stories/whats-it-really-study-science-uq"> What''s it really like to study science at UQ? </a><p>Uni life</p><h5> What''s it really like to study science at UQ? </h5><p>9-minute read</p><a href="/stories/whats-it-really-study-arts-uq"> What''s it really like to study arts at UQ? </a><p>Uni life</p><h5> What''s it really like to study arts at UQ? </h5><p>6-minute read</p><a href="/stories/why-uq-world-top-50-university"> Why is UQ a world top 50 university? </a><p>Uni life</p><h5> Why is UQ a world top 50 university? </h5><p>4-minute read</p>',
    total_course_duration = '4 Years (or part time equivalent)',
    offshore_tuition_fee = 227200,
    onshore_tuition_fee = 43660,
    enrolment_fee = NULL,
    materials_fee = NULL,
    entry_requirements = '<h4>Entry Requirements</h4> <p> <h5> Prerequisites </h5> </p> <ul><li>Queensland Year 12 (or equivalent) General English subject (Units 3 &amp; 4, C)</li><li>Mathematical Methods (Units 3 &amp; 4, C); and</li><li>one of Biology, Chemistry, Earth and Environmental Science or Physics (Units 3 &amp; 4, C)</li><li><strong>From Semester 1, 2028</strong>, Earth and Environmental Science will no longer be accepted.</li></ul> <p> <h5> Minimum entry score </h5> </p> <p>Select where you studied and your qualification to see the minimum entry score you need to be considered for this program.</p><p>Use the minimum entry score as a guide. Your score must be at least equivalent to the required Australian Year 12 ATAR score. Entry scores are reviewed each year.</p> <h5>Equivalent subjects</h5> <table><thead><tr><th>Subject</th><th>Qualification equivalent</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table><p> <h5> English language requirements </h5> </p> <p>IELTS overall 6.5; reading 6; writing 6; speaking 6; listening 6. For other English Language Proficiency Tests and Scores approved for UQ</p><p>TOEFL iBT (including Paper Edition) - Overall 87, listening 19, reading 19, writing 21 and speaking 19.</p><p>PTE Academic - Overall Score of 64 and 60 in all sub bands.</p><p>BE - A minimum overall grade of 4 plus a minimum grade of C in all macro skills.</p><p>CES - Overall 176 and 169 in all sub bands.</p><p>OET is not accepted.</p><p>There are other ways to meet the English language requirements. For some programs, additional conditions apply.</p><p><a href="/admissions/english-language-requirements">Learn how to meet the English language requirements</a></p> <p> <h5> Student visas </h5> </p> <p>International students who are accepted into full-time study in the Bachelors of Science / Arts are eligible to apply for an Australian student visa (subclass 500).</p><p>There are a number of requirements you must satisfy before a visa is granted, including the Genuine Student (GS) requirement.</p><p><a href="/university-life/getting-prepared-to-come-to-australia/student-visas">Learn more about student visas</a></p> <p> <h5> Need help meeting the entry requirements? </h5> </p> <p>We can help you meet the minimum entry score, subject prerequisites or English language requirements for your preferred program.</p><p><a href="/admissions/undergraduate/consider-your-pathway-options">Learn about pathway options</a></p>',
    apply_form = 'https://study.uq.edu.au/study-options/programs/bachelors-science-arts-2478',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '013827E';

UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Overview</h4> <p> Turn your passion for science into a rewarding career in secondary education. </p><p>This 4-year dual degree equips you with deep scientific knowledge and the skills to inspire the next generation.</p><p>You''ll gain expertise in 2 teaching areas through the Bachelor of Science, while the Bachelor of Education (Secondary) provides the professional training, hands-on experience, and qualifications needed for teacher registration.</p><p>With school-based learning and research-backed teaching methods, you''ll graduate ready for the classroom—or for roles in business and industry training.</p><p>The science component offers one of Australia’s broadest selections of disciplines, allowing you to tailor your studies to your interests while building interdisciplinary expertise and practical skills.</p><p><a href="#tab1">Domestic</a><a href="#tab2">International</a></p><p><a href="#entry-requirements">See full entry requirements</a></p>LocationSt LuciaDuration 4 Years (or part time equivalent)Start SemesterSemester 1 (22 Feb, 2027), Semester 2 (26 Jul, 2027)QTAC Code<p>731302</p>Program Code2479AQFLevel 7<p><a href="#how-to-apply">Admission schemes available</a></p><p><a href="#fees-scholarships">Scholarships available</a></p><p><a href="#entry-requirements">See full entry requirements</a></p>LocationSt LuciaFees<a href="#fees-scholarships">A$56800</a>Duration 4 Years Start Semester Semester 1 (22 Feb, 2027) Semester dates for 2028 are yet to be confirmed QTAC Code<p>731302</p>Program Code2479CRICOS Code061063BAQFLevel 7<p><a href="#fees-scholarships">Scholarships available</a></p> <p> <h5> Program highlights </h5> </p> <p> <h5> Program highlights </h5> </p> <ul><li>Earn 2 degrees and expertise in multiple science teaching areas. </li><li>Gain classroom experience, with placements available from early in your degree. </li><li>Graduate with high-level teaching ability and a wide range of scientific skills, ready to excel in a challenging and rewarding profession.</li></ul> <p>41 in the world for education</p><p>QS World University Rankings 2026</p> <p>1 in Queensland for education and training</p><p>QS World University Rankings 2026</p> <p> <h5> Majors </h5> </p> <p>Tailor your studies to suit your goals. This program offers these options:</p><ul><li><p>Applied Mathematics</p></li><li><p>Applied Mathematics</p></li><li><p>Astrophysics</p></li><li><p>Biochemistry and Molecular Biology</p></li></ul><p><a href="#majors">See all majors</a></p> <p> <h5> How you''ll learn </h5> </p> <p>Your learning experiences are designed to best suit the learning outcomes of the courses you choose.</p><ul><li>Lectures</li><li>Tutorials</li><li>Work placements</li><li>Laboratory work</li><li>Fieldwork</li><li>Seminars</li><li>Workshops</li></ul> <p> <h5> Placements and work experience </h5> </p> <p>Students undertaking a Bachelor of Science/Bachelor of Education (Secondary) dual program must complete a minimum of 80 days of supervised and assessed professional experience throughout the program. Students must enrol full-time in Professional Year Courses in their final year of study.</p><p>Every effort is made to place students within a reasonable distance of their home base, but they can be expected to travel up to 90 minutes due to public transport connections and incur costs associated with travel and possible lost income over this period.</p><p>Students are generally placed at Ipswich, Brisbane, and southeast Queensland and are encouraged to explore the option of a rural placement. Financial assistance may be available to assist with travel and accommodation costs for rural placements.</p><p>Students are required to have a current Blue Card (Working with Children Check) before commencing practicum. The Professional Experience Handbook for this program provides information about practicum and school experience requirements. Please visit the <a href="https://education.uq.edu.au/professional-experience-pex/students-0">School of Education website</a> to access required resources.</p> <p> <h5> What you''ll study </h5> </p> <p>At UQ, degrees are called ''programs'' and subjects are called ''courses''.</p><p><a href="https://programs-courses.uq.edu.au/requirements/program/2479/2027">See courses and program structure</a></p><p><a href="https://www.uq.edu.au/study/docs/dual-degree-planners-2027/2027-Bachelors-of-Science-Education-Secondary-2479.pdf">View dual degree planner (PDF)</a></p> <p> <h5> Career possibilities </h5> </p> <p>Our programs prepare you for your first job and beyond. Depending on which major you choose, here are some of the careers you could be on your way to:</p><ul><li>Secondary school teacher</li><li>School laboratory technician</li><li>School curriculum adviser</li><li>Head of curriculum</li><li>Science technician</li><li>Middle school teacher</li></ul> <p>Average annual salary range</p><h5>Science Teacher</h5>$105–$110K<p>seek.com.au</p><p>Average annual salary range</p><h5>Laboratory Supervisor</h5>$105–$125K<p>seek.com.au</p> <p> <h5> Next steps after graduation </h5> </p> <p>You''ll be eligible to apply for registration as a teacher with the Queensland College of Teachers, and to work as a school teacher in state and independent schools in Australia and worldwide.</p><p>Further study and experience can lead to roles as a head of department, principal, guidance officer, learning support teacher or student adviser.</p><p>Other graduates choose to work with non-school-based education providers (such as tutoring companies), government agencies or education advocacy organisations.</p> <p> <h5> Professional memberships </h5> </p> <p>When you graduate, you may be eligible for memberships with the following professional organisations. Contact the organisation to find out how to become a member.</p><ul><li>Queensland College of Teachers</li></ul> <p> <h5> Professional registration </h5> </p> <p>When you graduate, you may be eligible for registration with the following professional organisations. Contact the organisation to find out how to register.</p><ul><li>Queensland College Of Teachers</li></ul> <p> <h5> Program accreditation </h5> </p> <p>The Bachelors of Science / Education (Secondary) is accredited by:</p><ul><li>Australian Institute For Teaching And School Leadership</li></ul> <p>Thanks to UQ’s program and supportive staff, I felt unbelievably prepared and excited to start teaching and helping students learn about science and themselves.</p><p> Matthew Gover </p><p> Bachelor of Science / Bachelor of Education (Secondary) </p> <p><a href="/events">See all events</a></p> <a href="/events/uq-open-day"> UQ Open Day </a><p>2 August </p><h5> UQ Open Day </h5><p>St Lucia</p><a href="/events/master-teaching-information-webinar"> Master of Teaching information webinar </a><p>20 October </p><h5> Master of Teaching information webinar </h5><p>Online</p><a href="/events/postgraduate-educational-studies-information-webinar"> Postgraduate educational studies information webinar </a><p>3 November </p><h5> Postgraduate educational studies information webinar </h5><p>Online</p> <p><a href="/stories">See all stories</a></p> <a href="/stories/whats-it-really-study-science-uq"> What''s it really like to study science at UQ? </a><p>Uni life</p><h5> What''s it really like to study science at UQ? </h5><p>9-minute read</p><a href="/stories/why-be-a-teacher"> Why be a teacher? </a><p>Careers</p><h5> Why be a teacher? </h5><p>4-minute read</p><a href="/stories/why-uq-world-top-50-university"> Why is UQ a world top 50 university? </a><p>Uni life</p><h5> Why is UQ a world top 50 university? </h5><p>4-minute read</p>',
    total_course_duration = '4 Years (or part time equivalent)',
    offshore_tuition_fee = 227200,
    onshore_tuition_fee = 28620,
    enrolment_fee = NULL,
    materials_fee = NULL,
    entry_requirements = '<h4>Entry Requirements</h4> <p> <h5> Prerequisites </h5> </p> Queensland Year 12 (or equivalent):<ul><li>General English subject (Units 3 &amp; 4, C);</li><li>Mathematical Methods (Units 3 &amp; 4, C);</li><li>and one of Biology, Chemistry, Earth and Environmental Science, or Physics (Units 3 &amp; 4, C).</li><li><strong>From Semester 1, 2028</strong>, Earth and Environmental Science will no longer be accepted.</li></ul> <p> <h5> Minimum entry score </h5> </p> <p>Select where you studied and your qualification to see the minimum entry score you need to be considered for this program.</p><p>Use the minimum entry score as a guide. Your score must be at least equivalent to the required Australian Year 12 ATAR score. Entry scores are reviewed each year.</p> <h5>Equivalent subjects</h5> <table><thead><tr><th>Subject</th><th>Qualification equivalent</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table><p> <h5> English language requirements </h5> </p> <p>IELTS score of 7.5 overall; speaking 8; listening 8, reading 7, writing 7. For other English Language Proficiency Tests and Scores approved for UQ.</p><p>TOEFL iBT (Paper Edition), PTE Academic, BE, CES, and OET are not accepted.</p><p>There are other ways to meet the English language requirements. For some programs, additional conditions apply.</p><p><a href="/admissions/english-language-requirements">Learn how to meet the English language requirements</a></p> <p> <h5> Inherent requirements </h5> </p> <p>To complete this degree, you have to meet its inherent requirements by demonstrating essential skills and attributes. Read the inherent requirements before you apply.</p><p><a href="/admissions/inherent-requirements/inherent-requirements-education-programs">Learn about inherent requirements</a></p> <p> <h5> Student visas </h5> </p> <p>International students who are accepted into full-time study in the Bachelors of Science / Education (Secondary) are eligible to apply for an Australian student visa (subclass 500).</p><p>There are a number of requirements you must satisfy before a visa is granted, including the Genuine Student (GS) requirement.</p><p><a href="/university-life/getting-prepared-to-come-to-australia/student-visas">Learn more about student visas</a></p> <p> <h5> Need help meeting the entry requirements? </h5> </p> <p>We can help you meet the minimum entry score, subject prerequisites or English language requirements for your preferred program.</p><p><a href="/admissions/undergraduate/consider-your-pathway-options">Learn about pathway options</a></p>',
    apply_form = 'https://study.uq.edu.au/study-options/programs/bachelors-science-education-secondary-2479',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '061063B';

UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Overview</h4> <p> Combine the analytical precision of science with the storytelling power of journalism and prepare for a dynamic career. </p><p>This 4-year dual degree equips you with expertise in scientific research and media communication, opening doors to diverse opportunities.</p><p>The Bachelor of Science offers one of Australia’s broadest discipline selections, allowing you to tailor your studies with single, extended, or dual majors. Gain hands-on experience through internships, industry placements and global study opportunities.</p><p>The Bachelor of Journalism provides professional training in media and communication, developing your skills in reporting, analysis and storytelling.</p><p>With a unique blend of scientific and journalistic expertise, you’ll graduate ready to thrive in an evolving job market, where you''ll be in demand for your technical, communication, independent thinking and problem-solving skills.</p><p><a href="#tab1">Domestic</a><a href="#tab2">International</a></p><p><a href="#entry-requirements">See full entry requirements</a></p>LocationSt LuciaDuration 4 Years (or part time equivalent)Start SemesterSemester 1 (22 Feb, 2027), Semester 2 (26 Jul, 2027)QTAC Code<p>731602</p>Program Code2496AQFLevel 7<p><a href="#how-to-apply">Admission schemes available</a></p><p><a href="#fees-scholarships">Scholarships available</a></p><p><a href="#entry-requirements">See full entry requirements</a></p>LocationSt LuciaFees<a href="#fees-scholarships">A$56800</a>Duration 4 Years Start Semester Semester 1 (22 Feb, 2027), Semester 2 (26 Jul, 2027) Semester dates for 2028 are yet to be confirmed QTAC Code<p>731602</p>Program Code2496CRICOS Code043735EAQFLevel 7<p><a href="#fees-scholarships">Scholarships available</a></p> <p> <h5> Program highlights </h5> </p> <p> <h5> Program highlights </h5> </p> <ul><li>Study at a university with more national teaching awards than any other Australian university.</li><li>Tailor your science studies with 16 extended majors, 26 majors and 35 minors, all backed by cutting-edge research and industry insights.</li><li>Explore new digital frontiers in journalism, drawing on interviews, complex data analysis, observation and research to produce rich media content.</li><li>Gain a competitive edge with this unique dual degree.</li></ul> <p>1 in Australia for environmental sciences</p><p>QS World University Rankings 2026</p> <p>1 in Queensland for arts and humanities</p><p>QS World University Rankings 2026</p> <p> <h5> Majors </h5> </p> <p>Tailor your studies to suit your goals. This program offers these options:</p><ul><li><p>Applied Mathematics</p></li><li><p>Applied Mathematics</p></li><li><p>Archaeological Science</p></li><li><p>Archaeological Science</p></li></ul><p><a href="#majors">See all majors</a></p> <p> <h5> How you''ll learn </h5> </p> <p>Your learning experiences are designed to best suit the learning outcomes of the courses you choose.</p><ul><li>Lectures</li><li>Tutorials</li><li>Overseas study</li><li>Research experience</li><li>Laboratory work</li><li>Fieldwork</li><li>Studios</li></ul> <p> <h5> What you''ll study </h5> </p> <p>At UQ, degrees are called ''programs'' and subjects are called ''courses''.</p><p><a href="https://programs-courses.uq.edu.au/requirements/program/2496/2027">See courses and program structure</a></p><p><a href="https://www.uq.edu.au/study/docs/dual-degree-planners-2027/2027-Bachelors-of-Science-Journalism-2496.pdf">View dual degree planner (PDF)</a></p> <p> <h5> Career possibilities </h5> </p> <p>Our programs prepare you for your first job and beyond. Depending on which major you choose, here are some of the careers you could be on your way to:</p><ul><li>Environmental and science communicator</li><li>Correspondent/Journalist</li><li>Science technician</li><li>Digital content producer</li><li>Journalist</li><li>Foreign media correspondent</li><li>Science writer and editor</li><li>Content writer</li><li>Social media manager</li><li>Broadcaster</li></ul> <p>Average annual salary range</p><h5>Technical Writer</h5>$95K–$115K<p>seek.com.au</p><p>Average annual salary range</p><h5>Communications Adviser</h5>$105–$115K<p>seek.com.au</p> <p> <h5> Next steps after graduation </h5> </p> <p>After graduating with 2 highly respected degrees, you’ll have the pick of a broad range of career possibilities around the world.</p><p><a href="http://career-profiles.science.uq.edu.au/">Find out more about careers that started in science</a></p> <p>Studying journalism has helped me to visualise storylines and come up with alternative narratives. By combining science (the ''analytical'') with journalism (the ''creative''), my studies put me in good stead for a career in factual television. </p><p> Abi Lees </p><p> Graduate, Bachelors of Science / Journalism </p> <p><a href="/events">See all events</a></p> <a href="/events/ancient-history-experience-day"> Ancient History Experience Day </a><p>15 July </p><h5> Ancient History Experience Day </h5><p>St Lucia</p><a href="/events/world-religions-experience-day-2026"> World Religions Experience Day 2026 </a><p>22 July - 23 July </p><h5> World Religions Experience Day 2026 </h5><p>St Lucia</p><a href="/events/uq-open-day"> UQ Open Day </a><p>2 August </p><h5> UQ Open Day </h5><p>St Lucia</p> <p><a href="/stories">See all stories</a></p> <a href="/stories/whats-it-really-study-science-uq"> What''s it really like to study science at UQ? </a><p>Uni life</p><h5> What''s it really like to study science at UQ? </h5><p>9-minute read</p><a href="/stories/is-a-journalism-degree-worth-it"> Is a journalism degree worth it? </a><p>Study tips</p><h5> Is a journalism degree worth it? </h5><p>10-minute read</p><a href="/stories/why-uq-world-top-50-university"> Why is UQ a world top 50 university? </a><p>Uni life</p><h5> Why is UQ a world top 50 university? </h5><p>4-minute read</p>',
    total_course_duration = '4 Years (or part time equivalent)',
    offshore_tuition_fee = 227200,
    onshore_tuition_fee = 51480,
    enrolment_fee = NULL,
    materials_fee = NULL,
    entry_requirements = '<h4>Entry Requirements</h4> <p> <h5> Prerequisites </h5> </p> <ul><li>Queensland Year 12 (or equivalent) General English subject (Units 3 &amp; 4, C)</li><li>Mathematical Methods (Units 3 &amp; 4, C); and</li><li>one of Biology, Chemistry, Earth and Environmental Science or Physics (Units 3 &amp; 4, C)</li><li><strong>From Semester 1, 2028</strong>, Earth and Environmental Science will no longer be accepted.</li></ul> <p> <h5> Minimum entry score </h5> </p> <p>Select where you studied and your qualification to see the minimum entry score you need to be considered for this program.</p><p>Use the minimum entry score as a guide. Your score must be at least equivalent to the required Australian Year 12 ATAR score. Entry scores are reviewed each year.</p> <h5>Equivalent subjects</h5> <table><thead><tr><th>Subject</th><th>Qualification equivalent</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table><p> <h5> English language requirements </h5> </p> <p>IELTS overall 6.5; reading 6; writing 6; speaking 6; listening 6. For other English Language Proficiency Tests and Scores approved for UQ</p><p>TOEFL iBT (including Paper Edition) - Overall 87, listening 19, reading 19, writing 21 and speaking 19.</p><p>PTE Academic - Overall Score of 64 and 60 in all sub bands.</p><p>BE - A minimum overall grade of 4 plus a minimum grade of C in all macro skills.</p><p>CES - Overall 176 and 169 in all sub bands.</p><p>OET is not accepted.</p><p>There are other ways to meet the English language requirements. For some programs, additional conditions apply.</p><p><a href="/admissions/english-language-requirements">Learn how to meet the English language requirements</a></p> <p> <h5> Student visas </h5> </p> <p>International students who are accepted into full-time study in the Bachelors of Science / Journalism are eligible to apply for an Australian student visa (subclass 500).</p><p>There are a number of requirements you must satisfy before a visa is granted, including the Genuine Student (GS) requirement.</p><p><a href="/university-life/getting-prepared-to-come-to-australia/student-visas">Learn more about student visas</a></p> <p> <h5> Need help meeting the entry requirements? </h5> </p> <p>We can help you meet the minimum entry score, subject prerequisites or English language requirements for your preferred program.</p><p><a href="/admissions/undergraduate/consider-your-pathway-options">Learn about pathway options</a></p>',
    apply_form = 'https://study.uq.edu.au/study-options/programs/bachelors-science-journalism-2496',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '043735E';

UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Overview</h4> <p> Develop the expertise to thrive in a science and technology-driven economy while building a strong foundation in law. </p><p>Gain in-demand technical skills by combining scientific study with a practical understanding of legal principles.</p><p>As a Bachelor of Science student, you’ll have the flexibility to explore a broad range of disciplines before specialising in a major.</p><p>The Bachelor of Laws (Honours) builds your legal expertise through interactive, seminar-style classes that encourage collaboration, critical thinking and debate. You''ll acquire a deep understanding of core areas such as contracts, torts, criminal law and property, alongside elective options to tailor your studies.</p><p>Graduating with an internationally respected law degree and advanced scientific knowledge will set you apart in a competitive job market and open pathways for research or further study.</p><p><a href="#tab1">Domestic</a><a href="#tab2">International</a></p><p><a href="#entry-requirements">See full entry requirements</a></p>LocationSt LuciaDuration 5 Years (or part time equivalent)Start SemesterSemester 1 (22 Feb, 2027)QTAC Code<p>731401</p>Program Code2472AQFLevel 8<p><a href="#how-to-apply">Admission schemes available</a></p><p><a href="#fees-scholarships">Scholarships available</a></p><p><a href="#entry-requirements">See full entry requirements</a></p>LocationSt LuciaFees<a href="#fees-scholarships">A$56800</a>Duration 5 Years Start Semester Semester 1 (22 Feb, 2027) Semester dates for 2028 are yet to be confirmed QTAC Code<p>731401</p>Program Code2472CRICOS Code103167JAQFLevel 8<p><a href="#fees-scholarships">Scholarships available</a></p> <p> <h5> Program highlights </h5> </p> <p> <h5> Program highlights </h5> </p> <ul><li>Learn in world-class facilities with cutting-edge teaching and research spaces.</li><li>Gain real-world skills in a top-tier laws program that blends theory with active learning.</li><li>Study at a globally recognised school known for excellence in teaching and research.</li><li>Meet the academic requirements for legal practice across Australia.</li></ul> <p>1 in Queensland for law and legal studies</p><p>QS World University Rankings 2026</p> <p>1 in Australia for environmental sciences</p><p>QS World University Rankings 2026</p> <p> <h5> Majors </h5> </p> <p>Tailor your studies to suit your goals. This program offers these options:</p><ul><li><p>Applied Mathematics</p></li><li><p>Applied Mathematics</p></li><li><p>Archaeological Science</p></li><li><p>Archaeological Science</p></li></ul><p><a href="#majors">See all majors</a></p> <p> <h5> How you''ll learn </h5> </p> <p>Your learning experiences are designed to best suit the learning outcomes of the courses you choose.</p><ul><li>Lectures</li><li>Tutorials</li><li>Overseas study</li><li>Research experience</li><li>Seminars</li></ul> <p> <h5> What you''ll study </h5> </p> <p>At UQ, degrees are called ''programs'' and subjects are called ''courses''.</p><p><a href="https://programs-courses.uq.edu.au/requirements/program/2472/2027">See courses and program structure</a></p><p><a href="https://www.uq.edu.au/study/docs/dual-degree-planners-2027/2027-Bachelors-of-Science-Laws-Honours-2472.pdf">View dual degree planner (PDF)</a></p> <p> <h5> Career possibilities </h5> </p> <p>Our programs prepare you for your first job and beyond. Depending on which major you choose, here are some of the careers you could be on your way to:</p><ul><li>Solicitor</li><li>Barrister</li><li>Community laws officer</li><li>Compliance coordinator</li><li>Legal counsel</li><li>Sustainability adviser</li><li>Research officer</li><li>Environment and resource manager</li><li>Conservation officer</li></ul> <p>Average annual salary range</p><h5>Sustainability Officer</h5>$100–$120K<p>seek.com.au</p><p>Average annual salary range</p><h5>Legal Counsel</h5>$145–$165K<p>seek.com.au</p> <p> <h5> Next steps after graduation </h5> </p> <p>You''ll graduate with an internationally respected honours qualification that satisfies the academic requirements for admission as a legal practitioner in Australia. </p><p>Graduates wishing to practise law must also complete practical legal training and meet the admission requirements set by the relevant legal practitioners admissions board.</p><p>As admission requirements may change, students should refer to the current advice issued by the relevant admissions board.</p><p>A law degree also opens pathways beyond legal practice. Graduates use their legal knowledge, analytical skills and understanding of institutions in a wide range of careers, working in:</p><ul><li>government</li><li>business</li><li>policy and regulation</li><li>consulting</li><li>advocacy</li><li>diplomacy</li><li>community organisations and the not-for-profit sector.</li></ul> <p> <h5> Professional memberships </h5> </p> <p>When you graduate, you may be eligible for memberships with the following professional organisations. Contact the organisation to find out how to become a member.</p><ul><li>Bar Association of Queensland</li><li>Queensland Law Society</li></ul> <p> <h5> Program accreditation </h5> </p> <p>The Bachelors of Science / Laws (Honours) is accredited by:</p><ul><li>Legal Practitioners Admissions Board</li></ul> <p>My program is very flexible, as I can study a variety of subjects and keep things interesting. UQ is great for mixing subjects around and under or over-loading per semester, as there is an option to complete studies in the summer. </p><p> Sarah Ridgeway-Cross </p><p> Current student, Bachelors of Science / Laws (Honours) </p><p>My placement through the Clinical Legal Education subject gave me invaluable experience to shadow a Human Rights Lawyer as she provided legal advice to highly vulnerable homeless individuals. I saw how empathetic lawyers and accessible legal advice can change lives.</p><p> Annabelle (Annie) Khoo </p><p> Graduate, Bachelor of Laws (Honours) </p> <p><a href="/events">See all events</a></p> <a href="/events/uq-open-day"> UQ Open Day </a><p>2 August </p><h5> UQ Open Day </h5><p>St Lucia</p> <p><a href="/stories">See all stories</a></p> <a href="/stories/how-law-degree-can-help-you-drive-positive-social-impact"> How to use law as an instrument of social change </a><p>Careers</p><h5> How to use law as an instrument of social change </h5><p>6-minute read</p><a href="/stories/extracurricular-activities-and-opportunities-law-students"> Extracurricular activities and opportunities for law students </a><p>Uni life</p><h5> Extracurricular activities and opportunities for law students </h5><p>5-minute read</p><a href="/stories/whats-it-really-study-science-uq"> What''s it really like to study science at UQ? </a><p>Uni life</p><h5> What''s it really like to study science at UQ? </h5><p>9-minute read</p>',
    total_course_duration = '5 Years (or part time equivalent)',
    offshore_tuition_fee = 284000,
    onshore_tuition_fee = 66925,
    enrolment_fee = NULL,
    materials_fee = NULL,
    entry_requirements = '<h4>Entry Requirements</h4> <p> <h5> Prerequisites </h5> </p> Queensland Year 12 (or equivalent):<ul><li>General English subject (Units 3 &amp; 4, C)</li><li>Mathematical Methods (Units 3 &amp; 4, C)</li><li>one of Biology, Chemistry, Earth and Environmental Science or Physics (Units 3 &amp; 4, C)</li><li><strong>From Semester 1, 2028</strong>, Earth and Environmental Science will no longer be accepted.</li></ul> <p> <h5> Minimum entry score </h5> </p> <p>Select where you studied and your qualification to see the minimum entry score you need to be considered for this program.</p><p>Use the minimum entry score as a guide. Your score must be at least equivalent to the required Australian Year 12 ATAR score. Entry scores are reviewed each year.</p> <h5>Equivalent subjects</h5> <table><thead><tr><th>Subject</th><th>Qualification equivalent</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table><p> <h5> English language requirements </h5> </p> <p>IELTS overall 7; writing 7; speaking 7; reading 6; listening 6. For other English Language Proficiency Tests and Scores approved for UQ</p><p>TOEFL iBT (including Paper Edition) - Overall 100, listen 19, read 19, write 27, speak 23</p><p>PTE Academic - Overall 72, listen 60, read 60, write 72, speak 72</p><p>BE - A minimum overall grade of 5 plus a minimum grade of A in Writing and Speaking</p><p>CES - Overall 185, listening 169, reading 169, writing 185, speaking 185</p><p>OET is not accepted</p><p>There are other ways to meet the English language requirements. For some programs, additional conditions apply.</p><p><a href="/admissions/english-language-requirements">Learn how to meet the English language requirements</a></p> <p> <h5> Student visas </h5> </p> <p>International students who are accepted into full-time study in the Bachelors of Science / Laws (Honours) are eligible to apply for an Australian student visa (subclass 500).</p><p>There are a number of requirements you must satisfy before a visa is granted, including the Genuine Student (GS) requirement.</p><p><a href="/university-life/getting-prepared-to-come-to-australia/student-visas">Learn more about student visas</a></p> <p> <h5> Need help meeting the entry requirements? </h5> </p> <p>We can help you meet the minimum entry score, subject prerequisites or English language requirements for your preferred program.</p><p><a href="/admissions/undergraduate/consider-your-pathway-options">Learn about pathway options</a></p>',
    apply_form = 'https://study.uq.edu.au/study-options/programs/bachelors-science-laws-honours-2472',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '103167J';

UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Overview</h4> <p> Open up pathways to further research, postgraduate study options and exciting career opportunities with an additional year of honours study. </p><p>Designed for science graduates, the Bachelor of Science (Honours) program offers the chance to undertake an independent research project in your area of interest.</p><p>Working closely with a researcher, you''ll gain practical experience in designing and executing experiments or field studies, and analysing and visualising data in ways specific to your field of study.</p><p>Learn to communicate like a professional scientist as you produce your thesis and deliver oral presentations.</p><p>Graduate equipped with project management experience, allowing you to work independently in research roles across industry and government, or pursue a higher research degree.</p><p><a href="#tab1">Domestic</a><a href="#tab2">International</a></p><p><a href="#entry-requirements">See full entry requirements</a></p><p>LocationHerston, St LuciaDuration 1 Year full-time (or part-time equivalent) Start SemesterSemester 1 (22 Feb, 2027), Semester 2 (26 Jul, 2027)Program Code2031AQFLevel 8</p><p><a href="#fees-scholarships">Scholarships available</a></p><p><a href="#entry-requirements">See full entry requirements</a></p><p>LocationHerston, St LuciaFees<a href="#fees-scholarships">A$56800</a>Duration 1 Year full-time Start Semester Semester 1 (22 Feb, 2027), Semester 2 (26 Jul, 2027) Semester dates for 2028 are yet to be confirmed Program Code2031CRICOS Code082958MAQFLevel 8</p><p><a href="#fees-scholarships">Scholarships available</a></p> <p> <h5> Program highlights </h5> </p> <p> <h5> Program highlights </h5> </p> <ul><li>Tailor your studies to your interests and career goals with a flexible program.</li><li>Work with a researcher to gain hands-on experience in experiments, data analysis and result presentation.</li><li>Gain in-demand skills, including the ability to work independently.</li></ul> <p>1 in Australia for environmental sciences</p><p>QS World University Rankings 2026</p> <p>1 in Australia for agriculture and forestry</p><p>QS World University Rankings 2026</p> <p> <h5> Majors </h5> </p> <p>Tailor your studies to suit your goals. This program offers these options:</p><ul><li><p>Anatomy</p></li><li><p>Archaeological Science</p></li><li><p>Biochemistry and Molecular Biology</p></li><li><p>Bioinformatics</p></li></ul><p><a href="#majors">See all majors</a></p> <p> <h5> How you''ll learn </h5> </p> <p>Your learning experiences are designed to best suit the learning outcomes of the courses you choose.</p><ul><li>Research experience</li><li>Laboratory work</li><li>Fieldwork</li></ul> <p> <h5> What you''ll study </h5> </p> <p>At UQ, degrees are called ''programs'' and subjects are called ''courses''. Here''s a sample of the courses you could study in this program:</p><ul><li>Honours Research Project [Core course] </li><li>Research Methods [Core course] </li></ul><p><a href="https://programs-courses.uq.edu.au/requirements/program/2031/2027">See courses and program structure</a></p> <p> <h5> Career possibilities </h5> </p> <p>Our programs prepare you for your first job and beyond. Depending on which major you choose, here are some of the careers you could be on your way to:</p><ul><li>Biopharmaceutical scientist</li><li>Academic researcher</li><li>Animal research scientist</li><li>Research officer</li><li>Clinical genetics scientist</li><li>Marine research officer</li><li>Environment and sustainability consultant</li><li>Conservation researcher</li><li>Data scientist</li><li>Food technologist</li></ul> <p>Average annual salary range</p><h5>Environmental Officer</h5>$90K–$95K<p>seek.com.au</p><p>Average annual salary range</p><h5>Data Scientist</h5>$115–$135K<p>seek.com.au</p> <p> <h5> Next steps after graduation </h5> </p> <p>When you graduate, you''ll be in high demand by employers for your advanced technical, communication, independent thinking and problem-solving skills.</p><p>Depending on your field of study, you''ll have the pick of a broad range of career possibilities in areas including:</p><ul><li>academia and research</li><li>government</li><li>industry</li><li>finance</li><li>hospitals and health</li><li>marine preservation</li><li>environmental planning and site assessment</li><li>operations research and logistics</li><li>animal welfare and management.</li></ul><p>Alternatively, you can further your research ambitions by applying for postgraduate study.</p><p><a href="http://career-profiles.science.uq.edu.au/">Find out more about careers that started in science</a></p> <p>My experience as an honours student helped me understand what it takes to lead a research project. The subjects throughout my degree were a wonderful mix of theoretical and field-based learning, led by engaging lecturers and tutors who were always happy to have a chat. </p><p> Allie Nance </p><p> Graduate, Bachelor of Science (Honours) (Ecology and Zoology) </p><p>My honours year allowed me to conduct research on major real-world issues that are currently affecting coral reef ecosystems on a global scale. This taught me how to think like a scientist, and create relevant research questions and studies on our most pressing issues. </p><p> Chelsea Waters </p><p> Graduate, Bachelor of Science (Honours) (Marine Biology) </p><p>At UQ I had the opportunity to work on a coral metagenomics research study which allowed me to gain additional fieldwork experience on the Great Barrier Reef whilst learning new laboratory and bioinformatics skills that are essential to the research I do now.</p><p> Margot Bligh </p><p> Graduate, Bachelor of Science (Honours) (Microbiology) </p><p>UQ has a fantastic physics department, the research is excellent, and the co-curricular and extra-curricular activities enhance your learning significantly. Take advantage of the many opportunities to try new, unusual, and exciting things – you’ll be doing yourself a great service. </p><p> Conor O''Neill </p><p> Graduate, Bachelor of Science (Honours) in Physics </p><p>Studying at UQ gave me a strong technical background and plenty of opportunities to be actively involved in cutting-edge research to ensure I was well equipped to rapidly acquire the skills and knowledge needed to become an expert within my field.</p><p> Katelin Haynes </p><p> Graduate, Bachelor of Science (Biochemistry and Molecular Biology) </p> <p><a href="/events">See all events</a></p> <a href="/events/uq-open-day"> UQ Open Day </a><p>2 August </p><h5> UQ Open Day </h5><p>St Lucia</p> <p><a href="/stories">See all stories</a></p> <a href="/stories/whats-it-really-study-science-uq"> What''s it really like to study science at UQ? </a><p>Uni life</p><h5> What''s it really like to study science at UQ? </h5><p>9-minute read</p><a href="/stories/career-opportunities-in-agricultural-science"> Career opportunities in agricultural science </a><p>Careers</p><h5> Career opportunities in agricultural science </h5><p>4-minute read</p><a href="/stories/why-study-environmental-science"> Why study environmental science? </a><p>Careers</p><h5> Why study environmental science? </h5><p>6-minute read</p>',
    total_course_duration = '1 Year full-time (or part-time equivalent)',
    offshore_tuition_fee = 56800,
    onshore_tuition_fee = 10100,
    enrolment_fee = NULL,
    materials_fee = NULL,
    entry_requirements = '<h4>Entry Requirements</h4> <h5>Prerequisites</h5> All fields of study<strong> (excluding Psychology):</strong><br/>Bachelor of Science (or equivalent), with:<ul><li>a grade point average (GPA) of 4.0 on a 7-point scale, and</li><li>a GPA of at least 4.5* for 8 units of courses at level 3 or higher relevant to the honours project, and</li><li>have secured an honours project and supervisor, and</li><li>satisfied any additional requirements set by the head of school.</li></ul>* GPA of at least 5.0 for the Mathematics, Physics, and Statistics fields of study.<br/>Archaeological Science honours commences in Semester 1 (February) only.<br/><br/><a href="https://www.psy.uq.edu.au/future-students/4thyear/">Psychology field of study</a>:<br/>UQ Bachelor of Science with:<ul><li>a grade point average (GPA) of 5.0 for level 2 and 3 courses in the Psychology extended major, and</li><li>satisfied any additional requirements set by the head of school.</li></ul>Students with non-UQ qualifications should refer to the <a href="https://psychology.uq.edu.au/study/honours">School of Psychology honours information</a>.Psychology honours commences in Semester 1 (February) only. <p> <h5> Minimum entry score </h5> </p> <p>Select where you studied and your qualification to see the minimum entry score you need to be considered for this program.</p><p>Use the minimum entry score as a guide. Your score must be at least equivalent to the required Australian Year 12 ATAR score. Entry requirements are subject to change.</p> <h5>Equivalent subjects</h5> <table><thead><tr><th>Subject</th><th>Qualification equivalent</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table><p> <h5> English language requirements </h5> </p> <p>IELTS overall 6.5; reading 6; writing 6; speaking 6; listening 6. For other English Language Proficiency Tests and Scores approved for UQ</p><p>TOEFL iBT (including Paper Edition) - Overall 87, listening 19, reading 19, writing 21 and speaking 19.</p><p>PTE Academic - Overall Score of 64 and 60 in all sub bands.</p><p>BE - A minimum overall grade of 4 plus a minimum grade of C in all macro skills.</p><p>CES - Overall 176 and 169 in all sub bands.</p><p>OET is not accepted.</p><p>There are other ways to meet the English language requirements. For some programs, additional conditions apply.</p><p><a href="/admissions/english-language-requirements">Learn how to meet the English language requirements</a></p> <p> <h5> Student visas </h5> </p> <p>International students who are accepted into full-time study in the Bachelor of Science (Honours) are eligible to apply for an Australian student visa (subclass 500).</p><p>There are a number of requirements you must satisfy before a visa is granted, including the Genuine Student (GS) requirement.</p><p><a href="/university-life/getting-prepared-to-come-to-australia/student-visas">Learn more about student visas</a></p>',
    apply_form = 'https://study.uq.edu.au/study-options/programs/bachelor-science-honours-2031',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '082958M';

