UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Overview</h4> <p> Take a deep dive into your specialty in social sciences and develop your research skills and knowledge, while gaining a valuable additional qualification which will differentiate you in the job market. </p><p>This single year of full-time (or part-time equivalent) advanced-level study allows you to apply your research skills in the humanities and social sciences.</p><p>Your honours program will combine a flexible mix of coursework and independent study, during which you''ll prepare and undertake an approved independent social science research project and submit a formal honours thesis.</p><p>Under the honours program, you''ll be encouraged to extend your specialised study in either Health and Social Policy, Development, or Environment and Society, and the program can be individually supervised across relevant UQ schools or research centres.</p><p>The program will allow you to develop, extend and consolidate your knowledge and skills in social science theory and research in relation to your specialisation area. It''s a valuable additional qualification on entering the job market.</p><p>If you excel through the honours program, you''ll have the opportunity to progress to a Master of Philosophy or further postgraduate study.</p><p><a href="#tab1">Domestic</a><a href="#tab2">International</a></p><p><a href="#entry-requirements">See full entry requirements</a></p><p>LocationSt LuciaDuration 1 Year full-time (or part-time equivalent) Start SemesterSemester 1 (22 Feb, 2027)Program Code2033AQFLevel 8</p><p><a href="#fees-scholarships">Scholarships available</a></p><p><a href="#entry-requirements">See full entry requirements</a></p><p>LocationSt LuciaFees<a href="#fees-scholarships">A$48080</a>Duration 1 Year full-time Start Semester Semester 1 (22 Feb, 2027) Semester dates for 2028 are yet to be confirmed Program Code2033CRICOS Code081757FAQFLevel 8</p><p><a href="#fees-scholarships">Scholarships available</a></p> <p> <h5> Program highlights </h5> </p> <p> <h5> Program highlights </h5> </p> <ul><li>Enjoy individual supervision from UQ''s leading academics as you develop your honours thesis.</li><li>Hone your research skills and knowledge of your chosen field and gain a valuable additional qualification.</li><li>Unlock pathways to further advanced study with a higher postgraduate degree.</li></ul> <p>3 in Australia for social sciences and humanities</p><p>CWTS Leiden Ranking 2025</p> <p>83 in the world for social sciences</p><p>Times Higher Education World University Rankings 2026</p> <p> <h5> Majors </h5> </p> <p>Tailor your studies to suit your goals. This program offers these options:</p><ul><li><p>Development</p></li><li><p>Environment and Society</p></li><li><p>Health and Social Policy</p></li></ul><p><a href="#majors">See all majors</a></p> <p> <h5> How you''ll learn </h5> </p> <p>Your learning experiences are designed to best suit the learning outcomes of the courses you choose.</p><ul><li>Fieldwork</li><li>Seminars</li><li>Workshops</li></ul> <p> <h5> What you''ll study </h5> </p> <p>At UQ, degrees are called ''programs'' and subjects are called ''courses''. Here''s a sample of the courses you could study in this program:</p><ul><li>Research Design in the Social Sciences</li><li>Research Design in Humanities</li><li>Honours Research Thesis</li></ul><p><a href="https://programs-courses.uq.edu.au/requirements/program/2033/2027">See courses and program structure</a></p> <p> <h5> Career possibilities </h5> </p> <p>Our programs prepare you for your first job and beyond. Depending on which major you choose, here are some of the careers you could be on your way to:</p><ul><li>Aid project officer</li><li>Public policy adviser</li><li>Policy and research officer</li><li>Social and government researcher</li><li>Social and welfare services planner</li><li>Community planning and policy adviser</li><li>Community development manager</li><li>Environment and sustainability consultant</li><li>Academic researcher</li></ul> <p>Average annual salary range</p><h5>Policy Adviser</h5>$105–$125K<p>seek.com.au</p> <p> <h5> Next steps after graduation </h5> </p> <p>Graduating from the Bachelor of Social Science (Honours) prepares you for roles across government, policy and community sectors, while also opening pathways to postgraduate research for those seeking to continue their academic journey.</p> <p>The year-long research project was one of the most beneficial parts of my degree, as I gained a lot of industry experience, which I was able to use to promote myself, and draw on my project management, data analysis and writing skills.</p><p> Kanika Shukla </p><p> Graduate, Bachelor of Social Science (Development) </p><p>The social science degree gave me exciting opportunities to put learning into practice through internships with Queensland Ambulance Service and Friends of the Earth, which have been invaluable in applying for jobs and future opportunities. </p><p> Amy MacMahon </p><p> Graduate, Bachelors of Arts / Social Science (Development) (Honours) </p><p>What I liked best about the Honours program at UQ is that it allows for interdisciplinary collaboration amongst students. For me this not only helped me learn different skills, but also reflected what is required from most jobs. </p><p> Bryonie White </p><p> Graduate, Bachelor of Social Science (Criminal Justice) (Honours) </p><p>My studies not only developed my theoretical knowledge, but also provided the environment for me to put this knowledge into practice, engage with industry professionals, participate in skill-building courses, develop my professional networks and learn from lecturers who constantly challenged me to better myself. </p><p> Rhian Stack </p><p> Graduate, Bachelor of Social Science (Criminal Justice) (Honours) </p> <p><a href="/events">See all events</a></p> <a href="/events/ancient-history-experience-day"> Ancient History Experience Day </a><p>15 July </p><h5> Ancient History Experience Day </h5><p>St Lucia</p><a href="/events/world-religions-experience-day-2026"> World Religions Experience Day 2026 </a><p>22 July - 23 July </p><h5> World Religions Experience Day 2026 </h5><p>St Lucia</p><a href="/events/uq-open-day"> UQ Open Day </a><p>2 August </p><h5> UQ Open Day </h5><p>St Lucia</p> <p><a href="/stories">See all stories</a></p> <a href="/stories/turning-her-curiosity-healthcare-career"> Turning her curiosity into a healthcare career </a><p>UQ people</p><h5> Turning her curiosity into a healthcare career </h5><p>4-minute read</p><a href="/stories/how-uq-scholarship-helped-paul-pursue-his-dream"> How a UQ scholarship helped Paul pursue his dream </a><p>UQ people</p><h5> How a UQ scholarship helped Paul pursue his dream </h5><p>5-minute read</p><a href="/stories/phd-story-chiemeka-chinaka"> Chiemeka’s PhD story: cost-effective treatment for brain disorders </a><p>UQ people</p><h5> Chiemeka’s PhD story: cost-effective treatment for brain disorders </h5><p>4-minute read</p>',
    total_course_duration = '1 Year full-time (or part-time equivalent)',
    offshore_tuition_fee = 48080,
    onshore_tuition_fee = 17400,
    enrolment_fee = NULL,
    materials_fee = NULL,
    entry_requirements = '<h4>Entry Requirements</h4> <h5>Prerequisites</h5> <ul><li>Bachelor of Social Science from the University (or equivalent); and</li><li>have gained a grade point average (GPA) of 5.0 on a 7-point scale from an approved combination of courses comprising:</li><li>all Level 2 and Level 3 BSocSc Core Courses and 6 units of Level 2 and Level 3 courses from the chosen BSocSc Major; or</li><li>satisfy the executive dean that the person is qualified to undertake the program based on the person''s academic records and subject to completion of additional work, if set.</li></ul>A person who completed their bachelor''s more than two years prior to program commencement must obtain approval from the executive dean to enrol.<br/><strong>Other Entry Requirements</strong><ul><li>The head of school may limit places depending on supervisor availability.</li><li>Once eligibility is established, entry is via a competitive selection process based on GPA.</li></ul> <p> <h5> Minimum entry score </h5> </p> <p>Select where you studied and your qualification to see the minimum entry score you need to be considered for this program.</p><p>Use the minimum entry score as a guide. Your score must be at least equivalent to the required Australian Year 12 ATAR score. Entry requirements are subject to change.</p> <h5>Equivalent subjects</h5> <table><thead><tr><th>Subject</th><th>Qualification equivalent</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table><p> <h5> English language requirements </h5> </p> <p>IELTS overall 6.5; reading 6; writing 6; speaking 6; listening 6. For other English Language Proficiency Tests and Scores approved for UQ</p><p>TOEFL iBT (including Paper Edition) - Overall 87, listening 19, reading 19, writing 21 and speaking 19.</p><p>PTE Academic - Overall Score of 64 and 60 in all sub bands.</p><p>BE - A minimum overall grade of 4 plus a minimum grade of C in all macro skills.</p><p>CES - Overall 176 and 169 in all sub bands.</p><p>OET is not accepted.</p><p>There are other ways to meet the English language requirements. For some programs, additional conditions apply.</p><p><a href="/admissions/english-language-requirements">Learn how to meet the English language requirements</a></p> <p> <h5> Student visas </h5> </p> <p>International students who are accepted into full-time study in the Bachelor of Social Science (Honours) are eligible to apply for an Australian student visa (subclass 500).</p><p>There are a number of requirements you must satisfy before a visa is granted, including the Genuine Student (GS) requirement.</p><p><a href="/university-life/getting-prepared-to-come-to-australia/student-visas">Learn more about student visas</a></p> <p> <h5> Additional application information </h5> </p> <p> Expressions of Interest are due in November the year prior to commencement. Applicants are encouraged to attend an Honours Information session the year prior to their intended commencement. Please refer to the <a href="&lt;34">https://social-science.uq.edu.au/honours&lt;34&gt;&gt; School of Social Sciences website</a> for further information. </p>',
    apply_form = 'https://study.uq.edu.au/study-options/programs/bachelor-social-science-honours-2033',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '081757F';

UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Overview</h4> <p> Take a lead in shaping a society built on respect, social justice and fairness. </p><p>As a qualified social worker, you''ll put your commitment to the wellbeing of society into action, using your skills to support individuals, families, groups and communities to achieve equitable access to opportunities and resources.</p><p>Through the Bachelor of Social Work, you''ll develop the skills to change the social circumstances of individuals and groups who are socially excluded. You''ll also work with people in distress, helping them to draw on their strengths to make positive changes in their lives and the lives of the people around them.</p><p>Gain hands-on experience with 1,000 hours of supervised placement across diverse settings, including hospitals and various public and private agencies. Plus, you may apply to complete a rural, interstate or international placement.</p><p>UQ lets you forge your own path in social work, undergoing foundation and professional practice in the areas of health and ageing, children, youth and families, and mental health.</p><p>Your focused learning, research and placement opportunities will be combined with core knowledge and skills in social work, social policy and research. Learn from leading researchers addressing crucial issues like family violence prevention, refugee mental health and innovative community development approaches.</p><p>With UQ’s Bachelor of Social Work, you’ll graduate ready to make a meaningful impact and drive positive change in the world.</p><p><a href="#tab1">Domestic</a><a href="#tab2">International</a></p><p><a href="#entry-requirements">See full entry requirements</a></p>LocationSt LuciaDuration 4 Years (or part time equivalent)Start SemesterSemester 1 (22 Feb, 2027), Semester 2 (26 Jul, 2027)QTAC Code<p>734001</p>Program Code2540AQFLevel 7<p><a href="#how-to-apply">Admission schemes available</a></p><p><a href="#fees-scholarships">Scholarships available</a></p><p><a href="#entry-requirements">See full entry requirements</a></p>LocationSt LuciaFees<a href="#fees-scholarships">A$48080</a>Duration 4 Years Start Semester Semester 1 (22 Feb, 2027), Semester 2 (26 Jul, 2027) Semester dates for 2028 are yet to be confirmed QTAC Code<p>734001</p>Program Code2540CRICOS Code001964FAQFLevel 7<p><a href="#fees-scholarships">Scholarships available</a></p> <p> <h5> Program highlights </h5> </p> <p> <h5> Program highlights </h5> </p> <ul><li>Acquire valuable research skills to inform policy and practice decisions. </li><li>Work with families and communities to address social issues and problems through interpersonal, community and policy solutions.</li><li>Build a strong foundation in social work education while developing your knowledge and capabilities, progressively mastering more complex social work tasks as you move through the program.</li><li>Benefit from innovative learning methods that simulate real client encounters and learn appropriate responses to diverse situations.</li></ul> <p>1 in Queensland for social sciences</p><p>Times Higher Education World University Rankings 2026</p> <p>27 in the world for psychology</p><p>QS World University Rankings 2026</p> <p> <h5> How you''ll learn </h5> </p> <p>Your learning experiences are designed to best suit the learning outcomes of the courses you choose.</p><ul><li>Lectures</li><li>Tutorials</li><li>Work placements</li><li>Online study</li><li>Fieldwork</li></ul> <p> <h5> Placements and work experience </h5> </p> <p> Students will undertake approximately 1000 hours of supervised clinical practice in a range of clinical settings that includes hospitals and a variety of public and private agencies. You will have the opportunity during your placements to apply your theoretical knowledge acquired through coursework to practice and develop their clinical skills in real life settings. You may also complete a rural, interstate or international placement in your final year. Clinical placements may be outside of the Brisbane metropolitan area where you will be required to fund your travel, accommodation and daily living expenses. <a href="https://my.uq.edu.au/information-and-services/manage-my-program/placements/hmbs">Learn more about placement requirements</a></p> <p> <h5> What you''ll study </h5> </p> <p>At UQ, degrees are called ''programs'' and subjects are called ''courses''. Here''s a sample of the courses you could study in this program:</p><ul><li>Human Development and Social Work</li><li>Working with Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander People</li><li>Moral and Ethical Foundations of Social Work</li><li>Social Work and the Legal Context</li></ul><p><a href="https://programs-courses.uq.edu.au/requirements/program/2540/2027">See courses and program structure</a></p> <p> <h5> Career possibilities </h5> </p> <p>Our programs prepare you for your first job and beyond. Here are some of the careers you could be on your way to:</p><ul><li>Counsellor</li><li>Child welfare worker</li><li>Family therapist</li><li>Community worker</li><li>Social and welfare services planner</li><li>Disability advocate</li><li>Disability support worker</li><li>Research and education adviser</li><li>Policy analyst</li><li>Aged carer</li></ul> <p>Graduate salary</p><h5>Social work (undergraduate)</h5>$52K–$64K<p>compared.edu.au</p> <p> <h5> Program accreditation </h5> </p> <p>The Bachelor of Social Work is accredited by:</p><ul><li>Australian Association Of Social Workers</li></ul> <p>In my third year, I completed a 500-hour placement at a major hospital, where I applied my skills in diverse settings. From crisis interventions in emergency care to supporting long-term oncology patients, I gained invaluable experience. This placement also led to a role as a social work assistant, further deepening my passion for healthcare social work.</p><p> Savanna Detlefson </p><p> Current student, Bachelor of Social Work </p><p>The educators at UQ are deeply passionate about mentoring the next generation of social workers. They inspire students through humour and authenticity, and I’ve been fortunate to gain once-in-a-lifetime opportunities during my studies, such as a 6-week research internship and a role as a research assistant.</p><p> Fuchsia Mallinson </p><p> Current student, Bachelor of Social Work </p><p>I’ve really enjoyed learning from my lecturers; their diverse perspectives and passion for social work have significantly enriched my education. Each of them brings unique insights that inspire me to grow as a future social worker.</p><p> Caleb Tan </p><p> Current student, Bachelor of Social Work </p><p>I’ve really enjoyed learning from my lecturers; their diverse perspectives and passion for social work have significantly enriched my education. Each of them brings unique insights that inspire me to grow as a future social worker.</p><p> Uttanka Patel </p><p> Current student, Bachelor of Social Work </p><p>Being part of UQ’s social work program has been such a rewarding journey. The lecturers are so inspiring, and I was lucky enough to do my placement in Norway, which was life changing! The community here is very supportive, and I feel fully prepared to go out and make a difference.</p><p> Yule Comerford </p><p> Current student, Bachelor of Social Work </p><p>I would definitely recommend studying social work at UQ as it offers a diverse and stimulating learning program. The social work teaching staff are so friendly, approachable and helpful. </p><p> Melissa Bennett </p><p> Graduate, Bachelor of Social Work (Honours) </p> <p><a href="/events">See all events</a></p> <a href="/events/ancient-history-experience-day"> Ancient History Experience Day </a><p>15 July </p><h5> Ancient History Experience Day </h5><p>St Lucia</p><a href="/events/world-religions-experience-day-2026"> World Religions Experience Day 2026 </a><p>22 July - 23 July </p><h5> World Religions Experience Day 2026 </h5><p>St Lucia</p><a href="/events/uq-open-day"> UQ Open Day </a><p>2 August </p><h5> UQ Open Day </h5><p>St Lucia</p> <p><a href="/stories">See all stories</a></p> <a href="/stories/why-study-social-work-uq"> Why study social work at UQ? </a><p>Study tips</p><h5> Why study social work at UQ? </h5><p>6-minute read</p><a href="/stories/what-does-social-worker-do"> What does a social worker do? </a><p>Careers</p><h5> What does a social worker do? </h5><p>4-minute read</p><a href="/stories/whats-it-really-study-social-work-uq"> What''s it really like to study social work at UQ? </a><p>Uni life</p><h5> What''s it really like to study social work at UQ? </h5><p>7-minute read</p>',
    total_course_duration = '4 Years (or part time equivalent)',
    offshore_tuition_fee = 192320,
    onshore_tuition_fee = 41820,
    enrolment_fee = NULL,
    materials_fee = NULL,
    entry_requirements = '<h4>Entry Requirements</h4> <p> <h5> Prerequisites </h5> </p> Queensland Year 12 (or equivalent): <ul><li>General English subject (Units 3 &amp; 4, C).</li></ul> <h5> Minimum entry score </h5> <p>Select where you studied and your qualification to see the minimum entry score you need to be considered for this program.</p><p>Use the minimum entry score as a guide. Your score must be at least equivalent to the required Australian Year 12 ATAR score. Entry requirements are subject to change.</p> <h5>Equivalent subjects</h5> <table><thead><tr><th>Subject</th><th>Qualification equivalent</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table><p> <h5> English language requirements </h5> </p> <p>IELTS overall 7; reading 7; writing 7; speaking 7; listening 7. For other English Language Proficiency Tests and Scores approved for UQ</p><p>TOEFL iBT (including Paper Edition) - Overall 100, listening 25, reading 25, writing 27, speaking 23.</p><p>PTE Academic - Overall 72, sub bands minimum 72.</p><p>BE - A minimum overall grade of 5 plus a minimum grade of A in all macro skills.</p><p>CES - Overall 185, All sub bands minimum 185.</p><p>OET is not accepted.</p><p>There are other ways to meet the English language requirements. For some programs, additional conditions apply.</p><p><a href="/admissions/english-language-requirements">Learn how to meet the English language requirements</a></p> <p> <h5> Inherent requirements </h5> </p> <p>To complete this degree, you have to meet its inherent requirements by demonstrating essential skills and attributes. Read the inherent requirements before you apply.</p><p><a href="/admissions/inherent-requirements/inherent-requirements-social-work-programs">Learn about inherent requirements</a></p> <p> <h5> Student visas </h5> </p> <p>International students who are accepted into full-time study in the Bachelor of Social Work are eligible to apply for an Australian student visa (subclass 500).</p><p>There are a number of requirements you must satisfy before a visa is granted, including the Genuine Student (GS) requirement.</p><p><a href="/university-life/getting-prepared-to-come-to-australia/student-visas">Learn more about student visas</a></p> <p> <h5> Need help meeting the entry requirements? </h5> </p> <p>We can help you meet the minimum entry score, subject prerequisites or English language requirements for your preferred program.</p><p><a href="/admissions/undergraduate/consider-your-pathway-options">Learn about pathway options</a></p> <p> <h5> Additional application information </h5> </p> <p> Before you apply for this program, you must make sure you will be able to meet any <a href="&lt;34">https://my.uq.edu.au/information-and-services/manage-my-program/placements/hmbs&lt;34&gt;&gt;placement requirements</a>. </p>',
    apply_form = 'https://study.uq.edu.au/study-options/programs/bachelor-social-work-2540',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '001964F';

UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Overview</h4> <p> Take a lead in shaping a society built on respect, social justice and fairness. </p><p>The Bachelor of Social Work (Honours) is designed for current <a href="/study-options/programs/bachelor-social-work-2540?year=2027">Bachelor of Social Work</a> students passionate about research, offering the opportunity to transfer into the program after your third year. Under the guidance of an experienced academic mentor, you''ll conduct independent research in a specific area of social work.</p><p>As a qualified social worker, you''ll use your skills to support individuals, families, groups and communities in achieving equitable access to opportunities and resources while helping those who are socially excluded or in distress draw on their strengths to create positive change in their lives and communities.</p><p>Gain hands-on experience with 1,000 hours of supervised placement across diverse settings, including hospitals and various public and private agencies. Plus, you may apply to complete a rural, interstate or international placement.</p><p>UQ lets you forge your own path in social work, undergoing foundation and professional practice in the areas of health and ageing, children, youth and families, and mental health.</p><p>Your focused learning, research and placement opportunities will be combined with core knowledge and skills in social work, social policy and research. Learn from leading researchers addressing crucial issues like family violence prevention, refugee mental health and innovative community development approaches.</p><p>This program provides a strong foundation for postgraduate study or a PhD while enhancing your career prospects in industry, research, or academia, ensuring you stand out with a competitive edge in your field.</p><p>With UQ’s Bachelor of Social Work (Honours), you’ll graduate ready to make a meaningful impact and drive positive change in the world.</p><p><a href="#tab1">Domestic</a><a href="#tab2">International</a></p><p><a href="#entry-requirements">See full entry requirements</a></p><p>LocationSt LuciaDuration 4 Years (or part time equivalent)Start SemesterSemester 1 (22 Feb, 2027), Semester 2 (26 Jul, 2027)Program Code2382AQFLevel 8</p><p><a href="#fees-scholarships">Scholarships available</a></p><p><a href="#entry-requirements">See full entry requirements</a></p><p>LocationSt LuciaFees<a href="#fees-scholarships">A$48080</a>Duration 4 Years Start Semester Semester 1 (22 Feb, 2027) Semester dates for 2028 are yet to be confirmed Program Code2382CRICOS Code085539FAQFLevel 8</p><p><a href="#fees-scholarships">Scholarships available</a></p> <p> <h5> Program highlights </h5> </p> <p> <h5> Program highlights </h5> </p> <ul><li>Graduate with a highly respected honours qualification, with advanced knowledge and skills that will set you apart in a competitive job market and provide a pathway to future research and learning. </li><li>Undertake your own research project under the guidance of an experienced supervisor.</li><li>Acquire valuable research skills to inform policy and practice decisions.</li></ul> <p>27 in the world for psychology</p><p>QS World University Rankings 2026</p> <p>1 in Queensland for psychology</p><p>Global Ranking of Academic Subjects 2025</p> <p> <h5> How you''ll learn </h5> </p> <p>Your learning experiences are designed to best suit the learning outcomes of the courses you choose.</p><ul><li>Lectures</li><li>Tutorials</li><li>Work placements</li><li>Online study</li><li>Fieldwork</li></ul> <p> <h5> Placements and work experience </h5> </p> <p> Students will undertake approximately 1000 hours of supervised clinical practice in a range of clinical settings that includes hospitals and a variety of public and private agencies. You will have the opportunity during your placements to apply your theoretical knowledge acquired through coursework to practice and develop their clinical skills in real life settings. You may also complete a rural, interstate or international placement in your final year. Clinical placements may be outside of the Brisbane metropolitan area where you will be required to fund your travel, accommodation and daily living expenses. <a href="https://my.uq.edu.au/information-and-services/manage-my-program/placements/hmbs">Learn more about placement requirements</a></p> <p> <h5> What you''ll study </h5> </p> <p>At UQ, degrees are called ''programs'' and subjects are called ''courses''. Here''s a sample of the courses you could study in this program:</p><ul><li>Human Development and Social Work</li><li>Working with Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander People</li><li>Moral and Ethical Foundations of Social Work</li><li>Social Work and the Legal Context</li></ul><p><a href="https://programs-courses.uq.edu.au/requirements/program/2382/2027">See courses and program structure</a></p> <p> <h5> Career possibilities </h5> </p> <p>Our programs prepare you for your first job and beyond. Here are some of the careers you could be on your way to:</p><ul><li>Counsellor</li><li>Child welfare worker</li><li>Family therapist</li><li>Community worker</li><li>Social and welfare services planner</li><li>Disability advocate</li><li>Disability support worker</li><li>Policy analyst</li></ul> <p>Average annual salary range</p><h5>Social Worker</h5>$85K–$105K<p>seek.com.au</p> <p> <h5> Program accreditation </h5> </p> <p>The Bachelor of Social Work (Honours) is accredited by:</p><ul><li>Australian Association Of Social Workers</li></ul> <p>Being part of UQ’s social work program has been such a rewarding journey. The lecturers are so inspiring, and I was lucky enough to do my placement in Norway, which was life changing! The community here is very supportive, and I feel fully prepared to go out and make a difference.</p><p> Yule Comerford </p><p> Current student, Bachelor of Social Work </p><p>I’ve really enjoyed learning from my lecturers; their diverse perspectives and passion for social work have significantly enriched my education. Each of them brings unique insights that inspire me to grow as a future social worker.</p><p> Uttanka Patel </p><p> Current student, Bachelor of Social Work </p><p>I’ve really enjoyed learning from my lecturers; their diverse perspectives and passion for social work have significantly enriched my education. Each of them brings unique insights that inspire me to grow as a future social worker.</p><p> Caleb Tan </p><p> Current student, Bachelor of Social Work </p><p>The educators at UQ are deeply passionate about mentoring the next generation of social workers. They inspire students through humour and authenticity, and I’ve been fortunate to gain once-in-a-lifetime opportunities during my studies, such as a 6-week research internship and a role as a research assistant.</p><p> Fuchsia Mallinson </p><p> Current student, Bachelor of Social Work </p><p>In my third year, I completed a 500-hour placement at a major hospital, where I applied my skills in diverse settings. From crisis interventions in emergency care to supporting long-term oncology patients, I gained invaluable experience. This placement also led to a role as a social work assistant, further deepening my passion for healthcare social work.</p><p> Savanna Detlefson </p><p> Current student, Bachelor of Social Work </p><p>I would definitely recommend studying social work at UQ as it offers a diverse and stimulating learning program. The social work teaching staff are so friendly, approachable and helpful. </p><p> Melissa Bennett </p><p> Graduate, Bachelor of Social Work (Honours) </p> <p><a href="/events">See all events</a></p> <a href="/events/ancient-history-experience-day"> Ancient History Experience Day </a><p>15 July </p><h5> Ancient History Experience Day </h5><p>St Lucia</p><a href="/events/world-religions-experience-day-2026"> World Religions Experience Day 2026 </a><p>22 July - 23 July </p><h5> World Religions Experience Day 2026 </h5><p>St Lucia</p><a href="/events/uq-open-day"> UQ Open Day </a><p>2 August </p><h5> UQ Open Day </h5><p>St Lucia</p> <p><a href="/stories">See all stories</a></p> <a href="/stories/what-does-social-worker-do"> What does a social worker do? </a><p>Careers</p><h5> What does a social worker do? </h5><p>4-minute read</p><a href="/stories/whats-it-really-study-social-work-uq"> What''s it really like to study social work at UQ? </a><p>Uni life</p><h5> What''s it really like to study social work at UQ? </h5><p>7-minute read</p><a href="/stories/how-are-our-social-and-physical-worlds-shaping-us"> How are our social and physical worlds shaping us? </a><p>UQ people</p><h5> How are our social and physical worlds shaping us? </h5><p>3-minute read</p>',
